L06F1:	db	'"Ah, yes. I once had a scroll that told of a talisman by tha'
	db	't name. If only I could remember where I put it. Dost thou b'
	db	'y chance have the parchment entitled Scroll of Infinity with'
	db	' thee?'
L07AB:	db	00
L07AC:	db	'"If thou dost not have the scroll, I cannot help thee in thi'
	db	's matter."'
L07F2:	db	00
L07F3:	db	'"Here we are. Now then, it appears to be written in a strang'
	db	'e format. One might even say a code of sorts... I have it! A'
	db	'pparently, the Talisman currently resides in the Great Void.'
	db	' A plane somewhat removed from ours. If thou wishest to gain'
	db	' access to this void, thou shalt need to craft two lenses: o'
	db	'ne concave, the other convex. Light focused through the prop'
	db	'erly enchanted lenses will open a conduit between our realm '
	db	'and the void. I believe this treatise speaks of three Talism'
	db	'ans of Principle that send out a call to the Infinity Talism'
	db	'an and bring it here. Once here, it would seem that its sole'
	db	' purpose is to coerce a powerful force into the void." A tho'
	db	'ught hits the mage like lightning strikes a tree. "Oh no, Av'
	db	'atar... Thou shan't gain any more aid from me. I may be blin'
	db	'd, but I see through thy sham. I'll not help thee send the C'
	db	'ore into the void." Erethian falls silent, and it would appe'
	db	'ar that he'll speak no more.'
