	db	'l flowed. 'Tis sad to lose such an artifact." As if suddenly'
	db	' remembering with whom he is speaking, he ammends, "Much bet'
	db	'ter than having Mondain running about mucking with things, I'
	db	' suppose."'
L3322:	db	00
L3323:	db	'Gem of Immortality'
L3335:	db	00
L3336:	db	'skull'
L333B:	db	00
L333C:	db	'"'Twould seem that someone," he pauses dramatically, "let th'
	db	'at slip into a volcano..." His wry smile belies his careless'
	db	' tone.'
L33BA:	db	00
L33BB:	db	'skull'
L33C0:	db	00
L33C1:	db	'daemon mirror'
L33CE:	db	00
L33CF:	db	'"Ah, so thou hast met that old windbag. Truly, I feel that I'
	db	' would do better to free myself of that burdensome beast, bu'
	db	't he sometimes proves to be useful. If it weren't for his wh'
	db	'ining, perhaps he and I would get along better."'
L34B3:	db	00
L34B4:	db	'free'
L34B8:	db	00
L34B9:	db	'whining'
L34C0:	db	00
L34C1:	db	'daemon mirror'
L34CE:	db	00
L34CF:	db	'whining'
L34D6:	db	00
L34D7:	db	'"'Tis his favorite passtime. He begs, pleads, and threatens '
	db	'me to free him from that stupid mirror. Believe me, if I cou'
	db	'ld I would have done it long ago." Erethian's lined face sho'
	db	'ws his chagrin.'
L359A:	db	00
L359B:	db	'whining'
L35A2:	db	00
L35A3:	db	'free'
L35A7:	db	00
L35A8:	db	'"He wants this special bauble. I once possessed this gem he '
	db	'seeks, and I don't think he'd be very happy once he gets it.'
	db	' I have tried to tell him that 'twould only imprison	him in '
	db	'a more mobile jail, but alas, his head is made of stone."'
L3695:	db	00
L3696:	db	'jail'
L369A:	db	00
L369B:	db	'free'
L369F:	db	00
L36A0:	db	'jail'
L36A4:	db	00
L36A5:	db	'"Quite. Arcadion seeks to have dominion over Britannia and b'
	db	'elieves that the gem will give him the ability to exert his '
	db	'power here. In truth, the Ether Gem works in the reverse, hi'
	db	's power will become accessible to the one who possesses the '
	db	'gem."'
L379A:	db	00
L379B:	db	'Ether Gem'
L37A4:	db	00
L37A5:	db	'jail'
L37A9:	db	00
L37AA:	db	'Ether Gem'
L37B3:	db	00
L37B4:	db	'"The gem was pilfered from me by an ill tempered dragon. She'
	db	' blew her way into this castle, waylayed the golems that pro'
	db	'tect the Shrine of Principle, then destroyed a perfectly goo'
	db	'd secret door on her way to the Test of Courage. I'd have li'
	db	'ked to see her squeeze through the hole she made, 'tis hardl'
	db	'y big enough for a creature of her bulk." The mage's milky e'
	db	'yes twinkle with suppressed mirth.'
L393E:	db	00
L393F:	db	'Test of Courage'
L394E:	db	00
L394F:	db	'Shrine of Principle'
L3962:	db	00
L3963:	db	'golems'
L3969:	db	00
L396A:	db	'Ether Gem'
L3973:	db	00
L3974:	db	'golems'
L397A:	db	00
L397B:	db	'"Mmmm... Yes. This pair of manshaped, magical constucts used'
	db	' to guard the Shrine of Principle, but alas, one fell pray t'
	db	'o falling rocks when the dragon assaulted the castle. The ot'
	db	'her picked up his, ah... brother, for lack of a better word,'
	db	' and carried him off through the portal to the Test of Love.'
	db	'"'
L3AA8:	db	00
L3AA9:	db	'Test of Love'
L3AB5:	db	00
L3AB6:	db	'golems'
L3ABC:	db	00
L3ABD:	db	'Shrine of Principle'
L3AD0:	db	00
L3AD1:	db	'"The shrine lies through the doors at the rear of the main h'
	db	'all. There thou canst find three statues, each one dedicated'
	db	' to a Principle set forth by Lord Britsh at the beginning of'
	db	' the Age of Enlightenment." Conspiratorially he adds, "A bit'
	db	' stuffy, but they make nice cloakracks."'
L3BE9:	db	00
L3BEA:	db	'Shrine of Principle'
L3BFD:	db	00
L3BFE:	db	'Test of Love'
L3C0A:	db	00
L3C0B:	db	'"I not had the chance to inspect that oddity yet, however, t'
	db	'hou art welcome to peruse it at thy leisure." He smiles like'
	db	' a grandfather giving a present to a child.'
L3CAE:	db	00
L3CAF:	db	'Test of Love'
L3CBB:	db	00
L3CBC:	db	'Test of Courage'
L3CCB:	db	00
L3CCC:	db	'heroine's'
L3CD5:	db	00
L3CD6:	db	'hero's'
L3CDC:	db	00
L3CDD:	db	'"I believe 'twas set in motion by Lord British in order to t'
	db	'est..." He gestures in your direction, "A virtuous '
L3D4C:	db	00
L3D4D:	db	' fighting ability and courage. The statues in the back of th'
	db	'is castle can tell thee more about the tests, though." Ereth'
	db	'ian grins mysteriously.'
L3DDC:	db	00
L3DDD:	db	'Test of Courage'
L3DEC:	db	00
L3DED:	db	'daemon gem'
L3DF7:	db	00
L3DF8:	db	'"So... thou hast made a servant of Arcadion. 'Tis good to be'
	db	' rid of his incessant whining. I hope that thou findest him '
	db	'to be as useful as I didst." You're not sure, but his words '
	db	'might be construed as a curse.'
L3ECA:	db	00
L3ECB:	db	'The gem glows brighter, "'Tis good to see the last of thee, '
	db	'also, old man. Perhaps in another life, I shall be thy maste'
	db	'r, and thou the slave." The daemon lets out a chilling littl'
	db	'e laugh.'
L3F87:	db	00
L3F88:	db	'Erethian looks a little shaken at hearing the daemon's voice'
	db	', but quickly recovers his composure. "I think not, daemon. '
	db	'I'm not at all sure that there is a way for thou to get out '
	db	'of that little gem." The elderly mage's expression is unread'
	db	'able.*'
L407E:	db	00
L407F:	db	'daemon gem'
L4089:	db	00
L408A:	db	'daemon blade'
L4096:	db	00
L4097:	db	'"I see that thou didst not heed my warning. Alas, my pity sh'
	db	'all be thine eternally. And so, what wouldst thou have of me'
	db	', Master and Slave of the Shade Blade."'
L4136:	db	00
L4137:	db	'daemon blade'
L4143:	db	00
L4144:	db	'bye'
L4147:	db	00
L4148:	db	'"Goodbye and good luck... Thou'lt need it." The old mage sni'
	db	'ckers under his breath as if enjoying a personal joke, quite'
	db	' possibly at your expense.*'
L41DB:	db	00
L41DC:	db	'"Goodbye and good luck..." Erethian sounds truly sympathetic'
	db	'.'
