		.funcnumber	0269H	;* Time lord.
		.data
L0000:	db	'"Congratulations, Avatar, on destroying the Sphere. I am fre'
	db	'e from my celestial prison. I thank thee. But I regret to in'
	db	'form thee that The Guardian engineered the Sphere such that '
	db	'its destruction has permanently disabled the Moongates, and '
	db	'thine Orb of the Moons as well. Thou canst not return to thi'
	db	'ne home by way of a red Moongate.~~'
L014F:	db	00
L0150:	db	'"Thine only hope of leaving Britannia at the conclusion of t'
	db	'hy quest is to use The Guardian's own vehicle for entering t'
	db	'he land -- The Black Gate.'
L01E2:	db	00
L01E3:	db	'"The Guardian's followers are building The Black Gate of bla'
	db	'ckrock and will be using magic and natural elements to activ'
	db	'ate it. The Guardian plans to enter Britannia during the upc'
	db	'oming Astronomical Alignment, which is imminent. That is the'
	db	' only time when the elements will work well enough for The B'
	db	'lack Gate to be permeable and active. Thou wilt need a devic'
	db	'e which has the ability to vanquish blackrock. If thou hast '
	db	'not already encountered such a device, thou canst find somet'
	db	'hing to help thee in the workshop of Rudyom the Mage, in Cov'
	db	'e.'
L0401:	db	00
L0402:	db	'"Before thou canst locate The Black Gate, there is one more '
	db	'generator which must be destroyed. It is the device used to '
	db	'transmit The Guardian's voice to his followers and charm the'
	db	'm into obeying his wishes. Look in the area near Serpent's H'
	db	'old for a dungeon containing this generator. It is most like'
	db	'ly shaped like a Cube. It could very well be on The Fellowsh'
	db	'ip's island east of Serpent's Hold.'
L058D:	db	00
L058E:	db	'"When thou hast completed this task, concentrate thine effor'
	db	'ts in Buccaneer's Den. Thou mayest find clues there as to th'
	db	'e location of The Black Gate.'
L0623:	db	00
L0624:	db	'"Shouldst thou wish to speak with me again, simply use the h'
	db	'ourglass. Goodbye."*'
L0674:	db	00
L0675:	db	'"Avatar! The Astronomical Alignment is almost at hand! Time '
	db	'is running out! The Guardian must be prevented from coming t'
	db	'hrough The Black Gate!'
L0703:	db	00
L0704:	db	'"The Cube will help thee find the location of The Black Gate'
	db	'. With it in thy possession, those under the influence of Th'
	db	'e Guardian will be more receptive to speaking the truth to t'
	db	'hee.'
L07BC:	db	00
L07BD:	db	'"Go to Buccaneer's Den. Search for the one called 'Hook'. Ta'
	db	'lk to the so-called Fellowship. Thou shouldst have no troubl'
	db	'e ascertaining his whereabouts there. I am sure that thou wi'
	db	'lt eventually find the location of The Black Gate! Good luck'
	db	'!"*'
L08B0:	db	00
L08B1:	db	'bye'
L08B4:	db	00
L08B5:	db	'job'
L08B8:	db	00
L08B9:	db	'name'
L08BD:	db	00
L08BE:	db	'You see a vaguely familiar but intimidating figure enclosed '
	db	'in some kind of cylindrical cell. He looks at you intently.~'
	db	'~"It has been many years since we met during the time of Exo'
	db	'dus! I have never wanted to see thee again as badly as most '
	db	'recently! It is about time thou shouldst arrive! I do not ha'
	db	've eras to waste whilst I wait for thee! There is a crisis a'
	db	'nd Britannia needs thine help! I need thine help! The entire'
	db	' universe needs thine help!"'
L0A7E:	db	00
L0A7F:	db	'crisis'
L0A85:	db	00
L0A86:	db	'about time'
L0A90:	db	00
L0A91:	db	'"Hast thou decided if thou wilt help me?"'
L0ABA:	db	00
L0ABB:	db	'The Time Lord looks relieved.'
L0AD8:	db	00
L0AD9:	db	'"Then I have a mission for thee."'
L0AFA:	db	00
L0AFB:	db	'mission'
L0B02:	db	00
L0B03:	db	'"Then away with thee!"*'
L0B1A:	db	00
L0B1B:	db	'"How may I help thee, Avatar?" the Time Lord asks.'
L0B4D:	db	00
L0B4E:	db	'The Guardian'
L0B5A:	db	00
L0B5B:	db	'ethereal defense'
L0B6B:	db	00
L0B6C:	db	'Tetrahedron'
L0B77:	db	00
L0B78:	db	'ethereal defense'
L0B88:	db	00
L0B89:	db	'Tetrahedron'
L0B94:	db	00
L0B95:	db	'Moongate'
L0B9D:	db	00
L0B9E:	db	'Sphere'
L0BA4:	db	00
L0BA5:	db	'Moongate'
L0BAD:	db	00
L0BAE:	db	'Sphere'
L0BB4:	db	00
L0BB5:	db	'Cube'
L0BB9:	db	00
L0BBA:	db	'noise'
L0BBF:	db	00
L0BC0:	db	'Cube'
L0BC4:	db	00
L0BC5:	db	'noise'
L0BCA:	db	00
L0BCB:	db	'Cube'
L0BCF:	db	00
L0BD0:	db	'fix magic'
L0BD9:	db	00
L0BDA:	db	'fix magic'
L0BE3:	db	00
L0BE4:	db	'name'
L0BE8:	db	00
L0BE9:	db	'"I am known as the Time Lord."'
L0C07:	db	00
L0C08:	db	'name'
L0C0C:	db	00
L0C0D:	db	'job'
L0C10:	db	00
L0C11:	db	'"I ensure that time flows smoothly through space." He shrugs'
	db	' his shoulders. "Do not ask me to explain this. It is beyond'
	db	' mortal beings' comprehension."'
L0CA8:	db	00
L0CA9:	db	'about time'
L0CB3:	db	00
L0CB4:	db	'"It was I who sent the red moongate to thine homeland to lur'
	db	'e thee to Britannia! It took every bit of my strength to mak'
	db	'e it functional, and still something went wrong. Thou didst '
	db	'arrive in Trinsic, which was not mine intention. It has ther'
	db	'efore taken thee much longer to reach me than I anticipated.'
L0DE0:	db	00
L0DE1:	db	'"Once thou didst arrive in Britannia, the only other way I c'
	db	'ould contact thee was via the Wisps. After the considerable '
	db	'rest I had since creating the red moongate, I managed to rep'
	db	'air the one Orb of the Moons location that would bring thee '
	db	'to me. I cannot roam freely through time and space, doing my'
	db	' work, whilst I am trapped here."'
L0F2E:	db	00
L0F2F:	db	'about time'
L0F39:	db	00
L0F3A:	db	'Wisps'
L0F3F:	db	00
L0F40:	db	'crisis'
L0F46:	db	00
L0F47:	db	'"The land is under attack by a powerful and malicious being '
	db	'from another dimension, and thou art the only one who can st'
	db	'op him! I have been trapped here by a trick, due to a sorcer'
	db	'y which The Guardian has performed. The Guardian has put a w'
	db	'rinkle in the space-time continuum by creating a powerful 'g'
	db	'enerator' which has made the Moongates and thine Orb of the '
	db	'Moons mostly inoperable.'
L10C7:	db	00
L10C8:	db	'"Thou -must- free me and we must work together in battling T'
	db	'he Guardian. The fate of thy people depends upon it. Dost th'
	db	'ou accept?"'
L114B:	db	00
L114C:	db	'"Then I have a mission for thee."'
L116D:	db	00
L116E:	db	'mission'
L1175:	db	00
L1176:	db	'"Then thou shalt be doomed to never finish thy quest. Art th'
	db	'ou sure? I give thee one more chance. Dost thou want to help'
	db	'?"'
L11F0:	db	00
L11F1:	db	'"Then I have a mission for thee."'
L1212:	db	00
L1213:	db	'"Then farewell, Avatar. Leave now. Thou wilt come back when '
	db	'thou dost realize it is thy destiny to help me."*'
L1280:	db	00
L1281:	db	'crisis'
L1287:	db	00
L1288:	db	'mission'
L128F:	db	00
L1290:	db	'"I knew thou wouldst not let me down.~~"Go at once to the Se'
	db	'rpent's Spine area. Search for the entrance to a dungeon som'
	db	'ewhere northwest of Britain. I believe it may be called 'Dun'
	db	'geon Despise'. This will lead thee to the generator causing '
	db	'the problem. If mine hunch is correct, it will resemble a la'
	db	'rge Sphere.'
L13C7:	db	00
L13C8:	db	'"Thou may have already seen it.'
L13E7:	db	00
L13E8:	db	'"Thou must find a way to destroy it.'
L140C:	db	00
L140D:	db	'"It may have a defense mechanism. If thou canst not conquer '
	db	'it, return here and describe the defense to me. Perhaps I ca'
	db	'n help thee more. It might be wise to use the spells Mark an'
	db	'd Recall to save thyself the trouble of finding thy way thro'
	db	'ugh the entire dungeon a second time, should thou have to tr'
	db	'avel there again."'
L154B:	db	00
L154C:	db	'Sphere'
L1552:	db	00
L1553:	db	'"Its defense, as thou dost know, is an unusual Moongate."'
L158C:	db	00
L158D:	db	'Moongate'
L1595:	db	00
L1596:	db	'Sphere'
L159C:	db	00
L159D:	db	'mission'
L15A4:	db	00
L15A5:	db	'Wisps'
L15AA:	db	00
L15AB:	db	'"Oddly aloof creatures. They have made good messengers in th'
	db	'e past."'
L15EF:	db	00
L15F0:	db	'Wisps'
L15F5:	db	00
L15F6:	db	'The Guardian'
L1602:	db	00
L1603:	db	'"He is an embodiment of supreme evil. He must be stopped. He'
	db	' thrives on domination and control."'
L1663:	db	00
L1664:	db	'The Guardian'
L1670:	db	00
L1671:	db	'Sphere'
L1677:	db	00
L1678:	db	'"It is a magic generator that The Guardian was able to send '
	db	'from his world. Its purpose is to disable the Moongates. Tho'
	db	'u must break its outer defense and enter the structure, taki'
	db	'ng the smaller Sphere floating inside. Keep the small Sphere'
	db	', as it will be useful later."'
L1786:	db	00
L1787:	db	'Sphere'
L178D:	db	00
L178E:	db	'Moongate'
L1796:	db	00
L1797:	db	'"The Sphere's outer defense sends thy party back to a specif'
	db	'ic position in space. Until this defense is broken, thou can'
	db	'st not enter the generator. Thou must find Nicodemus' hourgl'
	db	'ass.~~"If I am correct in mine hypothesis, the Sphere's inne'
	db	'r defense will involve Moongates. Look for a visual pattern '
	db	'to help thee solve this mystery."'
L18E4:	db	00
L18E5:	db	'Moongate'
L18ED:	db	00
L18EE:	db	'Nicodemus'
L18F7:	db	00
L18F8:	db	'hourglass'
L1901:	db	00
L1902:	db	'hourglass'
L190B:	db	00
L190C:	db	'"It is an enchanted hourglass which will help thee if it is '
	db	'used at the site of the Sphere. Once I am free of the power '
	db	'of the generator, thou canst summon me by using the hourglas'
	db	's."'
L19C3:	db	00
L19C4:	db	'hourglass'
L19CD:	db	00
L19CE:	db	'"It is of no use to thee now, unless thou dost want to summo'
	db	'n me again."'
L1A16:	db	00
L1A17:	db	'hourglass'
L1A20:	db	00
L1A21:	db	'Nicodemus'
L1A2A:	db	00
L1A2B:	db	'"He is a mage that lives west of the forest of Yew."'
L1A5F:	db	00
L1A60:	db	'Nicodemus'
L1A69:	db	00
L1A6A:	db	'fix magic'
L1A73:	db	00
L1A74:	db	'The Time Lord thinks a moment.~~"The ether must be repaired '
	db	'before the mages in Britannia can use magic again. I suggest'
	db	' that thou seest Penumbra in Moonglow. She may be able to he'
	db	'lp thee with this problem."'
L1B43:	db	00
L1B44:	db	'Penumbra'
L1B4C:	db	00
L1B4D:	db	'"Magic must be functioning properly now, Avatar. Use it wise'
	db	'ly."'
L1B8D:	db	00
L1B8E:	db	'fix magic'
L1B97:	db	00
L1B98:	db	'Tetrahedron'
L1BA3:	db	00
L1BA4:	db	'"It is a magic generator that The Guardian has sent from his'
	db	' world. It is controlling the ether which is depended upon b'
	db	'y the mages to perform magic. Like the Sphere, thou must pen'
	db	'etrate its outer defense, enter the structure, and take the '
	db	'smaller Tetrahedron floating inside."'
L1CB9:	db	00
L1CBA:	db	'Tetrahedron'
L1CC5:	db	00
L1CC6:	db	'ethereal defense'
L1CD6:	db	00
L1CD7:	db	'"It is not surprising that the Tetrahedron has such a defens'
	db	'e. Penumbra in Moonglow should be able to help thee with tha'
	db	't. It is obvious now that the Tetrahedron must be destroyed '
	db	'before thou canst destroy the Sphere.~~"I am not sure what k'
	db	'ind of inner defense the Tetrahedron may hold. It may be dan'
	db	'gerous. Be sure to be well-armed when entering it."'
L1E36:	db	00
L1E37:	db	'ethereal defense'
L1E47:	db	00
L1E48:	db	'Penumbra'
L1E50:	db	00
L1E51:	db	'"She is an elderly mage who lives in Moonglow."'
L1E80:	db	00
L1E81:	db	'Penumbra'
L1E89:	db	00
L1E8A:	db	'Cube'
L1E8E:	db	00
L1E8F:	db	'"It is a magic generator which The Guardian has sent from hi'
	db	's world. From what thou dost say, it sounds to me like the d'
	db	'evice he uses to 'speak' to his followers and charm them int'
	db	'o submitting to his wishes. I am afraid that before thou can'
	db	'st destroy it, thou must take care of the other magic genera'
	db	'tors which The Guardian has placed in Britannia."'
L1FEC:	db	00
L1FED:	db	'"It is the third and final magic generator which The Guardia'
	db	'n has sent from his world. It is the device he uses to 'spea'
	db	'k' to his followers and charm them into submitting to his wi'
	db	'shes. Tis in a dungeon near Serpents Hold. Thou must destroy'
	db	' its outer defense, enter it, and take the smaller Cube floa'
	db	'ting inside."'
L2126:	db	00
L2127:	db	'Cube'
L212B:	db	00
L212C:	db	'Cube defense'
L2138:	db	00
L2139:	db	'noise'
L213E:	db	00
L213F:	db	'Cube defense'
L214B:	db	00
L214C:	db	'"This outer defense can be conquered by using special helmet'
	db	's which cover your ears. The helmets must be made from a rar'
	db	'e mineral called 'Caddellite'. It is present in meteors. See'
	db	'k out Brion, at the Observatory near the Lycaeum. He can giv'
	db	'e thee more advice on finding this mineral.~~"The inner defe'
	db	'nse will most likely involve The Guardian himself. Do not li'
	db	'sten to what he might tell thee."'
L22D5:	db	00
L22D6:	db	'noise'
L22DB:	db	00
L22DC:	db	'Cube defense'
L22E8:	db	00
L22E9:	db	'bye'
L22EC:	db	00
L22ED:	db	'"Farewell, Avatar. Good luck to thee."*'
