		.funcnumber	03F7H	;* Golem
		.data
L0000:	db	'"Hast thou in thy possesion the book on the Stone of Castamb'
	db	're?"'
L0040:	db	00
L0041:	db	'His eyes reveal his hope. As he takes the book from you, it '
	db	'almost appears as if he is smiling."'
L00A1:	db	00
L00A2:	db	'"That is, indeed, a pity," he says, shaking his head in sadn'
	db	'ess.'
L00E2:	db	00
L00E3:	db	'"Greetings to thee, honorable one. I can but assume that my '
	db	'presence here was thy doing." It becomes quickly apparent th'
	db	'at this creature possesses a greater	capability for speech t'
	db	'han his fallen companion.'
L01B0:	db	00
L01B1:	db	'The recently raised golem stares down at the prone, lifeless'
	db	' body of Bollux. Quickly he looks up at you.~"Wh-what has ha'
	db	'ppened?"'
L0231:	db	00
L0232:	db	'"Now thou must excuse me, for I am off to find my fellow sen'
	db	'try."*'
L0274:	db	00
L0275:	db	'"Hail, friend. I hope that I may assist thee in some way."'
L02AF:	db	00
L02B0:	db	'"Art thou here to aid me in healing my brother?"'
L02E0:	db	00
L02E1:	db	'"Very good. I am pleased to call thee friend."'
L030F:	db	00
L0310:	db	'"Then begone, for I have work to do!"*'
L0336:	db	00
