L0087:	db	00
L0088:	db	'Spark'
L008D:	db	00
L008E:	db	'You see the familiar face of your good friend, Dupre. While '
	db	'somewhat older, he still seems full of his usual casual good'
	db	' humor.'
L010D:	db	00
L010E:	db	'"How may I assist thee, '
L0126:	db	00
L0127:	db	'?" asks Sir Dupre.'
L0139:	db	00
L013A:	db	'name'
L013E:	db	00
L013F:	db	'"Why, dost thou not recognize me? It is I, Lord British!" he'
	db	' laughs. "Dost thou not know thy friend Dupre when thou sees'
	db	't him, '
L01BE:	db	00
L01BF:	db	'?"'
L01C1:	db	00
L01C2:	db	'"Do not be so modest, Sir Dupre. Thou shouldst tell the Avat'
	db	'ar that thou hast been knighted since last you met."*'
L0233:	db	00
L0234:	db	'Sir Dupre looks quite embarrassed. "Well, yes, I would have '
	db	'gotten around to that."'
L0287:	db	00
L0288:	db	'"Do not be so modest, Sir Dupre. Thou shouldst tell the Avat'
	db	'ar that thou hast been knighted since last you met."*'
L02F9:	db	00
