		.data
L0000:	db	'bye'
L0003:	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
L0007:	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
L000C:	db	00
L000D:	db	'audition'
L0015:	db	00
L0016:	db	'Max'
L0019:	db	00
L001A:	db	'Miranda'
L0021:	db	00
L0022:	db	'You can see the creativity literally flowing in abundance fr'
	db	'om this fellow. He looks at you with interest.'
L008C:	db	00
L008D:	db	'"Yes, yes?" Raymundo snaps. "What dost thou want? I'm busy!"'
L00C9:	db	00
L00CA:	db	'name'
L00CE:	db	00
L00CF:	db	'"I am Raymundo."'
L00DF:	db	00
L00E0:	db	'name'
L00E4:	db	00
L00E5:	db	'job'
L00E8:	db	00
L00E9:	db	'"Why, I am famous throughout the land! Hast thou not heard o'
	db	'f me?"'
L012B:	db	00
L012C:	db	'"I told thee so!'
L013C:	db	00
L013D:	db	'"-Really-!? I am surprised! But never mind...'
L016A:	db	00
L016B:	db	'"I am the Director of the Royal Theatre here in Britain. I a'
	db	'm also Playwright-in-Residence. I compose a tune now and the'
	db	'n as well. I sometimes act, but it is not wise to act in som'
	db	'ething that one directs.~'
L0238:	db	00
L0239:	db	'"We are working on a play at the moment."'
L0262:	db	00
L0263:	db	'"Come by the theatre during the day and watch the rehearsals'
	db	' for our play."'
L02AE:	db	00
L02AF:	db	'play'
L02B3:	db	00
L02B4:	db	'Royal Theatre'
L02C1:	db	00
L02C2:	db	'play'
L02C6:	db	00
L02C7:	db	'"It's a little something I wrote entitled 'The Trials of the'
	db	' Avatar'. It's about a legendary figure in Britannian histor'
	db	'y." The artist looks you up and down.'
L0364:	db	00
L0365:	db	'"Hmmm. Thou dost have a certain quality... hast thou ever ac'
	db	'ted on stage?"'
L03AF:	db	00
L03B0:	db	'"I thought so!'
L03BE:	db	00
L03BF:	db	'"Well, it does not matter. I am sure thou couldst quickly ad'
	db	'apt.'
L03FF:	db	00
L0400:	db	'"Officially, auditions have closed and the play is already c'
	db	'ast. However, we need someone to understudy the role of the '
	db	'Avatar. Wouldst thou like to audition?"'
L049F:	db	00
L04A0:	db	'"Excellent! What thou needest to do is to visit Gaye's Cloth'
	db	'ier Shoppe and purchase an Avatar costume. I can audition th'
	db	'ee once I see thee in -proper- attire. Run along and do that'
	db	', quickly now, I'm a busy man."*'
L0574:	db	00
L0575:	db	'"No? Thou hast never dreamed of performing on the stage? See'
	db	'ing thy name in torches? Donning the olde grease paint and w'
	db	'ig? Bowing to thunderous applause? Well, begone then, I have'
	db	' not the time for chatting with the public."*'
L0656:	db	00
L0657:	db	'Royal Theatre'
L0664:	db	00
L0665:	db	'"'Tis a wonderful space, dost thou not think? 'Twas opened o'
	db	'nly last year, thanks to the sponsorship of a few wealthy ci'
	db	'tizens of our great city."'
L06F7:	db	00
L06F8:	db	'Royal Theatre'
L0705:	db	00
L0706:	db	'citizens'
L070E:	db	00
L070F:	db	'sponsorship'
L071A:	db	00
L071B:	db	'sponsorship'
L0726:	db	00
L0727:	db	'"The construction of the actual theatre building was paid fo'
	db	'r by the Royal Mint, but the theatre company relies solely o'
	db	'n the support of individuals such as thyself. Wouldst thou l'
	db	'ike to make a modest contribution of, say, ten gold pieces t'
	db	'o our theatre company?"'
L082E:	db	00
L082F:	db	'"I thank thee. Thou hast shown thyself to be a true patron o'
	db	'f the arts and a person of culture and refinement."'
L089E:	db	00
L089F:	db	'"Thine unconvincing performance gave thy game away! Thou dos'
	db	't not have ten gold pieces!"'
L08F7:	db	00
L08F8:	db	'"Give a man a loaf of bread and thou hast fed him for a day,'
	db	' give a man a play and perhaps thou hast fed his soul for a '
	db	'lifetime! Once thou hast seen one of our productions I am ce'
	db	'rtain thou shalt reconsider."'
L09C9:	db	00
L09CA:	db	'sponsorship'
L09D5:	db	00
L09D6:	db	'audition'
L09DE:	db	00
L09DF:	db	'"I see thou art ready? Very well. Take center stage, wouldst'
	db	' thou?"'
L0A22:	db	00
L0A23:	db	'"Where is thy costume? Thou cannot audition without a costum'
	db	'e!"*'
L0A63:	db	00
L0A64:	db	'"Come to the theatre during rehearsal hours, wouldst thou?"*'
L0AA0:	db	00
L0AA1:	db	'Miranda'
L0AA8:	db	00
L0AA9:	db	'Raymundo takes a deep breath and smiles.'
L0AD1:	db	00
L0AD2:	db	'"Ah, lovely woman. 'Tis a pity she is more interested in pol'
	db	'itics than the stage. But I must say that we get along famou'
	db	'sly!"'
L0B4F:	db	00
L0B50:	db	'Miranda'
L0B57:	db	00
L0B58:	db	'Max'
L0B5B:	db	00
L0B5C:	db	'"He is quite a character, is he not?" Raymundo's face fills '
	db	'with pride.'
L0BA3:	db	00
L0BA4:	db	'"Takes after his old man, I must say. He is sure to be a gre'
	db	'at actor. Or writer. Or director. Or producer."'
L0C0F:	db	00
L0C10:	db	'Max'
L0C13:	db	00
L0C14:	db	'citizens'
L0C1C:	db	00
L0C1D:	db	'"Well, I am really not at liberty to divulge the names of ou'
	db	'r patrons. But most of them belong to The Fellowship."'
L0C8F:	db	00
L0C90:	db	'citizens'
L0C98:	db	00
L0C99:	db	'Fellowship'
L0CA3:	db	00
L0CA4:	db	'patrons'
L0CAB:	db	00
L0CAC:	db	'patrons'
L0CB3:	db	00
L0CB4:	db	'"These are people who contribute to our theatre. They come f'
	db	'rom all walks of life and have little in common besides a lo'
	db	've of fine theatre."'
L0D40:	db	00
L0D41:	db	'patrons'
L0D48:	db	00
L0D49:	db	'Fellowship'
L0D53:	db	00
L0D54:	db	'"For non-artists, they have given generous contributions to '
	db	'the theatre. They are -fine- people in my book!" He rubs his'
	db	' hands with glee.'
L0DDD:	db	00
L0DDE:	db	'"I am not a member, though."'
L0DFA:	db	00
L0DFB:	db	'Fellowship'
L0E05:	db	00
L0E06:	db	'bye'
L0E09:	db	00
L0E0A:	db	'"Leaving? Sorry, I do not give autographs."*'
L0E36:	db	00
L0E37:	db	'@Louder! I can't hear thee!@'
L0E53:	db	00
L0E54:	db	'@Move stage right, please.@'
L0E6F:	db	00
L0E70:	db	'@Try that scene again.@'
L0E87:	db	00
L0E88:	db	'@From the top, please.@'
L0E9F:	db	00
