		.funcnumber	0423H
		.data
L0000:	db	'bye'
L0003:	db	00
L0004:	db	'services'
L000C:	db	00
L000D:	db	'job'
L0010:	db	00
L0011:	db	'name'
L0015:	db	00
L0016:	db	'You see a healer who looks wise and honest.'
L0041:	db	00
L0042:	db	'"I have been looking forward to thine arrival, Avatar. Word '
	db	'spreads quickly. I am pleased to meet thee!"'
L00AA:	db	00
L00AB:	db	'"Hello again, Avatar!" Csil says with a smile.'
L00D9:	db	00
L00DA:	db	'name'
L00DE:	db	00
L00DF:	db	'"I am Csil the Healer, although in a past life I was known a'
	db	's Abrams. I became Csil when I was advanced."'
L0148:	db	00
L0149:	db	'name'
L014D:	db	00
L014E:	db	'advanced'
L0156:	db	00
L0157:	db	'job'
L015A:	db	00
L015B:	db	'"I am Britain's healer, and have been for many years. If tho'
	db	'u wishest to employ my services, please say so. I shall be o'
	db	'nly too happy to help."'
L01EA:	db	00
L01EB:	db	'advanced'
L01F3:	db	00
L01F4:	db	'"When my name was Abrams, I lived on the island of New Magin'
	db	'cia and did mine apprentice work there. My practice grew, an'
	db	'd soon I was travelling by ship to Moonglow to see patients '
	db	'there."'
L02AF:	db	00
L02B0:	db	'advanced'
L02B8:	db	00
L02B9:	db	'practice'
L02C1:	db	00
L02C2:	db	'patients'
L02CA:	db	00
L02CB:	db	'patients'
L02D3:	db	00
L02D4:	db	'"Soon I had patients on three islands. It was then that Lord'
	db	' British received word of my practice."'
L0337:	db	00
L0338:	db	'patients'
L0340:	db	00
L0341:	db	'Lord British'
L034D:	db	00
L034E:	db	'practice'
L0356:	db	00
L0357:	db	'"My practice grew swiftly. I am a modest man, but I do not m'
	db	'ind saying that I was a popular healer."'
L03BB:	db	00
L03BC:	db	'practice'
L03C4:	db	00
L03C5:	db	'"He is probably the best healer in all Britannia. Why, he cu'
	db	'red a, er, particular problem I had in no time at all."*'
L0439:	db	00
L043A:	db	'"Oh? What problem was that?"*'
L0457:	db	00
L0458:	db	'"Never mind. The whole world does not need to know about it.'
	db	'"*'
L0496:	db	00
L0497:	db	'Lord British'
L04A3:	db	00
L04A4:	db	'"Well, Lord British himself was struck down with some sort o'
	db	'f malady. He sent for me. I arrived at the castle as soon as'
	db	' I could leave my patients, and I examined the king. It appe'
	db	'ared to me that something had infested his blood. I have a t'
	db	'heory about it, which I am convinced is correct. Others, how'
	db	'ever, do not share my view."'
L05EC:	db	00
L05ED:	db	'Lord British'
L05F9:	db	00
L05FA:	db	'others'
L0600:	db	00
L0601:	db	'theory'
L0607:	db	00
L0608:	db	'theory'
L060E:	db	00
L060F:	db	'"I believe that most sicknesses are caused by tiny living th'
	db	'ings. We cannot see these things with the naked eye. However'
	db	', I am working on developing an instrument which -can- see t'
	db	'hese creatures. I believe that someday, healing will not dep'
	db	'end on magic at all, but on some form of treatment which mak'
	db	'es one less vulnerable to these living creatures. Since thes'
	db	'e animals are biological, I call this theorized treatment 'a'
	db	'ntibiotics'. What dost thou think, Avatar? Am I on the right'
	db	' track?"'
L07F7:	db	00
L07F8:	db	'theory'
L07FE:	db	00
L07FF:	db	'"Good. I thought so."'
L0814:	db	00
L0815:	db	'"No? Hmmm." Csil looks concerned. "Well, I cannot believe in'
	db	' the archaic tradition of bleeding a person until the sickne'
	db	'ss has left his body. There must be another way..."~~Csil lo'
	db	'oks at his notes, worried that his theory is invalid.'
L08FE:	db	00
L08FF:	db	'others'
L0905:	db	00
L0906:	db	'"There is a group of people who do not encourage my studies.'
	db	' We do not get along at all. I think they have something aga'
	db	'inst healers which goes beyond simple distrust. Dost thou kn'
	db	'ow whom I mean?"'
L09CA:	db	00
L09CB:	db	'Csil nods. "I thought so. The Fellowship is not... quite wha'
	db	't they seem."'
L0A14:	db	00
L0A15:	db	'"No?" Csil lowers his voice. "The Fellowship."'
L0A43:	db	00
L0A44:	db	'others'
L0A4A:	db	00
L0A4B:	db	'Fellowship'
L0A55:	db	00
L0A56:	db	'Fellowship'
L0A60:	db	00
L0A61:	db	'"They have a doctrine which outlines their beliefs. They bel'
	db	'ieve if one is faced with pain, then he has no choice but to'
	db	' go through it in order to be a 'better person'. I do not ag'
	db	'ree with this. No one should ever go through needless pain. '
	db	'But... they are entitled to their own opinions."'
L0B81:	db	00
L0B82:	db	'Fellowship'
L0B8C:	db	00
L0B8D:	db	'services'
L0B95:	db	00
L0B96:	db	'bye'
L0B99:	db	00
L0B9A:	db	'"Goodbye, Avatar."*'
L0BAD:	db	00
