L0000:	db	'Patterson is concentrating on the Fellowship meeting and doe'
	db	's not wish to speak.*'
L0051:	db	00
L0052:	db	'"I wonder where Batlin could be! 'Tis not like him to miss a'
	db	' meeting."'
L0098:	db	00
L0099:	db	'"I cannot stop to speak right now. I am late for the Fellows'
	db	'hip meeting!"*'
L00E3:	db	00
L00E4:	db	'bye'
L00E7:	db	00
L00E8:	db	'job'
L00EB:	db	00
L00EC:	db	'name'
L00F0:	db	00
L00F1:	db	'Candice'
L00F8:	db	00
L00F9:	db	'body'
L00FD:	db	00
L00FE:	db	'You see a nobleman in his forties who looks like either a po'
	db	'litician or a well-dressed merchant.'
L015E:	db	00
L015F:	db	'"Avatar! I was just alerted of thy presence in our fair city'
	db	'! I have been expecting thee!"'
L01B9:	db	00
L01BA:	db	'"Avatar! Er, uhm, how art thee? Oh, dost thou know Candice, '
	db	'the curator at the Royal Museum? She is a 'brother' at The F'
	db	'ellowship. I was, er, just seeing her home!"'
L025E:	db	00
L025F:	db	'"Hmmm. And does thy wife know thou art seeing Candice home?"'
L029B:	db	00
L029C:	db	'You ask if Judith knows about this.'
L02BF:	db	00
L02C0:	db	'"Why, she doth not need to know! It does not matter! 'Tis no'
	db	'thing, really!"~~The Mayor is sweating profusely. He looks a'
	db	't you with beady eyes. He knows he has been found out. His b'
	db	'ody slumps. He is mortified and ashamed.~~"Thou hast discove'
	db	'red my... our secret. Please do not tell Judith. I... will e'
	db	'nd this. I swear. Candice -- we must stop meeting. I... I'm '
	db	'sorry."~~You decide to leave Patterson and Candice to work o'
	db	'ut what has happened, and you hope that the Mayor has learne'
	db	'd something about honesty.*'
L04BB:	db	00
L04BC:	db	'"How may I help thee?" Patterson asks.'
L04E2:	db	00
L04E3:	db	'"How may I help thee?" Patterson asks.'
L0509:	db	00
L050A:	db	'name'
L050E:	db	00
L050F:	db	'"I am Patterson. Named after my father." He holds his hand o'
	db	'ut, takes yours, and shakes it firmly. "It is such a pleasur'
	db	'e to meet the Avatar!"'
L059D:	db	00
L059E:	db	'name'
L05A2:	db	00
L05A3:	db	'job'
L05A6:	db	00
L05A7:	db	'"Why, I am the Town Mayor! The Town Mayor of Britain, that i'
	db	's! I would have thee know that mine election was an overwhel'
	db	'ming victory! Mine opponent never had a chance!~~ "I am also'
	db	' President of the Britannian Tax Council."'
L0685:	db	00
L0686:	db	'Tax Council'
L0691:	db	00
L0692:	db	'opponent'
L069A:	db	00
L069B:	db	'election'
L06A3:	db	00
L06A4:	db	'election'
L06AC:	db	00
L06AD:	db	'"It was held two years ago. I received 84 percent of the vot'
	db	'es. It was an impressive victory, I must admit.~~ "Of course'
	db	', when one has a group like The Fellowship behind them..."'
L075F:	db	00
L0760:	db	'election'
L0768:	db	00
L0769:	db	'Fellowship'
L0773:	db	00
L0774:	db	'opponent'
L077C:	db	00
L077D:	db	'"He was an old farmer named Brownie. Didn't have much money '
	db	'to put into a campaign. Even the peasants didn't support him'
	db	'."'
L07F7:	db	00
L07F8:	db	'opponent'
L0800:	db	00
L0801:	db	'peasants'
L0809:	db	00
L080A:	db	'Fellowship'
L0814:	db	00
L0815:	db	'"My life has improved greatly since I joined. I find that mi'
	db	'ne honesty is impeccable, my leadership is unchallengeable, '
	db	'and my love for my wife is irreproachable.'
L08B7:	db	00
L08B8:	db	'"Thou shouldst consider attending one of our meetings in the'
	db	' evening."'
L08FE:	db	00
L08FF:	db	'"I would wager that thy life has improved as well!"'
L0932:	db	00
L0933:	db	'Fellowship'
L093D:	db	00
L093E:	db	'wife'
L0942:	db	00
L0943:	db	'honesty'
L094A:	db	00
L094B:	db	'peasants'
L0953:	db	00
L0954:	db	'"Did I say that? I certainly did not mean it. There is no cl'
	db	'ass system in Britain anymore, nor in the entire country, fo'
	db	'r that matter! What I meant is that the 'peasantry', that is'
	db	', those people who are not of superior lineage -- which is t'
	db	'he type of man Brownie is -- -they- did not support him eith'
	db	'er. They knew who would be the best leader!"'
L0AAC:	db	00
L0AAD:	db	'peasants'
L0AB5:	db	00
L0AB6:	db	'superior'
L0ABE:	db	00
L0ABF:	db	'superior'
L0AC7:	db	00
L0AC8:	db	'"Did I say that? I do not think I really meant that the way '
	db	'it sounded. What I meant to say was that there are people wh'
	db	'o come from families of better standing than others. And Bro'
	db	'wnie is not one of them! But do not misunderstand me -- I st'
	db	'ill maintain that the class system in Britannia has been abo'
	db	'lished!"'
L0BFC:	db	00
L0BFD:	db	'superior'
L0C05:	db	00
L0C06:	db	'Nanna'
L0C0B:	db	00
L0C0C:	db	'Nanna'
L0C11:	db	00
L0C12:	db	'"She said what? Well, she's wrong! And to think she is a 'br'
	db	'other'. One of The Fellowship! I shall have to speak to Batl'
	db	'in about her."~~You notice that Patterson seems ill-at-ease.'
L0CC6:	db	00
L0CC7:	db	'Nanna'
L0CCC:	db	00
L0CCD:	db	'honesty'
L0CD4:	db	00
L0CD5:	db	'"I am obviously the most honest person in Britain! Perhaps I'
	db	' should move to Moonglow! Ha!"'
L0D2F:	db	00
L0D30:	db	'honesty'
L0D37:	db	00
L0D38:	db	'Judith suspicious'
L0D49:	db	00
L0D4A:	db	'wife'
L0D4E:	db	00
L0D4F:	db	'"Her name is Judith. She's the music teacher at The Music Ha'
	db	'll. Perhaps thou hast met her. We have a wonderful relations'
	db	'hip."'
L0DCC:	db	00
L0DCD:	db	'wife'
L0DD1:	db	00
L0DD2:	db	'Tax Council'
L0DDD:	db	00
L0DDE:	db	'"The land must have some way of generating income. Taxes are'
	db	' the only solution. Every merchant and farmer is taxed. Anyo'
	db	'ne who works for a living is taxed."~~ "The Britannian Tax C'
	db	'ouncil has its main office in the Royal Mint."'
L0EC0:	db	00
L0EC1:	db	'Tax Council'
L0ECC:	db	00
L0ECD:	db	'Judith suspicious'
L0EDE:	db	00
L0EDF:	db	'"Why, I do not know what she is talking about! I work late, '
	db	'that is all!"'
L0F28:	db	00
L0F29:	db	'Iolo whispers to you, "This man seems very defensive, dost t'
	db	'hou not think? I say we should observe him and see where he '
	db	'goes after The Fellowship meeting tonight."'
L0FCC:	db	00
L0FCD:	db	'Judith suspicious'
L0FDE:	db	00
L0FDF:	db	'Candice'
L0FE6:	db	00
L0FE7:	db	'Patterson's eyes widen and for a moment looks very nervous. '
	db	'But very quickly he regains his composure.~~ "Candice? Why, '
	db	'she is a friend! A 'brother' at The Fellowship! That is all!'
	db	'"'
L109C:	db	00
L109D:	db	'Candice'
L10A4:	db	00
L10A5:	db	'body'
L10A9:	db	00
L10AA:	db	'You relate what Lord British said about the murder in Britai'
	db	'n a few years ago. Patterson nods.~~"I remember it well. Qui'
	db	'te gruesome, it was. There was a man named Finster who was r'
	db	'unning for public office. He was quite outspoken in his opin'
	db	'ions, and I suppose this got him into trouble."'
L11C9:	db	00
L11CA:	db	'body'
L11CE:	db	00
L11CF:	db	'opinions'
L11D7:	db	00
L11D8:	db	'opinions'
L11E0:	db	00
L11E1:	db	'"He was trying to make many social changes. He wanted more p'
	db	'ower for the Great Council and the Britannian Tax Council, a'
	db	'nd he wanted to disband The Fellowship. Finster was a noblem'
	db	'an with too much ambition. Anyway, his beliefs must have pro'
	db	'vided him with a few enemies."'
L12EF:	db	00
L12F0:	db	'opinions'
L12F8:	db	00
L12F9:	db	'enemies'
L1300:	db	00
L1301:	db	'enemies'
L1308:	db	00
L1309:	db	'"How should I know? Anyway, his body was found in an abandon'
	db	'ed building which is no longer standing. It used to be a sto'
	db	'rehouse of some kind, up near the castle. It was torn down a'
	db	' couple of years ago. The body was mutilated beyond belief. '
	db	'It was as if someone tied the poor man down with stakes and '
	db	'cut off all of his limbs. Finster was then beheaded. It was '
	db	'almost... what is the word... ritualistic!~~"And that is all'
	db	' I remember. No one was ever arrested for the crime."'
L14E2:	db	00
L14E3:	db	'enemies'
L14EA:	db	00
L14EB:	db	'bye'
L14EE:	db	00
L14EF:	db	'Patterson nods his head at you.*'
L150F:	db	00
