L0C60:	db	'Carrocio looks as if he is lost in a memory. After a moment '
	db	'he returns to reality.~~"I would not be a gentleman if I spo'
	db	'ke of this more, Forgive me the candor of mine heart's open '
	db	'door."~He appears somewhat embarrassed and clears his throat'
	db	' loudly several times.'
L0D66:	db	00
L0D67:	db	'wicked thrill'
L0D74:	db	00
L0D75:	db	'marriage'
L0D7D:	db	00
L0D7E:	db	'"My coins are arrows rushing to make good,~"'Til the day whe'
	db	'n the jeweller sells his ring,~"For my sure heart is not but'
	db	' carved from wood,~"And she doth tend to the bed of a king."'
L0E32:	db	00
L0E33:	db	'marriage'
