		.data
L0000:	db	'bye'
L0003:	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
L0007:	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
L000C:	db	00
L000D:	db	'Cynthia said'
L0019:	db	00
L001A:	db	'You see a sour-faced innkeeper who looks at you as if all of'
	db	' his problems were your fault.'
L0074:	db	00
L0075:	db	'"What must I do for thee now, '
L0093:	db	00
L0094:	db	'?" asks James.'
L00A2:	db	00
L00A3:	db	'name'
L00A7:	db	00
L00A8:	db	'"My name is James."'
L00BB:	db	00
L00BC:	db	'name'
L00C0:	db	00
L00C1:	db	'job'
L00C4:	db	00
L00C5:	db	'"I am the proprietor of the inn."'
L00E6:	db	00
L00E7:	db	'inn'
L00EA:	db	00
L00EB:	db	'proprietor'
L00F5:	db	00
L00F6:	db	'proprietor'
L0100:	db	00
L0101:	db	'"It is just another way of saying that I am the man who is t'
	db	'he desk clerk. Which thou mayest think is an easy job althou'
	db	'gh it is not, I can assure thee."'
L019A:	db	00
L019B:	db	'proprietor'
L01A5:	db	00
L01A6:	db	'not easy'
L01AE:	db	00
L01AF:	db	'desk clerk'
L01B9:	db	00
L01BA:	db	'inn'
L01BD:	db	00
L01BE:	db	'"This place is called the Wayfarer's Inn. It has a long and '
	db	'substantial history in Britain. If thy grandparents ever cam'
	db	'e to town this is probably where they stayed."'
L0264:	db	00
L0265:	db	'inn'
L0268:	db	00
L0269:	db	'desk clerk'
L0273:	db	00
L0274:	db	'"Of course, being desk clerk is not all I do. I must spend a'
	db	'll day listening to people talk about their problems as if I'
	db	' am supposed to solve them!"'
L0308:	db	00
L0309:	db	'desk clerk'
L0313:	db	00
L0314:	db	'solve'
L0319:	db	00
L031A:	db	'listening'
L0323:	db	00
L0324:	db	'listening'
L032D:	db	00
L032E:	db	'"That is correct, '
L0340:	db	00
L0341:	db	'. So if thou dost have a problem, allow me the courtesy of n'
	db	'ot having to hear all about it. Now what was it that I was s'
	db	'aying again?"'
L03C6:	db	00
L03C7:	db	'listening'
L03D0:	db	00
L03D1:	db	'solve'
L03D6:	db	00
L03D7:	db	'"Maybe solving people's problems is an easy task for other i'
	db	'nnkeepers, but, not only am I bad at it, I have mine own pro'
	db	'blems as well."'
L045E:	db	00
L045F:	db	'solve'
L0464:	db	00
L0465:	db	'problems'
L046D:	db	00
L046E:	db	'problems'
L0476:	db	00
L0477:	db	'"I do not like my job! I never wanted to be an innkeeper, I '
	db	'just wanted to keep the place going after my father passed o'
	db	'n. Now that I am married to Cynthia, I am more tied down tha'
	db	'n ever!"'
L0533:	db	00
L0534:	db	'problems'
L053C:	db	00
L053D:	db	'Cynthia'
L0544:	db	00
L0545:	db	'innkeeper'
L054E:	db	00
L054F:	db	'innkeeper'
L0558:	db	00
L0559:	db	'"Instead of being an innkeeper I always secretly wanted to b'
	db	'e a pirate! When I was not sailing the seas I would be livin'
	db	'g in Buccaneer's Den."'
L05E7:	db	00
L05E8:	db	'innkeeper'
L05F1:	db	00
L05F2:	db	'Buccaneer's Den'
L0601:	db	00
L0602:	db	'pirate'
L0608:	db	00
L0609:	db	'Buccaneer's Den'
L0618:	db	00
L0619:	db	'"As I understand it they have an excellent House of Games th'
	db	'ere as well as opulent baths. Or at least so I have heard fr'
	db	'om Gordon, the man who sells fish and chips."'
L06BE:	db	00
L06BF:	db	'Buccaneer's Den'
L06CE:	db	00
L06CF:	db	'Cynthia'
L06D6:	db	00
L06D7:	db	'"Do not mistake my words, '
L06F1:	db	00
L06F2:	db	'. I love Cynthia with all mine heart. But there are I times '
	db	'I feel I am too young to be married. Besides, I know I canno'
	db	't be a good husband for her."'
L0787:	db	00
L0788:	db	'Cynthia'
L078F:	db	00
L0790:	db	'good husband'
L079C:	db	00
L079D:	db	'pirate'
L07A3:	db	00
L07A4:	db	'"Thou knowest for certain that few if any people would pour '
	db	'their troubles out to pirates. If I were a pirate I could ge'
	db	't this bad foot replaced with a peg, too!"'
L0846:	db	00
L0847:	db	'pirate'
L084D:	db	00
L084E:	db	'good husband'
L085A:	db	00
L085B:	db	'"How can I make Cynthia happy on the pittance an innkeeper m'
	db	'akes when all day long she is counting all that money in the'
	db	' mint? I know I cannot."'
L08EB:	db	00
L08EC:	db	'good husband'
L08F8:	db	00
L08F9:	db	'mint'
L08FD:	db	00
L08FE:	db	'happy'
L0903:	db	00
L0904:	db	'mint'
L0908:	db	00
L0909:	db	'"I know the nature of the heart, my good friend. After being'
	db	' exposed to such large sums of money she shall begin to cove'
	db	't it. As I cannot provide it, she shall leave me to give her'
	db	' heart to a wealthy man. Perhaps a merchant or a nobleman. T'
	db	'he thought of it makes my blood boil."'
L0A1F:	db	00
L0A20:	db	'mint'
L0A24:	db	00
L0A25:	db	'not easy'
L0A2D:	db	00
L0A2E:	db	'"When one is an innkeeper one must run around all day long. '
	db	'If anyone wants anything thou art the one who must take care'
	db	' of it for them!"'
L0AB7:	db	00
L0AB8:	db	'not easy'
L0AC0:	db	00
L0AC1:	db	'room'
L0AC5:	db	00
L0AC6:	db	'run around'
L0AD0:	db	00
L0AD1:	db	'run around'
L0ADB:	db	00
L0ADC:	db	'"I spend so much time running around that I have gotten a ba'
	db	'd foot."'
L0B20:	db	00
L0B21:	db	'run around'
L0B2B:	db	00
L0B2C:	db	'happy'
L0B31:	db	00
L0B32:	db	'"Already I can sense she is worried about our marriage. I kn'
	db	'ow that there is something wrong between us."'
L0B9B:	db	00
L0B9C:	db	'happy'
L0BA1:	db	00
L0BA2:	db	'room'
L0BA6:	db	00
L0BA7:	db	'"Oh, I suppose thou wouldst like a room now! There, that is '
	db	'just what I mean! It is ten gold pieces per person for a nig'
	db	'ht. Thou dost want a room, dost thou not?"'
L0C49:	db	00
L0C4A:	db	'"Thou art carrying too much to take the room key!"'
L0C7C:	db	00
L0C7D:	db	'"Here is thy room key. It is only good until thou leavest th'
	db	'e inn."'
L0CC0:	db	00
L0CC1:	db	'"Thou dost not have enough gold to get a room here. Now I su'
	db	'ppose thou shalt be telling me all about how such a sorry st'
	db	'ate befell thee. Well, I shall not listen to thee!"'
L0D6C:	db	00
L0D6D:	db	'James wipes his brow. "Phew! That was a close call!"'
L0DA1:	db	00
L0DA2:	db	'"Please, '
L0DAB:	db	00
L0DAC:	db	'. Do allow me some time to myself! Presently I am not doing '
	db	'the business of the inn and I do wish to keep it that way. T'
	db	'hou must attend to the inn during business hours."'
L0E56:	db	00
L0E57:	db	'room'
L0E5B:	db	00
L0E5C:	db	'Cynthia said'
L0E68:	db	00
L0E69:	db	'You repeat the words that Cynthia had said to you about him.'
	db	' A smile comes across his face. "Aww, who wants to be a pira'
	db	'te anyway? I would hate that!" With that he goes back to wip'
	db	'ing the bar, but you notice that the smile is still there.'
L0F57:	db	00
L0F58:	db	'Cynthia'
L0F5F:	db	00
L0F60:	db	'bye'
L0F63:	db	00
L0F64:	db	'"Oh, thou shalt just come back again wanting something else '
	db	'from me! I just know it!"*'
L0FBA:	db	00
