		.data
L0000:	db	'bye'
L0003:	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
L0007:	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
L000C:	db	00
L000D:	db	'Jeanette'
L0015:	db	00
L0016:	db	'made bread'
L0020:	db	00
L0021:	db	'sell flour'
L002B:	db	00
L002C:	db	'You see a very clean-looking, portly young man who waves at '
	db	'you frantically.'
L0078:	db	00
L0079:	db	'"Ah, hello there! Good to see thee again!" says Willy.'
L00AF:	db	00
L00B0:	db	'name'
L00B4:	db	00
L00B5:	db	'"My given name is Wilhelm, although no one calls me that. I '
	db	'prefer to be addressed as Willy. Thank thee very much."'
L0128:	db	00
L0129:	db	'name'
L012D:	db	00
L012E:	db	'job'
L0131:	db	00
L0132:	db	'"I am the baker here in Britain and I make the sweetest brea'
	db	'd thou hast ever tasted! '
L0187:	db	00
L0188:	db	'"Hast thou had a chance to sample any of my bread yet?"'
L01BF:	db	00
L01C0:	db	'"Ah, then thou dost agree it is the sweetest, dost thou not?'
	db	'"'
L01FD:	db	00
L01FE:	db	'"Ha! Thou dost see, then? Everyone agrees! That should be pr'
	db	'oof enough!"'
L0246:	db	00
L0247:	db	'"I want some!"*'
L0256:	db	00
L0257:	db	'"Here thou art, laddie." Willy hands Spark a pastry and the '
	db	'boy devours it in one gulp.*'
L02AF:	db	00
L02B0:	db	'"Mmmmm! I say, '
L02BF:	db	00
L02C0:	db	', I think we need a lot of this for the road. We had best bu'
	db	'y some, all right?"*'
L0310:	db	00
L0311:	db	'"Thou dost not?! Why, do not be ridiculous! Of course thou d'
	db	'ost!"'
L0352:	db	00
L0353:	db	'"Then here, thou must have some!" He tears a piece of bread '
	db	'off of one of several loaves he is carrying and stuffs it in'
	db	'to your mouth. "There! Is it not the sweetest bread thou has'
	db	't ever tasted? It is, is it not?!" You chew as fast as you c'
	db	'an in order to answer him.'
L045D:	db	00
L045E:	db	'He grabs your face by the cheeks and plants a big kiss on yo'
	db	'ur forehead. "Thou art truly a person of good palate and ref'
	db	'ined taste!"'
L04E2:	db	00
L04E3:	db	'Dejectedly Willy looks down at the loaf of bread he is carry'
	db	'ing. He sniffs at it twice and tosses it out of sight.'
L0555:	db	00
L0556:	db	'bread'
L055B:	db	00
L055C:	db	'baker'
L0561:	db	00
L0562:	db	'"Please come to the bakery when it is open in daytime hours '
	db	'and thou shalt sample some!"'
L05BA:	db	00
L05BB:	db	'baker'
L05C0:	db	00
L05C1:	db	'He nods. "Yes, I am a baker and I have many secret recipes p'
	db	'assed down to me by my father and mother. Why, there are eve'
	db	'n those who say I am a master baker!'
L065D:	db	00
L065E:	db	'"And there are those who call me a... doughnut," he says wit'
	db	'h a frown.'
L06A4:	db	00
L06A5:	db	'baker'
L06AA:	db	00
L06AB:	db	'doughnut'
L06B3:	db	00
L06B4:	db	'master baker'
L06C0:	db	00
L06C1:	db	'father and mother'
L06D2:	db	00
L06D3:	db	'secret recipes'
L06E1:	db	00
L06E2:	db	'secret recipes'
L06F0:	db	00
L06F1:	db	'"Oh, dear. Do not tell me that thou art yet another person w'
	db	'ho is trying to pry one of my secret recipes out of me! If t'
	db	'hat is what thou art after then thou wilt just be disappoint'
	db	'ed!"'
L07A9:	db	00
L07AA:	db	'secret recipes'
L07B8:	db	00
L07B9:	db	'father and mother'
L07CA:	db	00
L07CB:	db	'Willy wipes away a tear. "Gone. Both of them. Gone to join m'
	db	'ine ancestors in that great kitchen in the sky. I will never'
	db	' be able to cook as they did. Still I plod along, trying to '
	db	'keep the family name alive, and that is why I am a baker. Bu'
	db	't I suppose it is not the only reason."'
L08E2:	db	00
L08E3:	db	'father and mother'
L08F4:	db	00
L08F5:	db	'why'
L08F8:	db	00
L08F9:	db	'master baker'
L0905:	db	00
L0906:	db	'"Yes, many people tell me that. Now thou dost say it, too. I'
	db	'f thou dost say so, then it must be true!"'
L096C:	db	00
L096D:	db	'Willy takes a bite of his own bread. "Mmmm. I -am- a master '
	db	'baker!"'
L09B0:	db	00
L09B1:	db	'master baker'
L09BD:	db	00
L09BE:	db	'doughnut'
L09C6:	db	00
L09C7:	db	'He gives you a long puzzled look. After a moment he takes on'
	db	'e of his loaves of bread and swats you over the head with it'
	db	'.'
L0A40:	db	00
L0A41:	db	'doughnut'
L0A49:	db	00
L0A4A:	db	'why'
L0A4D:	db	00
L0A4E:	db	'"Actually, there is a very good reason why I am a baker."'
L0A87:	db	00
L0A88:	db	'why'
L0A8B:	db	00
L0A8C:	db	'reason'
L0A92:	db	00
L0A93:	db	'reason'
L0A99:	db	00
L0A9A:	db	'"Because the way to a woman's heart is through her stomach. '
	db	'Why, I have two women in love with me right now and I did no'
	db	't even have to pursue either one."'
L0B34:	db	00
L0B35:	db	'reason'
L0B3B:	db	00
L0B3C:	db	'two women'
L0B45:	db	00
L0B46:	db	'two women'
L0B4F:	db	00
L0B50:	db	'He sighs. "If thou must know, their names are Jeanette and G'
	db	'aye."'
L0B91:	db	00
L0B92:	db	'two women'
L0B9B:	db	00
L0B9C:	db	'Gaye'
L0BA0:	db	00
L0BA1:	db	'Jeanette'
L0BA9:	db	00
L0BAA:	db	'Jeanette'
L0BB2:	db	00
L0BB3:	db	'"Jeanette is a pleasant enough girl, but to be honest I cann'
	db	'ot see myself with a tavern wench. She thinks I have not not'
	db	'iced how she feels about me. Frankly, I wish she would just '
	db	'leave me alone."'
L0C77:	db	00
L0C78:	db	'Jeanette'
L0C80:	db	00
L0C81:	db	'Gaye'
L0C85:	db	00
L0C86:	db	'"Gaye, who runs the costume shoppe, is of more interest to m'
	db	'e. But she is a Fellowship member and I have no wish to beco'
	db	'me one. I hope that it does not prevent us from courting."'
L0D38:	db	00
L0D39:	db	'Gaye'
L0D3D:	db	00
L0D3E:	db	'bread'
L0D43:	db	00
L0D44:	db	'"My bread is the finest in Britannia. It is renown for both '
	db	'its pleasant taste and its very reasonable price. But it is '
	db	'a lot of work making enough to satisfy the constant demand f'
	db	'or it. I need to hire someone to help me."'
L0E22:	db	00
L0E23:	db	'bread'
L0E28:	db	00
L0E29:	db	'hire'
L0E2D:	db	00
L0E2E:	db	'buy'
L0E31:	db	00
L0E32:	db	'buy'
L0E35:	db	00
L0E36:	db	'"I not only have bread for sale, but pastries, cakes and rol'
	db	'ls as well. The most delicious baked goods thou couldst ever'
	db	' wish to pop into thy mouth! Wouldst thou like to buy some?"'
L0EEA:	db	00
L0EEB:	db	'"If thou wert a person of truly refined taste, thou wouldst '
	db	'buy some!"'
L0F31:	db	00
L0F32:	db	'"I am afraid the bakery is closed. Please come back during n'
	db	'ormal business hours."'
L0F84:	db	00
L0F85:	db	'buy'
L0F88:	db	00
L0F89:	db	'hire'
L0F8D:	db	00
L0F8E:	db	'"Thou couldst work for me here in the shoppe making bread. O'
	db	'r I will buy sacks of flour from thee. Thou couldst buy them'
	db	' wholesale in Paws, and I will pay thee 4 gold per sack."'
L103F:	db	00
L1040:	db	'"Dost thou wish to work here in the shoppe for me?" Willy as'
	db	'ks hopefully.'
L1089:	db	00
L108A:	db	'"Excellent! Thou canst start work immediately! I shall pay t'
	db	'hee 5 gold for every five loaves of bread thou dost make. Al'
	db	'l right?"'
L110B:	db	00
L110C:	db	'"First thou must make dough from the flour. Simply spread so'
	db	'me flour out on the table, add some water to make it thick a'
	db	'nd, well, doughy. Then use the dough in the oven to bake it.'
	db	' Wait a bit, then-- voila! Thou dost have bread!"'
L11F1:	db	00
L11F2:	db	'"Very well. But I warn thee that employment is hard to obtai'
	db	'n in these times!"'
L1240:	db	00
L1241:	db	'"'Tis a pity thou art unavailable. Thou dost look like one w'
	db	'ho doth know their way around a kitchen."'
L12A6:	db	00
L12A7:	db	'"I would be happy to talk with thee about employment at my s'
	db	'hoppe during normal business hours."'
L1307:	db	00
L1308:	db	'hire'
L130C:	db	00
L130D:	db	'made bread'
L1317:	db	00
L1318:	db	'made bread'
L1322:	db	00
L1323:	db	'sell flour'
L132D:	db	00
L132E:	db	'sell flour'
L1338:	db	00
L1339:	db	'bye'
L133C:	db	00
L133D:	db	'"Good day to thee, '
L1350:	db	00
L1351:	db	', and bon appetit!"*'
L1365:	db	00
L1366:	db	'@Luscious bread!@'
L1377:	db	00
L1378:	db	'@Delicious pastries!@'
L138D:	db	00
L138E:	db	'@Bread fit for a king!@'
L13A5:	db	00
L13A6:	db	'@Fresh pastries!@'
