		.data
L0000:	db	'bye'
L0003:	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
L0007:	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
L000C:	db	00
L000D:	db	'Crown Jewel'
L0018:	db	00
L0019:	db	'Before you stands an old sailing man whose determined face a'
	db	'ppears to have weathered many a storm.'
L007B:	db	00
L007C:	db	'"And what be thy business with me this time, '
L00A9:	db	00
L00AA:	db	'?" says Clint.'
L00B8:	db	00
L00B9:	db	'name'
L00BD:	db	00
L00BE:	db	'"I be Clint."'
L00CB:	db	00
L00CC:	db	'name'
L00D0:	db	00
L00D1:	db	'job'
L00D4:	db	00
L00D5:	db	'"In my youth I was a sailor who sailed across the sea in tal'
	db	'l ships. Now I must content myself solely with selling ships'
	db	' and sextants to others."'
L0166:	db	00
L0167:	db	'buy'
L016A:	db	00
L016B:	db	'sailor'
L0171:	db	00
L0172:	db	'sailor'
L0178:	db	00
L0179:	db	'"Of course this was in the day when it took mighty men to be'
	db	' a sailor. Nowadays those who set out to sea would not have '
	db	'lasted a day. But I suppose it is the nature of the universe'
	db	' that everything slowly becomes more tame."'
L0258:	db	00
L0259:	db	'sailor'
L025F:	db	00
L0260:	db	'tame'
L0264:	db	00
L0265:	db	'tame'
L0269:	db	00
L026A:	db	'"Soon all the monsters will die off and the whole world will'
	db	' join together in trust and worthiness and unity like all th'
	db	'ose Fellowship people say. Bah! The world was a better place'
	db	' when everybody fought everybody else, I say."'
L034C:	db	00
L034D:	db	'tame'
L0351:	db	00
L0352:	db	'Fellowship'
L035C:	db	00
L035D:	db	'Fellowship'
L0367:	db	00
L0368:	db	'"No offense intended, of course. I did not realize that thou'
	db	' art a member." Clint reacts as if he has just touched a lep'
	db	'er.'
L03E3:	db	00
L03E4:	db	'Fellowship'
L03EE:	db	00
L03EF:	db	'"It is always the best thing to make thine own way in the wo'
	db	'rld and not listen to what thou art told to believe. Thou ha'
	db	'st better remember that!"'
L0480:	db	00
L0481:	db	'Fellowship'
L048B:	db	00
L048C:	db	'buy'
L048F:	db	00
L0490:	db	'"If thou art in need of a ship I hold the deed to a fine one'
	db	'. Thou wilt also need a sextant to help steer her true."'
L0504:	db	00
L0505:	db	'buy sextant'
L0510:	db	00
L0511:	db	'buy ship deed'
L051E:	db	00
L051F:	db	'"My business is now closed. Return another time and I will b'
	db	'e happy to serve thee, '
L0572:	db	00
L0573:	db	'."'
L0575:	db	00
L0576:	db	'buy'
L0579:	db	00
L057A:	db	'buy ship deed'
L0587:	db	00
L0588:	db	'"I do believe I sold thee the deed to 'The Beast'! What happ'
	db	'ened to it? Hast thou lost the ship? If so, then thou must f'
	db	'ind another shipwright!"'
L0618:	db	00
L0619:	db	'"The deed to the ship 'The Beast' costs eight hundred gold p'
	db	'ieces. Dost thou wish to purchase her?"'
L067C:	db	00
L067D:	db	'"Here is thy deed, '
L0690:	db	00
L0691:	db	'."'
L0693:	db	00
L0694:	db	'"I would give thee thy deed but thou art carrying too much t'
	db	'o take it from me!"'
L06E3:	db	00
L06E4:	db	'"Thou dost not have enough gold to buy a ship!"'
L0713:	db	00
L0714:	db	'"If thou dost need a ship be sure to come back here."'
L0749:	db	00
L074A:	db	'buy ship deed'
L0757:	db	00
L0758:	db	'buy sextant'
L0763:	db	00
L0764:	db	'"A sextant costs one hundred gold pieces. Does thou wish to '
	db	'buy one?"'
L07A9:	db	00
L07AA:	db	'"Here is thy sextant. She shall steer thee true, to be sure.'
	db	'"'
L07E7:	db	00
L07E8:	db	'"I would give thee thy sextant, but thou art carrying too mu'
	db	'ch to take it from me."'
L083B:	db	00
L083C:	db	'"Thou dost not have enough money to buy a sextant!"'
L086F:	db	00
L0870:	db	'"If thou shouldst ever need a sextant be sure to come back."'
L08AC:	db	00
L08AD:	db	'buy sextant'
L08B8:	db	00
L08B9:	db	'Crown Jewel'
L08C4:	db	00
L08C5:	db	'"The Crown Jewel came to Britain? Not anytime recently. Most'
	db	' certainly not. I remember the Crown Jewel and it has not be'
	db	'en to Britain for a long time."'
L095C:	db	00
L095D:	db	'"As I have told thee before, the Crown Jewel has not been he'
	db	're in a long time."'
L09AC:	db	00
L09AD:	db	'Crown Jewel'
L09B8:	db	00
L09B9:	db	'Crown Jewel'
L09C4:	db	00
L09C5:	db	'bye'
L09C8:	db	00
L09C9:	db	'"May thy travels do well." *'
L09E5:	db	00
L09E6:	db	'@Where's that spanner?@'
L09FD:	db	00
L09FE:	db	'@Where's mine hammer?@'
L0A14:	db	00
L0A15:	db	'@Ahh, smell that sea breeze...@'
L0A34:	db	00
L0A35:	db	'@Need a ship or sextant?@'
L0A4E:	db	00
