		.data
L0000:	db	'bye'
L0003:	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
L0007:	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
L000C:	db	00
L000D:	db	'pumpkins'
L0015:	db	00
L0016:	db	'You see a farmer who, despite showing considerable wear from'
	db	' hard work, appears energetic, cheerful and friendly.'
L0087:	db	00
L0088:	db	'"Hello again, '
L0096:	db	00
L0097:	db	'," Brownie greets you.'
L00AD:	db	00
L00AE:	db	'name'
L00B2:	db	00
L00B3:	db	'"I am Brownie."'
L00C2:	db	00
L00C3:	db	'name'
L00C7:	db	00
L00C8:	db	'job'
L00CB:	db	00
L00CC:	db	'"Well, I ran for the office of Mayor of Britain once, but I '
	db	'lost. Now I am back doing what I have been doing since I was'
	db	' a boy. Working the farm."'
L015E:	db	00
L015F:	db	'farm'
L0163:	db	00
L0164:	db	'Mayor'
L0169:	db	00
L016A:	db	'Mayor'
L016F:	db	00
L0170:	db	'"Patterson won the election. He spent a lot of money on his '
	db	'campaign. Most of it to buy votes. But I am not bitter. I wa'
	db	's just not meant to be Mayor."'
L0206:	db	00
L0207:	db	'Mayor'
L020C:	db	00
L020D:	db	'election'
L0215:	db	00
L0216:	db	'Patterson'
L021F:	db	00
L0220:	db	'Patterson'
L0229:	db	00
L022A:	db	'"Patterson courted the support of The Fellowship. They force'
	db	'd a vote from all their members. Once word spread, my suppor'
	db	't drained away. No one wants to be on the losing side." Brow'
	db	'nie sighs.'
L02E8:	db	00
L02E9:	db	'Patterson'
L02F2:	db	00
L02F3:	db	'losing'
L02F9:	db	00
L02FA:	db	'Fellowship'
L0304:	db	00
L0305:	db	'election'
L030D:	db	00
L030E:	db	'"I do not really have any wish to succeed in politics. It ju'
	db	'st made me ill seeing all of the people with riches mistreat'
	db	' all of the people who are poor, and then have to listen to '
	db	'them talk about how the class system has been abolished."'
L03FB:	db	00
L03FC:	db	'election'
L0404:	db	00
L0405:	db	'Fellowship'
L040F:	db	00
L0410:	db	'Brownie gestures toward your medallion. "Frankly, I do not k'
	db	'now what thou seest in that group."'
L046F:	db	00
L0470:	db	'"If thou art not with The Fellowship thou art against them. '
	db	'I think they saw me as a potential enemy that had to be stop'
	db	'ped."'
L04ED:	db	00
L04EE:	db	'Fellowship'
L04F8:	db	00
L04F9:	db	'losing'
L04FF:	db	00
L0500:	db	'"Of course, I could have won the election if I had wanted to'
	db	'. I had information about Patterson that would have ruined a'
	db	'ny chances of him winning."'
L0593:	db	00
L0594:	db	'losing'
L059A:	db	00
L059B:	db	'information'
L05A6:	db	00
L05A7:	db	'information'
L05B2:	db	00
L05B3:	db	'"I could have revealed a secret about Patterson but if I did'
	db	' it would have hurt someone close to him very much. I did no'
	db	't want to be mayor that badly."'
L064A:	db	00
L064B:	db	'information'
L0656:	db	00
L0657:	db	'secret'
L065D:	db	00
L065E:	db	'secret'
L0664:	db	00
L0665:	db	'"Patterson does little to hide his secret. If thou dost keep'
	db	' an eye on him thou wilt surely learn of it sooner or later.'
	db	'"'
L06DE:	db	00
L06DF:	db	'secret'
L06E5:	db	00
L06E6:	db	'farm'
L06EA:	db	00
L06EB:	db	'"I feel more at home on the farm growing vegetables. There i'
	db	's another farmer named Mack who works a farm near Britain as'
	db	' well. He raises chickens."'
L077E:	db	00
L077F:	db	'farm'
L0783:	db	00
L0784:	db	'Mack'
L0788:	db	00
L0789:	db	'vegetables'
L0793:	db	00
L0794:	db	'Mack'
L0798:	db	00
L0799:	db	'"I like him. He even voted for me. But to tell thee the trut'
	db	'h about Mack, he is a lunatic."'
L07F4:	db	00
L07F5:	db	'Mack'
L07F9:	db	00
L07FA:	db	'vegetables'
L0804:	db	00
L0805:	db	'"I raise pumpkins. But I am in a bind at the moment and need'
	db	' some help."'
L084D:	db	00
L084E:	db	'vegetables'
L0858:	db	00
L0859:	db	'help'
L085D:	db	00
L085E:	db	'bind'
L0862:	db	00
L0863:	db	'bind'
L0867:	db	00
L0868:	db	'"I strained my back the other day lifting heavy pumpkins. I '
	db	'cannot so much as lift a small one today! And I need help wi'
	db	'th the harvest of pumpkins so that I can get them to the mar'
	db	'ket."'
L0921:	db	00
L0922:	db	'bind'
L0926:	db	00
L0927:	db	'help'
L092B:	db	00
L092C:	db	'"There are piles of pumpkins at the north end of the field. '
	db	'I need them brought down near my farmhouse. If thou wilt hel'
	db	'p me by bringing the pumpkins to me, I will gladly pay thee '
	db	'for thy work. How does one gold coin for every pumpkin carri'
	db	'ed sound?"'
L0A26:	db	00
L0A27:	db	'"How nice! A helper! Please, feel free to start work at any '
	db	'time!"'
L0A69:	db	00
L0A6A:	db	'"Perhaps some other time, then."'
L0A8A:	db	00
L0A8B:	db	'help'
L0A8F:	db	00
L0A90:	db	'pumpkins'
L0A98:	db	00
L0A99:	db	'"Thou shouldst simply go to the north end of the field and b'
	db	'ring back as many pumpkins as thou can carry!"'
L0B03:	db	00
L0B04:	db	'pumpkins'
L0B0C:	db	00
L0B0D:	db	'bye'
L0B10:	db	00
L0B11:	db	'"Good day, '
L0B1C:	db	00
L0B1D:	db	'."*'
L0B20:	db	00
