		.funcnumber	043DH
		.data
L0000:	db	'bye'
L0003:	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
L0007:	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
L000C:	db	00
L000D:	db	'proof'
L0012:	db	00
L0013:	db	'picked eggs'
L001E:	db	00
L001F:	db	'You see a farmer with wild eyes widened in excitement.'
L0055:	db	00
L0056:	db	'"Avatar! Thou hast returned!" exclaims Mack.'
L0082:	db	00
L0083:	db	'name'
L0087:	db	00
L0088:	db	'"I am Mack."'
L0094:	db	00
L0095:	db	'name'
L0099:	db	00
L009A:	db	'job'
L009D:	db	00
L009E:	db	'"I am a farmer, though most folks just call me a lunatic."'
L00D8:	db	00
L00D9:	db	'lunatic'
L00E0:	db	00
L00E1:	db	'farmer'
L00E7:	db	00
L00E8:	db	'farmer'
L00EE:	db	00
L00EF:	db	'"On my farm I raise chickens and grow vegetables. If thou do'
	db	'st need work, talk to me!"'
L0145:	db	00
L0146:	db	'farmer'
L014C:	db	00
L014D:	db	'work'
L0151:	db	00
L0152:	db	'lunatic'
L0159:	db	00
L015A:	db	'"Thou dost also think so, eh? But I tell thee what I say is '
	db	'true! There are creatures visiting us from another place in '
	db	'the stars! I have seen them!"'
L01EF:	db	00
L01F0:	db	'lunatic'
L01F7:	db	00
L01F8:	db	'seen them'
L0201:	db	00
L0202:	db	'another place'
L020F:	db	00
L0210:	db	'creatures'
L0219:	db	00
L021A:	db	'creatures'
L0223:	db	00
L0224:	db	'"They are big mean ugly liontigers! Or is that tigerlions? T'
	db	'hey are ferocious and they want to eat us!"'
L028B:	db	00
L028C:	db	'creatures'
L0295:	db	00
L0296:	db	'another place'
L02A3:	db	00
L02A4:	db	'"All I can say is that there are certainly no such creatures'
	db	' in this world! Nor is their ship like any that has ever bee'
	db	'n seen anywhere in Britannia."'
L033A:	db	00
L033B:	db	'another place'
L0348:	db	00
L0349:	db	'seen them'
L0352:	db	00
L0353:	db	'"With mine own eyes I have seen a star creature and the inex'
	db	'plicable conveyance which enabled it to travel to Britannia!'
	db	' I swear to thee! I am completely sane! I have proof!"'
L0401:	db	00
L0402:	db	'seen them'
L040B:	db	00
L040C:	db	'proof'
L0411:	db	00
L0412:	db	'proof'
L0417:	db	00
L0418:	db	'"Go and look behind my farm in the middle of the field. Take'
	db	' a look for thyself and thou shalt see my proof."'
L0485:	db	00
L0486:	db	'"I told thee I was not a looney! Didst thou see the proof?"'
L04C1:	db	00
L04C2:	db	'"Thou must go and look at what is in my field! Then come bac'
	db	'k here, for I must talk about this with someone who knows th'
	db	'at I am not a looney!"'
L0550:	db	00
L0551:	db	'proof'
L0556:	db	00
L0557:	db	'"Did I not tell thee that I am no loonie? Still, my story of'
	db	' how I did come across this thing is beyond belief."'
L05C7:	db	00
L05C8:	db	'proof'
L05CD:	db	00
L05CE:	db	'story'
L05D3:	db	00
L05D4:	db	'story'
L05D9:	db	00
L05DA:	db	'"I like to stay up late. Sometimes I see bright lights flash'
	db	' across the sky. No one else ever pays them any mind. But on'
	db	'e night I see this bright light come crashing down and it la'
	db	'nds in my field."'
L069F:	db	00
L06A0:	db	'story'
L06A5:	db	00
L06A6:	db	'lands'
L06AB:	db	00
L06AC:	db	'bright lights'
L06B9:	db	00
L06BA:	db	'"I have been looking every night for another sign of those t'
	db	'hings but I have not seen any since that last time I told th'
	db	'ee about it."'
L073F:	db	00
L0740:	db	'story'
L0745:	db	00
L0746:	db	'bright lights'
L0753:	db	00
L0754:	db	'"I always watch for moving bright lights in the night sky. T'
	db	'hat is part of why people in the town say I am a loonie. But'
	db	' is what I do so different from what they do in the orrery?"'
L0808:	db	00
L0809:	db	'bright lights'
L0816:	db	00
L0817:	db	'lands'
L081C:	db	00
L081D:	db	'"After the explosion and crash I ran out to my field. There '
	db	'I saw the strange machine that thou hast seen, only it was g'
	db	'lowing hot. I was terrified. But then the top of the machine'
	db	' started to open."'
L08E3:	db	00
L08E4:	db	'lands'
L08E9:	db	00
L08EA:	db	'open'
L08EE:	db	00
L08EF:	db	'machine'
L08F6:	db	00
L08F7:	db	'machine'
L08FE:	db	00
L08FF:	db	'"It resembled a bird, but it was not a bird!"'
L092C:	db	00
L092D:	db	'machine'
L0934:	db	00
L0935:	db	'open'
L0939:	db	00
L093A:	db	'"I could not move from the spot as I saw the strange ship op'
	db	'en. From out of the top came the vicious tigerlion. There wa'
	db	's a savage hunger in its eyes."'
L09D1:	db	00
L09D2:	db	'open'
L09D6:	db	00
L09D7:	db	'hunger'
L09DD:	db	00
L09DE:	db	'tigerlion'
L09E7:	db	00
L09E8:	db	'hunger'
L09EE:	db	00
L09EF:	db	'"In other words, it looked like it might eat me!"'
L0A20:	db	00
L0A21:	db	'hunger'
L0A27:	db	00
L0A28:	db	'tigerlion'
L0A31:	db	00
L0A32:	db	'"It came at me like a predator comes after prey. It was so f'
	db	'ast that I could not even move. I thought I was going to be '
	db	'killed for certain. It reached me in a second. It looked int'
	db	'o mine eyes, and then it died."'
L0B05:	db	00
L0B06:	db	'tigerlion'
L0B0F:	db	00
L0B10:	db	'died'
L0B14:	db	00
L0B15:	db	'died'
L0B19:	db	00
L0B1A:	db	'"What it and I had failed to notice was that I was holding m'
	db	'ine hoe. It had once been accidentally enchanted by a passin'
	db	'g mage, and it works wondrously in the fields. I use it for '
	db	'everything! The tigerlion had run itself through upon it. As'
	db	' it died, the thing spoke."'
L0C25:	db	00
L0C26:	db	'died'
L0C2A:	db	00
L0C2B:	db	'hoe'
L0C2E:	db	00
L0C2F:	db	'spoke'
L0C34:	db	00
L0C35:	db	'spoke'
L0C3A:	db	00
L0C3B:	db	'"It said two words. "Kill Wrathy." I do not know who this Wr'
	db	'athy person is, or why the tigerlion wanted me to kill him. '
	db	'But I do know I sure get worried now whenever I see moving l'
	db	'ights in the night sky."'
L0D07:	db	00
L0D08:	db	'spoke'
L0D0D:	db	00
L0D0E:	db	'Kill Wrathy'
L0D19:	db	00
L0D1A:	db	'hoe'
L0D1D:	db	00
L0D1E:	db	'"I am sure thou dost know about the plague of looniness that'
	db	' has come to afflict all of the mages in the world. It was s'
	db	'everal years ago that I brought my broken hoe to a mage call'
	db	'ed Mumb. Fixing things was all he was good for anymore. Ther'
	db	'e was also some fighter who wanted Mumb to enchant his sword'
	db	', turning it into "The Sword of Death". It appears poor Mumb'
	db	' got confused and that fighter came back and killed him beca'
	db	'use the man wound up with a sword that was only good for cut'
	db	'ting weeds. I could never figure out exactly what happened. '
	db	'It appears that old Mumb made mine hoe into the Hoe of Destr'
	db	'uction! Unfortunately, the hoe is lost."'
L0F9E:	db	00
L0F9F:	db	'hoe'
L0FA2:	db	00
L0FA3:	db	'lost'
L0FA7:	db	00
L0FA8:	db	'lost'
L0FAC:	db	00
L0FAD:	db	'"Well, 'tis not really lost. It is locked up in my shed. It '
	db	'is the key to the shed that is lost! I think I might have ac'
	db	'cidentally used it as a fishhook when I was fishing on the b'
	db	'anks of Lock Lake. So now I cannot get into my shed. One wou'
	db	'ld think I -am- a looney!"'
L10B7:	db	00
L10B8:	db	'lost'
L10BC:	db	00
L10BD:	db	'Kill Wrathy'
L10C8:	db	00
L10C9:	db	'"I am quite certain that was it, or something like that. Any'
	db	'way the tigerlion itself proved to be quite delicious."'
L113C:	db	00
L113D:	db	'Kill Wrathy'
L1148:	db	00
L1149:	db	'work'
L114D:	db	00
L114E:	db	'"I need someone to work for me and help gather all the eggs '
	db	'being laid by the chickens! When that big thing came crashin'
	db	'g down it scared them all so much that they cannot stop layi'
	db	'ng eggs! Wilt thou work for me? I will pay thee 1 gold per e'
	db	'gg."'
L1242:	db	00
L1243:	db	'"Fine! Thou wilt find the chickens out back. Thou must feel '
	db	'around in the nest to find the eggs that are there. But ther'
	db	'e is a limit to how many they will produce in one day, of co'
	db	'urse."'
L12FD:	db	00
L12FE:	db	'"Ask me again if thou dost change thy mind."'
L132A:	db	00
L132B:	db	'work'
L132F:	db	00
L1330:	db	'picked eggs'
L133B:	db	00
L133C:	db	'picked eggs'
L1347:	db	00
L1348:	db	'bye'
L134B:	db	00
L134C:	db	'"I thank thee for thy decency and consideration."'
L137D:	db	00
