L0007:	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
L000C:	db	00
L000D:	db	'You see a filthy beggar who flashes you a grin as though you'
	db	' were his best friend in the whole world.'
L0072:	db	00
L0073:	db	'"Hello again, '
L0081:	db	00
L0082:	db	'," says Snaz.'
L008F:	db	00
L0090:	db	'name'
L0094:	db	00
L0095:	db	'"I am called Snaz."'
L00A8:	db	00
L00A9:	db	'name'
L00AD:	db	00
L00AE:	db	'job'
L00B1:	db	00
L00B2:	db	'"I have no job for I am a beggar. For a gold coin I shall te'
	db	'll thee a joke."'
L00FE:	db	00
L00FF:	db	'tell a joke'
L010A:	db	00
L010B:	db	'beggar'
L0111:	db	00
L0112:	db	'beggar'
L0118:	db	00
L0119:	db	'"When I was just a little boy I was made an orphan and left '
	db	'homeless and penniless. That was a joke life played on me. ''
	db	'Tis a funny joke, eh?~~"But I would not charge thee a gold p'
	db	'iece for that one."'
L01E0:	db	00
L01E1:	db	'beggar'
L01E7:	db	00
L01E8:	db	'tell a joke'
L01F3:	db	00
L01F4:	db	'"Dost thou wish to hear one?"'
L0211:	db	00
L0212:	db	'"All right, here is one..."'
L022D:	db	00
L022E:	db	'Fellowship joke'
L023D:	db	00
L023E:	db	'"If thou dost want to hear a joke, thou must pay me, '
L0273:	db	00
L0274:	db	'. Come back when thy pockets are full. The richer thou art, '
	db	'the funnier I get!"'
L02C3:	db	00
L02C4:	db	'"Have a heart, I pray thee! I have a wife and six hungry chi'
	db	'ldren to feed." He feels your stare upon him. "Oh, very well'
	db	'. Wouldst thou believe I have a cat and it just had kittens?'
	db	'"'
L0379:	db	00
L037A:	db	'tell a joke'
L0385:	db	00
L0386:	db	'Fellowship joke'
L0395:	db	00
L0396:	db	'"I was discussing philosophy with a Fellowship member the ot'
	db	'her day and he asked me, 'What, in thine opinion, is the hei'
	db	'ght of stupidity?'~~"So I said, 'I do not know. How tall art'
	db	' thou?'~~"No, really, I make sport of The Fellowship, but I '
	db	'mean it sincerely..."'
L049B:	db	00
L049C:	db	'Fellowship joke'
L04AB:	db	00
L04AC:	db	'Lord British joke'
L04BD:	db	00
L04BE:	db	'Fellowship'
L04C8:	db	00
L04C9:	db	'Fellowship'
L04D3:	db	00
L04D4:	db	'"That is what I dearly love about The Fellowship. They could'
	db	' always take a joke!~~"And from what I hear they play funny '
	db	'jokes themselves! Like the joke they played in Trinsic!"'
L0584:	db	00
L0585:	db	'Fellowship'
L058F:	db	00
L0590:	db	'Lord British joke'
L05A1:	db	00
L05A2:	db	'"For a gold coin I will tell thee another. Dost thou wish to'
	db	' hear it?"'
L05E8:	db	00
L05E9:	db	'"I see I have reached the limits of thy sense of humor."'
L0621:	db	00
L0622:	db	'Lord British joke'
L0633:	db	00
L0634:	db	'"I was at the castle of Lord British the other day and I not'
	db	'iced he has three large pools. So I asked why he doth have t'
	db	'hree of them.~~"He pointed to the first one and said the fir'
	db	'st was to swim in cool water. ~~"The second was for friends '
	db	'to swim in warm water.~~"I noticed that the third pool was e'
	db	'mpty and I asked him why.~~"He said that it was for people w'
	db	'ho could not swim!"'
L07AF:	db	00
L07B0:	db	'Lord British joke'
L07C1:	db	00
L07C2:	db	'Weston joke'
L07CD:	db	00
L07CE:	db	'Lord British'
L07DA:	db	00
L07DB:	db	'"Thou art more destitute than I! If I tell thee any more jok'
	db	'es now thou mayest steal mine act!"'
L083A:	db	00
L083B:	db	'Lord British joke'
L084C:	db	00
L084D:	db	'Lord British'
L0859:	db	00
L085A:	db	'"Poor Lord British! When faced with a gigantic menace that t'
	db	'hreatens his entire kingdom he is an extremely capable ruler'
	db	'.~~"But what happens when there are a myriad of smaller thin'
	db	'gs that all threaten the welfare of his people indirectly?~~'
	db	'"There is a riddle for thee to solve!"'
L0970:	db	00
L0971:	db	'Lord British'
L097D:	db	00
L097E:	db	'Weston joke'
L0989:	db	00
L098A:	db	'"For a gold coin I will tell thee another. Dost thou wish to'
	db	' hear it?"'
L09D0:	db	00
L09D1:	db	'"Very well. If thou didst not get the first two there is no '
	db	'good reason for me to continue now."'
L0A31:	db	00
L0A32:	db	'Weston joke'
L0A3D:	db	00
L0A3E:	db	'"A man named Weston came to me deep in perplexity.~~"He told'
	db	' me he wanted to steal some apples from the Royal Orchards b'
	db	'ut if he did he would feel bad about it in the morning.~~"So'
	db	' I gave him this advice -- sleep until noon!"'
L0B1F:	db	00
L0B20:	db	'Weston joke'
L0B2B:	db	00
L0B2C:	db	'mage joke'
L0B35:	db	00
L0B36:	db	'Weston'
L0B3C:	db	00
L0B3D:	db	'"Thy pockets are empty, '
L0B55:	db	00
L0B56:	db	'. Perhaps it is time to stop laughing and start worrying!"'
L0B90:	db	00
L0B91:	db	'Weston joke'
L0B9C:	db	00
L0B9D:	db	'Weston'
L0BA3:	db	00
L0BA4:	db	'"Weston now sits in the castle prison, where he shall most c'
	db	'ertainly rot for the rest of his life. Heh-heh-heh! ~~"Try a'
	db	's I might, I cannot best that little jest!"'
L0C47:	db	00
L0C48:	db	'Weston'
L0C4E:	db	00
L0C4F:	db	'mage joke'
L0C58:	db	00
L0C59:	db	'"For a gold coin I will tell thee another. Dost thou wish to'
	db	' hear it?"'
L0C9F:	db	00
L0CA0:	db	'"Thou art wise. Thou shouldst save thy gold to pay a healer '
	db	'to cure that ache in thy side."'
L0CFB:	db	00
L0CFC:	db	'mage joke'
L0D05:	db	00
L0D06:	db	'"Whilst travelling on the road I came across a mage.~~"He lo'
	db	'oked as if he had not eaten for days and complained of a ter'
	db	'rible pain in his stomach.~~"So I told him his stomach was e'
	db	'mpty. If he put something in it he would feel better.~~"Late'
	db	'r he complained to me of a headache. I said his headache was'
	db	' caused by a similar	problem as his stomach.~~"No doubt it d'
	db	'id hurt him so because, being a mage, there was nothing left'
	db	' in it!"'
L0EB2:	db	00
L0EB3:	db	'mage joke'
L0EBC:	db	00
L0EBD:	db	'Sullivan joke'
L0ECA:	db	00
L0ECB:	db	'mages'
L0ED0:	db	00
L0ED1:	db	'"Now thou art playing a joke on me. Thou art broke!"'
L0F05:	db	00
L0F06:	db	'mage joke'
L0F0F:	db	00
L0F10:	db	'mages'
L0F15:	db	00
L0F16:	db	'"All of the mages have gone daft or mad! What other proper r'
	db	'esponse is there in a world that is so terrifically funny?!"'
L0F8E:	db	00
L0F8F:	db	'mages'
L0F94:	db	00
L0F95:	db	'Sullivan joke'
L0FA2:	db	00
L0FA3:	db	'"Thou art a brave Avatar! Dost thou wish to hear another?"'
L0FDD:	db	00
L0FDE:	db	'"Aha! Not as brave as I thought!"'
L0FFF:	db	00
L1000:	db	'joke five'
L1009:	db	00
L100A:	db	'"Didst thou knowest that the notorious Sullivan the Trickste'
	db	'r recently became a father?~~"It is true! They say the baby '
	db	'has his father's eyes and his mother's nose, but they made t'
	db	'he baby give them back."'
L10D6:	db	00
L10D7:	db	'Sullivan joke'
L10E4:	db	00
L10E5:	db	'gold joke'
L10EE:	db	00
L10EF:	db	'Sullivan'
L10F7:	db	00
L10F8:	db	'"Thou mayest be laughing but surely thy purse is not, for it'
	db	' is empty."'
L113F:	db	00
L1140:	db	'Sullivan'
L1148:	db	00
L1149:	db	'"Yes, I know the man they call Sullivan the Trickster! In fa'
	db	'ct thou dost remind me of him!~~"Or does he remind me of the'
	db	'e?~~"He is so tricky that just talking about him has caused '
	db	'me to trick myself! Heh-Hee-Haa!"'
L121E:	db	00
L121F:	db	'Sullivan'
L1227:	db	00
L1228:	db	'gold joke'
L1231:	db	00
L1232:	db	'"I have amused thee so far! Wouldst thou like to hear anothe'
	db	'r? It is a joke about gold!"'
L128A:	db	00
L128B:	db	'"Thank thee very much! Now, goodbye!"'
L12B0:	db	00
L12B1:	db	'"Dost thou get it? Ha! Ha! Ha! Ha! If not, it would be my pl'
	db	'easure to repeat it."'
L1302:	db	00
L1303:	db	'"Wouldst thou like to hear the gold joke again?"'
L1333:	db	00
L1334:	db	'"Now listen carefully..."'
L134D:	db	00
L134E:	db	'"Oh, I am so sorry. I cannot tell thee the joke again for th'
	db	'ou art out of money."'
L139F:	db	00
L13A0:	db	'"I see thou art becoming wise to the ways of show business, '
L13DC:	db	00
L13DD:	db	'. Good day to thee!"'
L13F1:	db	00
L13F2:	db	'"I can see thou art so poor that thou cannot even afford a s'
	db	'ense of humor!"'
L143D:	db	00
L143E:	db	'"Oh, it is a pity that thou dost not wish to hear it! It is '
	db	'the funniest one yet and my personal favorite!"'
L14A9:	db	00
L14AA:	db	'gold joke'
L14B3:	db	00
