		.data
L0000:	db	'Millie ignores your attempts to get her attention and goes b'
	db	'ack to intently watching the Fellowship ceremony.*'
L006E:	db	00
L006F:	db	'Millie looks perturbed. "Batlin has never missed a meeting b'
	db	'efore. What does he expect? Does he want -me- to run the mee'
	db	'ting?"'
L00ED:	db	00
L00EE:	db	'"Sorry, I cannot speak with thee now! I am late for the Fell'
	db	'owship meeting!"*'
L013B:	db	00
L013C:	db	'bye'
L013F:	db	00
L0140:	db	'job'
L0143:	db	00
L0144:	db	'name'
L0148:	db	00
L0149:	db	'Thad'
L014D:	db	00
L014E:	db	'You see a cute-looking woman who beams with a huge smile whe'
	db	'n she notices you looking at her.'
L01AB:	db	00
L01AC:	db	'"It is good to speak with thee, again," says Millie.'
L01E0:	db	00
L01E1:	db	'name'
L01E5:	db	00
L01E6:	db	'"My name is Millie," she giggles coyly.'
L020D:	db	00
L020E:	db	'name'
L0212:	db	00
L0213:	db	'job'
L0216:	db	00
L0217:	db	'"I suppose I have no job, but is that really so bad? I am a '
	db	'member of The Fellowship and I talk to people about them all'
	db	' day long."'
L029A:	db	00
L029B:	db	'talk'
L029F:	db	00
L02A0:	db	'Fellowship'
L02AA:	db	00
L02AB:	db	'Fellowship'
L02B5:	db	00
L02B6:	db	'"I see we have the same job!" She laughs at her own joke. "D'
	db	'ost thou spend all thy time talking to people about The Fell'
	db	'owship? For if that is what thou dost do, thou must get thys'
	db	'elf another corner!" Millie's face wrinkles in displeasure.'
L03A5:	db	00
L03A6:	db	'"Dost thou know what The Fellowship is?"'
L03CE:	db	00
L03CF:	db	'"Oh, I think thou dost not really know!"'
L03F7:	db	00
L03F8:	db	'Fellowship'
L0402:	db	00
L0403:	db	'philosophy'
L040D:	db	00
L040E:	db	'Fellowship'
L0418:	db	00
L0419:	db	'philosophy'
L0423:	db	00
L0424:	db	'philosophy'
L042E:	db	00
L042F:	db	'"If thou dost wish, thou mayest attend tonight's meeting at '
	db	'the Fellowship Hall. It begins at nine o'clock sharp. Just t'
	db	'ell them that thou art my guest. I shall see thee there, I h'
	db	'ope." Millie giggles and looks away shyly.'
L050D:	db	00
L050E:	db	'philosophy'
L0518:	db	00
L0519:	db	'talk'
L051D:	db	00
L051E:	db	'"I spend all my time trying to recruit, er... spread the wor'
	db	'd of The Fellowship. It is better than having a job! I learn'
	db	'ed how to do this at the Meditation Retreat."'
L05C3:	db	00
L05C4:	db	'talk'
L05C8:	db	00
L05C9:	db	'Meditation Retreat'
L05DB:	db	00
L05DC:	db	'Meditation Retreat'
L05EE:	db	00
L05EF:	db	'"'Tis located on an island in south Britannia near Serpent's'
	db	' Hold. Most new Fellowship members spend some time down ther'
	db	'e learning the tenets of the group. One can also learn to he'
	db	'ar 'the voice' at the retreat."'
L06C2:	db	00
L06C3:	db	'the voice'
L06CC:	db	00
L06CD:	db	'Meditation Retreat'
L06DF:	db	00
L06E0:	db	'the voice'
L06E9:	db	00
L06EA:	db	'"Fellowship members have an inner voice which speaks to them'
	db	'. I have not heard it yet, but I am working toward it. I may'
	db	' need to spend another few days at the Meditation Retreat in'
	db	' order to do so. Batlin tells me not to be discouraged, thou'
	db	'gh. He says I will hear it when I have made myself worthy."'
L0815:	db	00
L0816:	db	'the voice'
L081F:	db	00
L0820:	db	'Thad'
L0824:	db	00
L0825:	db	'Millie rolls her eyes. "Thou hast met my brother? Thou poor '
	db	'thing! He is really a candidate for the asylum, I wouldst sa'
	db	'y! He believes The Fellowship kidnapped me and charmed me in'
	db	'to following them. Well, I joined of mine own free will, wit'
	db	'hout a second thought, and it was a pure lark! No one coerce'
	db	'd me! Thad can go hang! Mama always said he was the impulsiv'
	db	'e one in the family!"'
L09A2:	db	00
L09A3:	db	'Thad'
L09A7:	db	00
L09A8:	db	'bye'
L09AB:	db	00
L09AC:	db	'"I shall see thee later! Maybe even at tonight's Fellowship '
	db	'meeting!"*'
L09F2:	db	00
L09F3:	db	'Fellowship meeting tonight!@'
L0A0F:	db	00
L0A10:	db	'@Strive For Unity!@'
L0A23:	db	00
L0A24:	db	'@Trust Thy Brother!@'
L0A38:	db	00
L0A39:	db	'@Worthiness Precedes Reward!@'
