L0000:	db	'bye'
L0003:	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
L0007:	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
L000C:	db	00
L000D:	db	'Nystul'
L0013:	db	00
L0014:	db	'You see your former companion and friend, Geoffrey, Captain '
	db	'of the Guard.'
L005D:	db	00
L005E:	db	'"Yes, '
L0064:	db	00
L0065:	db	'?" Geoffrey asks.'
L0076:	db	00
L0077:	db	'name'
L007B:	db	00
L007C:	db	'Geoffrey chuckles. "Art thou joking? I am Geoffrey!"'
L00B0:	db	00
L00B1:	db	'name'
L00B5:	db	00
L00B6:	db	'job'
L00B9:	db	00
L00BA:	db	'"These days I remain in my position as Captain of the Guard.'
	db	' I am Lord British's personal bodyguard, and I am in charge '
	db	'of security at the castle. I do not have much time or use fo'
	db	'r adventuring now."'
L0181:	db	00
L0182:	db	'adventuring'
L018D:	db	00
L018E:	db	'adventuring'
L0199:	db	00
L019A:	db	'"I have aged a bit over the last 200 years. I am afraid I sh'
	db	'all not be joining thee this time. But my thoughts are with '
	db	'thee, and if I may offer some assistance, I shall be glad to'
	db	' do so."'
L0256:	db	00
L0257:	db	'adventuring'
L0262:	db	00
L0263:	db	'assistance'
L026D:	db	00
L026E:	db	'aged'
L0272:	db	00
L0273:	db	'aged'
L0277:	db	00
L0278:	db	'"Yes, it has been a long time by Britannian reckoning since '
	db	'I have seen mine homeland. When thou hast finished with thy '
	db	'business, do come back and tell me news of what is happening'
	db	' in our homeworld."'
L033F:	db	00
L0340:	db	'aged'
L0344:	db	00
L0345:	db	'assistance'
L034F:	db	00
L0350:	db	'"Mine advice to thee is to build up thine experience and ski'
	db	'lls as soon as possible. Thou hast been away from Britannia '
	db	'for a long time. Thou mightest not be in the same shape thou'
	db	' wert in at the end of thy last adventure here."'
L0434:	db	00
L0435:	db	'assistance'
L043F:	db	00
L0440:	db	'shape'
L0445:	db	00
L0446:	db	'experience'
L0450:	db	00
L0451:	db	'shape'
L0456:	db	00
L0457:	db	'"It is apparently another difference in our two worlds. When'
	db	'ever thou shalt return it is as if thy physical body has arr'
	db	'ived here for the first time. It is the reason why many of	t'
	db	'hine own companions have chosen to stay here even though the'
	db	'y have aged in Britannian time."'
L0567:	db	00
L0568:	db	'shape'
L056D:	db	00
L056E:	db	'experience'
L0578:	db	00
L0579:	db	'"Go and search for monsters. Vanquish them. Take their gold!'
	db	' Gain experience! Use that experience when thou dost visit t'
	db	'rainers. Increase thy strength, dexterity, and intelligence,'
	db	' as well as thy combat skill and ability to perform magic. T'
	db	'hou wilt be lost without this necessary evolution of experie'
	db	'nce!"'
L06AA:	db	00
L06AB:	db	'experience'
L06B5:	db	00
L06B6:	db	'Nystul'
L06BC:	db	00
L06BD:	db	'"He is quite looney. If thou dost ask me, I believe all the '
	db	'mages in the land are afflicted. Take a look and find out fo'
	db	'r thyself."'
L0740:	db	00
L0741:	db	'"He is much better now!"'
L0759:	db	00
L075A:	db	'Nystul'
L0760:	db	00
L0761:	db	'bye'
L0764:	db	00
L0765:	db	'"Have courage. Have faith. Be strong. Be wise."*'
L0795:	db	00
