		.data
L0000:	db	'bye'
L0003:	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
L0007:	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
L000C:	db	00
L000D:	db	'Nell'
L0011:	db	00
L0012:	db	'Jeanette'
L001A:	db	00
L001B:	db	'Thou art in luck'
L002B:	db	00
L002C:	db	'You see a young peasant with a tray of wine glasses.'
L0060:	db	00
L0061:	db	'"Hello, Avatar."'
L0071:	db	00
L0072:	db	'name'
L0076:	db	00
L0077:	db	'"I am Charles."'
L0086:	db	00
L0087:	db	'name'
L008B:	db	00
L008C:	db	'job'
L008F:	db	00
L0090:	db	'"I am a servant in Lord British's castle. I serve as a gentl'
	db	'eman's gentleman, among other things. Right now I am serving'
	db	' wine."'
L010F:	db	00
L0110:	db	'wine'
L0114:	db	00
L0115:	db	'servant'
L011C:	db	00
L011D:	db	'servant'
L0124:	db	00
L0125:	db	'"My family has been employed by Lord British for many years.'
	db	' My father, Bennie, once held the position I now hold. He is'
	db	' the head servant. I shall be head servant one day, I suppos'
	db	'e. Then perhaps my sweetheart will love me."'
L0205:	db	00
L0206:	db	'servant'
L020D:	db	00
L020E:	db	'sweetheart'
L0218:	db	00
L0219:	db	'family'
L021F:	db	00
L0220:	db	'family'
L0226:	db	00
L0227:	db	'"Thou wilt encounter them. My mother cooks in the kitchen. M'
	db	'y prudish sister is the chambermaid."'
L0288:	db	00
L0289:	db	'family'
L028F:	db	00
L0290:	db	'sweetheart'
L029A:	db	00
L029B:	db	'Charles sighs. He is clearly smitten. "She is Jeanette. She '
	db	'works in the Blue Boar. But I am afraid I am not 'up to her '
	db	'standards'. I believe she has her eye set on someone else. I'
	db	' do not know what to do about it."'
L0371:	db	00
L0372:	db	'sweetheart'
L037C:	db	00
L037D:	db	'Jeanette'
L0385:	db	00
L0386:	db	'Jeanette'
L038E:	db	00
L038F:	db	'"She does not love me, I know. She would rather marry a rich'
	db	' man. I have not a chance."'
L03E6:	db	00
L03E7:	db	'Jeanette'
L03EF:	db	00
L03F0:	db	'Thou art in luck'
L0400:	db	00
L0401:	db	'You tell Charles what Jeanette said.'
L0425:	db	00
L0426:	db	'"Really? Thou dost mean I have a chance?" Charles becomes so'
	db	' excited he nearly drops his tray. "Oh, I thank thee, Avatar'
	db	', for giving me this hopeful news! I must run and send her f'
	db	'lowers or some gift! I must declare my love!" He turns away '
	db	'from you, obviously walking on clouds.*'
L053D:	db	00
L053E:	db	'Nell'
L0542:	db	00
L0543:	db	'"She is engaged to the carousel manager. It is hard to get u'
	db	'sed to. I have always been overly protective of my little si'
	db	'ster. I would wager she has never even been kissed! Not even'
	db	' by Carrocio! That is mainly because I have looked after her'
	db	' all this time. I would smite anyone who laid a hand on her!'
	db	' Besides, Nell has always been chaste and prudish. She would'
	db	' never think to allow a man to kiss her."'
L06D4:	db	00
L06D5:	db	'Nell'
L06D9:	db	00
L06DA:	db	'child'
L06DF:	db	00
L06E0:	db	'child'
L06E5:	db	00
L06E6:	db	'You remember what Nell told you about her 'condition'. Do yo'
	db	'u mention it to Charles?'
L073A:	db	00
L073B:	db	'You tell Charles what Nell revealed in confidence.'
L076D:	db	00
L076E:	db	'Charles is wide-eyed and shocked. "Why, that hussy! My siste'
	db	'r! She is nothing more than a tramp! And wait until I get mi'
	db	'ne hands on Carrocio!"'
L07FC:	db	00
L07FD:	db	'Charles turns away. There is murder in his eyes.*'
L082E:	db	00
L082F:	db	'Your conscience rests easy, knowing that you resisted the te'
	db	'mptation to carry tales.'
L0883:	db	00
L0884:	db	'child'
L0889:	db	00
L088A:	db	'wine'
L088E:	db	00
L088F:	db	'"Wouldst thou like some wine?"'
L08AD:	db	00
L08AE:	db	'"'Tis on the house." Charles hands you and your friends glas'
	db	'ses of wine.'
L08F6:	db	00
L08F7:	db	'"Oops. Thou art carrying too much. Ask me again when thou do'
	db	'st not have thine hands full!"'
L0951:	db	00
L0952:	db	'"Some other time, then."'
L096A:	db	00
L096B:	db	'wine'
L096F:	db	00
L0970:	db	'bye'
L0973:	db	00
L0974:	db	'Charles nods his head at you, then goes about his business.*'
L09B0:	db	00
