L001E:	db	'Ariana'
L0024:	db	00
L0025:	db	'News of your father'
L0038:	db	00
L0039:	db	'kiss'
L003D:	db	00
L003E:	db	'This is an attractive young woman who seems sad.'
L006E:	db	00
L006F:	db	'Emotion immediately grips your heart to see such a beautiful'
	db	' young woman seem so sad.'
L00C4:	db	00
L00C5:	db	'She looks up as you introduce yourself.'
L00EC:	db	00
L00ED:	db	'"Hello again, '
L00FB:	db	00
L00FC:	db	'!" Nastassia says.'
L010E:	db	00
L010F:	db	'name'
L0113:	db	00
L0114:	db	'"I am Nastassia."'
L0125:	db	00
L0126:	db	'name'
L012A:	db	00
L012B:	db	'job'
L012E:	db	00
L012F:	db	'She thinks a moment. "I suppose my job is to keep the Shrine'
	db	' of Compassion pristine, though it is not an official positi'
	db	'on."'
L01AB:	db	00
L01AC:	db	'Shrine'
L01B2:	db	00
L01B3:	db	'Shrine'
L01B9:	db	00
L01BA:	db	'"The Shrine of Compassion has been here for many generations'
	db	', as have all the shrines in Britannia. My great-great-grand'
	db	'mother Ariana made a request in her will that her family lin'
	db	'e take care of this particular shrine."'
L0295:	db	00
L0296:	db	'take care'
L029F:	db	00
L02A0:	db	'all shrines'
L02AB:	db	00
L02AC:	db	'Shrine'
L02B2:	db	00
L02B3:	db	'all shrines'
L02BE:	db	00
L02BF:	db	'"Many of the shrines have fallen into disuse or have been ov'
	db	'ergrown to the point of being lost. It is sad."'
L032A:	db	00
L032B:	db	'all shrines'
L0336:	db	00
L0337:	db	'take care'
L0340:	db	00
L0341:	db	'"I am afraid that thou mightest find the other shrines in po'
	db	'or condition. I keep this one... well, nice. And I do it not'
	db	' only to keep alive my great-great-grandmother's tradition, '
	db	'but... for other reasons, too."'
L0414:	db	00
L0415:	db	'take care'
L041E:	db	00
L041F:	db	'reasons'
L0426:	db	00
L0427:	db	'tradition'
L0430:	db	00
L0431:	db	'tradition'
L043A:	db	00
L043B:	db	'"Some people may think it odd that a young person would clin'
	db	'g to the old ways so. But it is something that gives me grea'
	db	't comfort. It gives me the feeling that there is something i'
	db	'n this world that I belong to."'
L050E:	db	00
L050F:	db	'tradition'
L0518:	db	00
L0519:	db	'reasons'
L0520:	db	00
L0521:	db	'"I... I'd rather not say. Please do not ask."'
L054E:	db	00
L054F:	db	'"Thou dost know the reasons."'
L056C:	db	00
L056D:	db	'reasons'
L0574:	db	00
L0575:	db	'Ariana'
L057B:	db	00
L057C:	db	'she'
L057F:	db	00
L0580:	db	'he'
L0582:	db	00
L0583:	db	'"Yes, she was my great-great-grandmother. I understand that '
	db	'she actually met the Avatar and '
L05DF:	db	00
L05E0:	db	' made a profound impact on her life.~~"It is odd, but thou d'
	db	'ost resemble the portraits I have seen of the Avatar."'
L0652:	db	00
L0653:	db	'Ariana'
L0659:	db	00
L065A:	db	'I am the Avatar'
L0669:	db	00
L066A:	db	'Julius'
L0670:	db	00
L0671:	db	'"Thou dost know of my father? I suppose the townsfolk have b'
	db	'een talking again. I wish I had known him. There is somethin'
	db	'g within me that yearns for some news of him. Anything at al'
	db	'l."'
L0728:	db	00
L0729:	db	'Julius'
L072F:	db	00
L0730:	db	'Nadia'
L0735:	db	00
L0736:	db	'"My mother. She died horribly, and by her own hand. That is '
	db	'the true reason I pay homage to this Shrine. I hope someday '
	db	'to provide her with the means to rest in peace."'
L07DE:	db	00
L07DF:	db	'Nadia'
L07E4:	db	00
L07E5:	db	'Yew'
L07E8:	db	00
L07E9:	db	'"My father died in the Great Forest there. Some wild animal '
	db	'or something killed him. Art thou perhaps travelling to Yew?'
	db	'"'
L0862:	db	00
L0863:	db	'"Oh, '
L0868:	db	00
L0869:	db	', I do wish thou wouldst try to find out something about my '
	db	'father. How did he die? What happened? Please! Wilt thou sea'
	db	'rch for the truth and come back and tell me?"'
L090E:	db	00
L090F:	db	'"Bless thee! I shall be waiting here for thee."'
L093E:	db	00
L093F:	db	'"I know we have a strong kinship now. We shall be like siste'
	db	'rs."'
L097F:	db	00
L0980:	db	'Unexpectedly, Nastassia pulls your head down to hers and kis'
	db	'ses you on the mouth.'
L09D1:	db	00
L09D2:	db	'kiss'
L09D6:	db	00
L09D7:	db	'Nastassia turns away and looks as if she might cry. "Very we'
	db	'll. Please leave me alone."*'
L0A2F:	db	00
L0A30:	db	'"No? Well, let me know if thou art in the future. Perhaps th'
	db	'ou couldst help me."'
L0A80:	db	00
L0A81:	db	'Yew'
L0A84:	db	00
L0A85:	db	'kiss'
L0A89:	db	00
L0A8A:	db	'You kiss Nastassia and she moans.'
L0AAB:	db	00
L0AAC:	db	'The two of you rush into each other's arms and your mouths m'
	db	'eet. You had forgotten how good her lips felt against yours.'
L0B24:	db	00
L0B25:	db	'You kiss Nastassia's lovely mouth again. She responds.~~"No '
	db	'man hath done that as well as thee."~~ She looks at you with'
	db	' wide eyes.~~"Do it again, milord."'
L0BC0:	db	00
L0BC1:	db	'kiss'
L0BC5:	db	00
L0BC6:	db	'kiss again'
L0BD0:	db	00
L0BD1:	db	'kiss again'
L0BDB:	db	00
L0BDC:	db	'You kiss Nastassia yet again. This time your bodies press to'
	db	'gether tightly, and you know this promises to be more than a'
	db	' fleeting fling with some tavern wench.'
L0C7B:	db	00
L0C7C:	db	'You kiss Nastassia and she moans.'
L0C9D:	db	00
L0C9E:	db	'I am the Avatar'
L0CAD:	db	00
L0CAE:	db	'Nastassia studies your features.~~"Somehow I knew it. It hat'
	db	'h been said that thou wouldst return."'
L0D10:	db	00
L0D11:	db	'I am the Avatar'
L0D20:	db	00
L0D21:	db	'News of your father'
L0D34:	db	00
L0D35:	db	'You tell Nastassia what you learned from Trellek. She closes'
	db	' her eyes and it seems a great weight has lifted from her sh'
	db	'oulders.~~The woman raises her arms to the sky and cries out'
	db	', "Didst thou hear that, mother? Thine husband was only tryi'
	db	'ng to provide for his family! And he died... a hero! He was '
	db	'not a vagabond! Dost thou hear? Thou canst rest thy tortured'
	db	' soul now. Please, mother, forgive him. Do so, so that I can'
	db	' now forgive thee."~~She wipes the tears from her face and l'
	db	'ooks at you.'
L0F21:	db	00
L0F22:	db	'"I thank thee, '
L0F31:	db	00
L0F32:	db	'. Thou hast made me very happy. I shall always remember thee'
	db	'."'
L0F70:	db	00
L0F71:	db	'She kisses you once lightly. "Thank thee, '
L0F9B:	db	00
L0F9C:	db	'. Thou hast made me very happy. Shouldst thou become weary o'
	db	'f adventuring, I shall be waiting here for thee. Thou art we'
	db	'lcome to live and share thy life with me. Go now. Finish the'
	db	' job thou must needs do. But keep me in thy thoughts."'
L1086:	db	00
L1087:	db	'News of your father'
L109A:	db	00
L109B:	db	'bye'
L109E:	db	00
L109F:	db	'"Goodbye." She kisses you again, and then turns so that she '
	db	'will not see you leave.*'
L10F3:	db	00
L10F4:	db	'"Goodbye, '
L10FE:	db	00
L10FF:	db	'."*'
L1102:	db	00
L1103:	db	'"Goodbye, '
L110D:	db	00
L110E:	db	'."*'
