		.data
L0000:	db	'You see a cheerful woman with bright eyes and blonde hair.'
L003A:	db	00
L003B:	db	'"Hello again, '
L0049:	db	00
L004A:	db	'." says Xanthia.'
L005A:	db	00
L005B:	db	'bye'
L005E:	db	00
L005F:	db	'job'
L0062:	db	00
L0063:	db	'name'
L0067:	db	00
L0068:	db	'name'
L006C:	db	00
L006D:	db	'"Hello, my name is Xanthia."'
L0089:	db	00
L008A:	db	'name'
L008E:	db	00
L008F:	db	'job'
L0092:	db	00
L0093:	db	'"I am a member of the Artist's Guild in Minoc. I make and se'
	db	'll candelabras."'
L00DF:	db	00
L00E0:	db	'candelabras'
L00EB:	db	00
L00EC:	db	'Minoc'
L00F1:	db	00
L00F2:	db	'Artist's Guild'
L0100:	db	00
L0101:	db	'"If thou wouldst not mind, we can perhaps get to know each o'
	db	'ther during a more sociable occasion! Two people have been r'
	db	'ecently murdered over at William's sawmill! This is hardly t'
	db	'he time to get to know someone!"'
L01D5:	db	00
L01D6:	db	'murders'
L01DD:	db	00
L01DE:	db	'Artist's Guild'
L01EC:	db	00
L01ED:	db	'"We are a guild of artists and craftspeople united for the c'
	db	'ommon good and dedicated to the advancement of the arts, as '
	db	'well as showing other artists that it is possible to exist s'
	db	'olely by thine own efforts without sacrificing thy creativit'
	db	'y."'
L02E0:	db	00
L02E1:	db	'Artist's Guild'
L02EF:	db	00
L02F0:	db	'candelabras'
L02FB:	db	00
L02FC:	db	'"I make simple candelabras, but sometimes I will do commissi'
	db	'oned work, making more specific ones. I was hired by The Fel'
	db	'lowship to make the candelabras for all of their Fellowship '
	db	'halls."'
L03B7:	db	00
L03B8:	db	'candelabras'
L03C3:	db	00
L03C4:	db	'Fellowship'
L03CE:	db	00
L03CF:	db	'Fellowship'
L03D9:	db	00
L03DA:	db	'"Elynor, the head of the local Fellowship branch, showed me '
	db	'a picture of the Fellowship symbol and I based the design fo'
	db	'r my candelabra on that."'
L046B:	db	00
L046C:	db	'Fellowship'
L0476:	db	00
L0477:	db	'Elynor'
L047D:	db	00
L047E:	db	'candelabra at murder site'
L0497:	db	00
L0498:	db	'Elynor'
L049E:	db	00
L049F:	db	'"Yes, she's quite a recruiter. Why, she got Burnside, our Ma'
	db	'yor, to join, as well as Gregor, the local head of the Brita'
	db	'nnian Mining Company, and Owen, our shipwright. He is soon t'
	db	'o be famous, I am sorry to say. She has never asked me to jo'
	db	'in, thank goodness."'
L05A3:	db	00
L05A4:	db	'Elynor'
L05AA:	db	00
L05AB:	db	'Owen'
L05AF:	db	00
L05B0:	db	'candelabra at murder site'
L05C9:	db	00
L05CA:	db	'You describe the candelabra found at the murder scene to Xan'
	db	'thia. Her eyes widen with recognition. "Yes, that is one of '
	db	'the candelabras I made. 'Twas in the sawmill at the murder s'
	db	'ite?"'
L0683:	db	00
L0684:	db	'Xanthia looks shocked. "How horrible! I swear I do not know '
	db	'how it could have gotten there! Thou shouldst certainly ask '
	db	'Elynor about it!"'
L070D:	db	00
L070E:	db	'She gives you a slightly cross look. "Well, I hope that thou'
	db	' didst not steal it from Elynor."'
L076B:	db	00
L076C:	db	'candelabra at murder site'
L0785:	db	00
L0786:	db	'Minoc'
L078B:	db	00
L078C:	db	'"With the success of the mine, Minoc is a prosperous city. N'
	db	'ot a place where one is used to having murders happen. A goo'
	db	'd place for our Artist's Guild to do well. But things have a'
	db	'lways been hard for us here. Now I fear they may get worse."'
L087C:	db	00
L087D:	db	'Minoc'
L0882:	db	00
L0883:	db	'murders'
L088A:	db	00
L088B:	db	'worse'
L0890:	db	00
L0891:	db	'worse'
L0896:	db	00
L0897:	db	'"That is what Gladstone says. Thou hadst better ask him abou'
	db	't it."'
L08D9:	db	00
L08DA:	db	'worse'
L08DF:	db	00
L08E0:	db	'murders'
L08E7:	db	00
L08E8:	db	'"It is so terrible! I never knew Frederico or Tania personal'
	db	'ly, but I did meet their son, Sasha, once. He was a nice boy'
	db	', if somewhat misguided. He spent the night with us once at '
	db	'the Artist's Guild, as a guest of Seara."'
L09C5:	db	00
L09C6:	db	'murders'
L09CD:	db	00
L09CE:	db	'Owen'
L09D2:	db	00
L09D3:	db	'"They are to build a monument to Owen for some reason or ano'
	db	'ther. Owen and Elynor refuse to use anyone from the Guild to'
	db	' help build it! Rather rude of them, dost thou not think?"'
L0A85:	db	00
L0A86:	db	'Owen'
L0A8A:	db	00
L0A8B:	db	'bye'
L0A8E:	db	00
L0A8F:	db	'"Farewell, '
L0A9A:	db	00
L0A9B:	db	'. I hope I was of some assistance to thee."*'
L0AC7:	db	00
