		.data
L0000:	db	'Owen will not interrupt his participation in The Fellowship '
	db	'meeting to talk with you.*'
L0056:	db	00
L0057:	db	'"I am late for The Fellowship Meeting! I cannot speak with t'
	db	'hee now!"*'
L009D:	db	00
L009E:	db	'bye'
L00A1:	db	00
L00A2:	db	'job'
L00A5:	db	00
L00A6:	db	'name'
L00AA:	db	00
L00AB:	db	'Hook'
L00AF:	db	00
L00B0:	db	'Crown Jewel'
L00BB:	db	00
L00BC:	db	'ship'
L00C0:	db	00
L00C1:	db	'statue is cancelled'
L00D4:	db	00
L00D5:	db	'You see a young man dressed in an expensive tunic. He is ver'
	db	'y serious.'
L011B:	db	00
L011C:	db	'Owen looks at you and sniffs. "It would appear thou dost wis'
	db	'h to speak with me again."'
L0172:	db	00
L0173:	db	'name'
L0177:	db	00
L0178:	db	'"My name, '
L0182:	db	00
L0183:	db	', is Owen. It is a name I suspect thou shalt be hearing more'
	db	' of in the future."'
L01D2:	db	00
L01D3:	db	'name'
L01D7:	db	00
L01D8:	db	'statue is cancelled'
L01EB:	db	00
L01EC:	db	'job'
L01EF:	db	00
L01F0:	db	'He looks you in the eye and speaks without the slightest tra'
	db	'ce of modesty. "I am," he says, "the greatest shipwright in '
	db	'the history of Minoc. I am the greatest shipwright who has e'
	db	'ver lived!"'
L02AF:	db	00
L02B0:	db	'buy'
L02B3:	db	00
L02B4:	db	'Minoc'
L02B9:	db	00
L02BA:	db	'greatest'
L02C2:	db	00
L02C3:	db	'Hook'
L02C7:	db	00
L02C8:	db	'Crown Jewel'
L02D3:	db	00
L02D4:	db	'"After years of breaking my back trying to make something of'
	db	' this ungrateful little town, I'm giving up. I swear I will '
	db	'never build another ship as long as I live. That will teach '
	db	'them! No matter how they may beg or plead, I will not do it.'
	db	'"'
L03C5:	db	00
L03C6:	db	'ungrateful'
L03D0:	db	00
L03D1:	db	'statue is cancelled'
L03E4:	db	00
L03E5:	db	'"Well, I shall certainly forgive thy poor manners for I know'
	db	' how privileged thou must feel for meeting me, but thou must'
	db	' know that two people have just been discovered in the sawmi'
	db	'll, having been murdered!"'
L04B3:	db	00
L04B4:	db	'murders'
L04BB:	db	00
L04BC:	db	'greatest'
L04C4:	db	00
L04C5:	db	'"And dost thou know how I became that way? I shall tell thee'
	db	'! I started to hear a voice in mine head! Oh, I know that th'
	db	'ou shalt think me mad..."'
L0556:	db	00
L0557:	db	'greatest'
L055F:	db	00
L0560:	db	'voices'
L0566:	db	00
L0567:	db	'mad'
L056A:	db	00
L056B:	db	'voices'
L0571:	db	00
L0572:	db	'"These were not the voices of anyone I have ever known. But '
	db	'still these voices had a profound effect on me..."'
L05E0:	db	00
L05E1:	db	'voices'
L05E7:	db	00
L05E8:	db	'mad'
L05EB:	db	00
L05EC:	db	'"After searching for a meaning to this voice - which proved '
	db	'difficult, for how dost thou tell someone, especially a stra'
	db	'nger, that thou art hearing a voice in thine head - I came a'
	db	'cross The Fellowship. They taught me what the voice was."'
L06D9:	db	00
L06DA:	db	'mad'
L06DD:	db	00
L06DE:	db	'Fellowship'
L06E8:	db	00
L06E9:	db	'voice'
L06EE:	db	00
L06EF:	db	'voice'
L06F4:	db	00
L06F5:	db	'"This was the voice of reason within mine own mind which sou'
	db	'ght to guide my life in its proper direction. The Fellowship'
	db	' taught me how to trust this voice and heed what it says. An'
	db	'd thou canst see the results in mine own life! I have master'
	db	'ed my craft and advanced the techniques of ship-building thr'
	db	'ough the methods I have devised."'
L0842:	db	00
L0843:	db	'voice'
L0848:	db	00
L0849:	db	'methods'
L0850:	db	00
L0851:	db	'buy'
L0854:	db	00
L0855:	db	'Owen looks at you and suddenly seems flustered. "Uh, I have '
	db	'no ships for sale presently. I have been working on a few im'
	db	'provements. But if thou wouldst, thou couldst commission me '
	db	'to build one for thee. A deed to one of the ships I build co'
	db	'sts 1000 gold coins. Dost thou wish to buy one?"'
L0975:	db	00
L0976:	db	'"'Tis money well spent, thou shalt see! I shall begin work i'
	db	'mmediately. I will be building based upon some of my more re'
	db	'cent designs. I shall give thee thy ship's deed in advance"'
L0A29:	db	00
L0A2A:	db	'"It will be called the Excellencia."'
L0A4E:	db	00
L0A4F:	db	'"I would give thee thy deed but thou art carrying too much."'
L0A8B:	db	00
L0A8C:	db	'"Take thy gold back! I cannot in good conscious keep it!"'
L0AC5:	db	00
L0AC6:	db	'"I would give thee thy gold back but I seem to have misplace'
	db	'd it."'
L0B08:	db	00
L0B09:	db	'"I am dreadfully sorry," he sniffs, "but thou dost not have '
	db	'enough gold."'
L0B52:	db	00
L0B53:	db	'"Art thou certain? Thou shalt find no better ships in all of'
	db	' Britannia! Very well, then!"'
L0BAC:	db	00
L0BAD:	db	'"Wouldst thou perhaps be interested in purchasing a fine sex'
	db	'tant? I have one which I would be willing to part with for a'
	db	' fine bargain. The price is 150 gold. Art thou interested?"'
L0C60:	db	00
L0C61:	db	'"Excellent! I knew that thou wouldst appreciate owning the s'
	db	'extant of Owen the shipwright. Thou art a fine person, able '
	db	'to discern those quality items which are worth a bit of extr'
	db	'a coin."'
L0D1D:	db	00
L0D1E:	db	'"Thou knave! To get mine hopes up so, only to cruelly dash t'
	db	'hem. Thou dost not possess enough gold to buy my treasure. I'
	db	'f thou dost return with more coinage, PERHAPS I will allow t'
	db	'hee to bid on it again."'
L0DEA:	db	00
L0DEB:	db	'"Thou dost not have enough strength to add my treasure to th'
	db	'y pack. Thou must dispose of some of thy worthless dross to '
	db	'make room for this beauty. I will await thy return to purcha'
	db	'se the sextant at this fine, low price."'
L0EC7:	db	00
L0EC8:	db	'"Hmph. Well, let it be known that thou didst pass up the cha'
	db	'nce to buy the sextant of the famous Owen the shipwright, an'
	db	'd thou shalt be known for the knave and simpleton that thou '
	db	'art."'
L0F81:	db	00
L0F82:	db	'"Mine establishment is presently closed. I do not wish to di'
	db	'scuss business at this time."'
L0FDB:	db	00
L0FDC:	db	'buy'
L0FDF:	db	00
L0FE0:	db	'methods'
L0FE7:	db	00
L0FE8:	db	'"I have even written a book describing the advances I have m'
	db	'ade in the methods of ship-building. It is very advanced but'
	db	' I have tried to write it so that it is accessible to the la'
	db	'yman. Wouldst thou be interested in purchasing a copy?"'
L10D3:	db	00
L10D4:	db	'"Yes, of course thou wouldst."'
L10F2:	db	00
L10F3:	db	'"Here it is."'
L1100:	db	00
L1101:	db	'"Thou art carrying too much to take thy book."'
L112F:	db	00
L1130:	db	'"I shall return thy money."'
L114B:	db	00
L114C:	db	'"I wouldst give thee back thy gold but thou cannot take it."'
L1188:	db	00
L1189:	db	'"Thou dost not have enough money!"'
L11AB:	db	00
L11AC:	db	'"Hmph! I suppose that it would be beyond thy comprehension, '
	db	'anyway."'
L11F0:	db	00
L11F1:	db	'methods'
L11F8:	db	00
L11F9:	db	'ship'
L11FD:	db	00
L11FE:	db	'"I can well understand thine impatience but I have just begu'
	db	'n work on it. It shall be ready when I am finished with it. '
	db	'Now, until such time, I would appreciate it if thou wouldst '
	db	'not waste my valuable time."*'
L12CF:	db	00
L12D0:	db	'"I cannot build thee a ship as I suspect we both know."'
L1307:	db	00
L1308:	db	'"Nor can I take thy money for one. Here, I shall return it t'
	db	'o thee."'
L134C:	db	00
L134D:	db	'"Oh, my, thou art too encumbered to take back thy 1000 gold '
	db	'coins! Come back when thine hands are less full!"'
L13BA:	db	00
L13BB:	db	'"I cannot help thee with that."'
L13DA:	db	00
L13DB:	db	'ship'
L13DF:	db	00
L13E0:	db	'Minoc'
L13E5:	db	00
L13E6:	db	'"Despite all this business with murders, I must confess that'
	db	' I love it here. This is the place where I was born. They lo'
	db	've me. They are going to be building a monument here in mine'
	db	' honor. I suppose I have been worthy of it, but still I can''
	db	't help but be flattered."'
L14EF:	db	00
L14F0:	db	'monument'
L14F8:	db	00
L14F9:	db	'murders'
L1500:	db	00
L1501:	db	'Minoc'
L1506:	db	00
L1507:	db	'ungrateful'
L1511:	db	00
L1512:	db	'"Apparently, building the greatest ships to ever set sail in'
	db	' history and all that that has done for Minoc are no longer '
	db	'enough! No! Thanks to that pompous idiot of a mayor I am den'
	db	'ied the rightful tribute of which I have proven myself more '
	db	'than worthy. Design flaws, bah! How many ships has Mayor Bur'
	db	'nside built in his miserable little life?!"'
L1669:	db	00
L166A:	db	'there were deaths'
L167B:	db	00
L167C:	db	'ungrateful'
L1686:	db	00
L1687:	db	'murders'
L168E:	db	00
L168F:	db	'"That is right. The sawmill is located southeast of town. Al'
	db	'most everyone in town is down there. Thou shouldst probably '
	db	'go down there if thou dost want to find out more. I abhor vi'
	db	'olence."'
L174B:	db	00
L174C:	db	'He shakes his head slowly. "They are going to be unveiling m'
	db	'y monument sometime in the near future. Dost thou think that'
	db	' talk of these events will keep people away from the ceremon'
	db	'y? That would be a tragedy!"'
L181C:	db	00
L181D:	db	'murders'
L1824:	db	00
L1825:	db	'there were deaths'
L1836:	db	00
L1837:	db	'You tell him about the many innocent civilians who lost thei'
	db	'r lives on the ship he built. Owen shakes his head slowly. "'
	db	'I do not know. I have no idea how it could have happened. It'
	db	' is difficult to conceive of the pain such great loss of lif'
	db	'e brings into this world. But I did my best when I built tho'
	db	'se ships. I did not want those men to die. Thou must believe'
	db	' me."'
L19A4:	db	00
L19A5:	db	'Owen appears distressed. "The tribute to me is now no more t'
	db	'han a tombstone."'
L19F2:	db	00
L19F3:	db	'there were deaths'
L1A04:	db	00
L1A05:	db	'tribute'
L1A0C:	db	00
L1A0D:	db	'Fellowship'
L1A17:	db	00
L1A18:	db	'"The changes it has made in my personal life have helped me '
	db	'tremendously."'
L1A62:	db	00
L1A63:	db	'personal life'
L1A70:	db	00
L1A71:	db	'"Thou canst ask Elynor all about it unless she is not speaki'
	db	'ng to thee either. Perhaps the details of thy personal life '
	db	'will amuse her more than do mine."'
L1B0B:	db	00
L1B0C:	db	'personal life'
L1B19:	db	00
L1B1A:	db	'Fellowship'
L1B24:	db	00
L1B25:	db	'philosophy'
L1B2F:	db	00
L1B30:	db	'philosophy'
L1B3A:	db	00
L1B3B:	db	'personal life'
L1B48:	db	00
L1B49:	db	'"My friend, there was a time when I thought that my life was'
	db	' at its end. I felt as though I had been swallowed into a co'
	db	'ld, deep hole of darkness."'
L1BDC:	db	00
L1BDD:	db	'darkness'
L1BE5:	db	00
L1BE6:	db	'personal life'
L1BF3:	db	00
L1BF4:	db	'darkness'
L1BFC:	db	00
L1BFD:	db	'"My very soul felt as though it had sunk into a place into w'
	db	'hich no light could enter... Soon after I discovered The Fel'
	db	'lowship. The difference that it made in my life was miraculo'
	db	'us."'
L1CB5:	db	00
L1CB6:	db	'"I have been having a difficult time lately trying to speak '
	db	'to Elynor. It seems that she has no time for me. Back when I'
	db	' was making preparations for the monument she was always sto'
	db	'pping by and willing to have words with me."'
L1D96:	db	00
L1D97:	db	'darkness'
L1D9F:	db	00
L1DA0:	db	'monument'
L1DA8:	db	00
L1DA9:	db	'"Oh, thou canst ask anyone in town about it. They all know."'
L1DE5:	db	00
L1DE6:	db	'monument'
L1DEE:	db	00
L1DEF:	db	'tribute'
L1DF6:	db	00
L1DF7:	db	'"I know! My work will stand as my monument! My name will end'
	db	'ure long after any statue has worn away to dust! People will'
	db	' remember -me-, I promise thee that!"'
L1E94:	db	00
L1E95:	db	'And, with a dramatic flourish, Owen produces a dagger. Befor'
	db	'e you can stop him, he plunges it into his chest. He coughs '
	db	'loudly as blood spurts from his mouth, soaking his fine line'
	db	'n tunic in wine-red guilt. After a moment, it is all over. O'
	db	'wen, the greatest shipwright who ever lived, is dead.*'
L1FBB:	db	00
L1FBC:	db	'Crown Jewel'
L1FC7:	db	00
L1FC8:	db	'"The Crown Jewel was in town and left early this morning. It'
	db	' was scheduled to sail for Paws."'
L2025:	db	00
L2026:	db	'"I have heard nothing more of the Crown Jewel since we last '
	db	'spoke of it, '
L206F:	db	00
L2070:	db	'."'
L2072:	db	00
L2073:	db	'Crown Jewel'
L207E:	db	00
L207F:	db	'Hook'
L2083:	db	00
L2084:	db	'"I saw a man with a hook for a hand wandering around town la'
	db	'st night."'
L20CA:	db	00
L20CB:	db	'"I have heard nothing more of this man Hook since we last sp'
	db	'oke of him, '
L2113:	db	00
L2114:	db	'."'
L2116:	db	00
L2117:	db	'Hook'
L211B:	db	00
L211C:	db	'bye'
L211F:	db	00
L2120:	db	'"Tired of benefitting from my presence? Very well. I shall s'
	db	'ee thee again, I hope!"*'
L2174:	db	00
L2175:	db	'"Be on thy way, then. Time is fleeting, as is fame."*'
