		.data
L0000:	db	'bye'
L0003:	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
L0007:	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
L000C:	db	00
L000D:	db	'murders'
L0014:	db	00
L0015:	db	'Crown Jewel'
L0020:	db	00
L0021:	db	'Hook'
L0025:	db	00
L0026:	db	'You see a weary-looking man who is missing his right arm. Wi'
	db	'th his one hand he scratches his head and squints in your ge'
	db	'neral direction.'
L00AE:	db	00
L00AF:	db	'"Oy, how ye been, '
L00C1:	db	00
L00C2:	db	'?" Rutherford calls out to you.'
L00E1:	db	00
L00E2:	db	'name'
L00E6:	db	00
L00E7:	db	'He lets out a sharp cough to clear his throat. "Rutherford's'
	db	' me name. Pleased ta meet 'chur."~~ He extends his greasy ha'
	db	'nd for you to shake and does not retract it until it is clas'
	db	'ped.'
L019F:	db	00
L01A0:	db	'name'
L01A4:	db	00
L01A5:	db	'job'
L01A8:	db	00
L01A9:	db	'"Why I be the barkeep of The Checquered Cork. No better plac'
	db	'e in Minoc to discuss the events of the day."'
L0212:	db	00
L0213:	db	'He coughs into the rag he had just been using to polish the '
	db	'bar.'
L0253:	db	00
L0254:	db	'"Hello again, Sir Dupre! Didst thou enjoy mine establishment'
	db	' so much that thou hast returned?"*'
L02B3:	db	00
L02B4:	db	'"My dear Rutherford, this is not a reflection on The Checque'
	db	'red Cork, but I simply like a good drink!"*'
L031B:	db	00
L031C:	db	'room'
L0320:	db	00
L0321:	db	'buy'
L0324:	db	00
L0325:	db	'events'
L032B:	db	00
L032C:	db	'Minoc'
L0331:	db	00
L0332:	db	'"'Tis no time for idle chatter! There have been two people m'
	db	'urdered over at William's sawmill!"'
L0391:	db	00
L0392:	db	'buy'
L0395:	db	00
L0396:	db	'"We have a cornucopian variety of elixirs to quench thy tong'
	db	'ue and gourmet dishes to appease thy palate."'
L03FF:	db	00
L0400:	db	'"As I have finished my workday, I ask thee to come back anot'
	db	'her time. Thou dost have my thanks."'
L0460:	db	00
L0461:	db	'buy'
L0464:	db	00
L0465:	db	'room'
L0469:	db	00
L046A:	db	'"A room for the night is quite reasonable. Only 8 gold per p'
	db	'erson. Want one?"'
L04B7:	db	00
L04B8:	db	'"Thou art carrying too much to take the room key, '
L04EA:	db	00
L04EB:	db	'!"'
L04ED:	db	00
L04EE:	db	'"Here is thy room key. It is good only until thou dost leave'
	db	'."'
L052C:	db	00
L052D:	db	'"Thou dost not have enough gold, eh? That be right bad."'
L0565:	db	00
L0566:	db	'"Mayhaps another night, then."'
L0584:	db	00
L0585:	db	'"If thou wouldst please make thy request at a time that was '
	db	'during my normal business hours, I would be most grateful."'
L05FC:	db	00
L05FD:	db	'room'
L0601:	db	00
L0602:	db	'Minoc'
L0607:	db	00
L0608:	db	'"Yep, this town's usually bloody quiet. That was until recen'
	db	'tly!" His squinting eye suddenly opens wide and stares strai'
	db	'ght at you.'
L068B:	db	00
L068C:	db	'"Say, when exackly again didst thou say thou didst arrive in'
	db	' town, stranger?"~~After a moment of carefully observing you'
	db	', he shrugs his shoulders and goes back to wiping off the ba'
	db	'r.'
L0742:	db	00
L0743:	db	'Minoc'
L0748:	db	00
L0749:	db	'events'
L074F:	db	00
L0750:	db	'"Before all this evil at the sawmill, the buzz were all abou'
	db	't the monument."'
L079C:	db	00
L079D:	db	'events'
L07A3:	db	00
L07A4:	db	'sawmill'
L07AB:	db	00
L07AC:	db	'monument'
L07B4:	db	00
L07B5:	db	'murders'
L07BC:	db	00
L07BD:	db	'"Well, I suppose that clears thee from the list o' possible '
	db	'murderers. If'n thou wert the murderer, thou wouldst not hav'
	db	'e to be askin' questions o'people about wha' 'appened regard'
	db	'in' the murders. Thou wouldst already know, havin' been ther'
	db	'e."'
L08B0:	db	00
L08B1:	db	'murders'
L08B8:	db	00
L08B9:	db	'sawmill'
L08C0:	db	00
L08C1:	db	'"Say, thou be not from around here?" He looks at you skeptic'
	db	'ally. "Thou art not from the Fellowship by any chance, art t'
	db	'hou?"'
L093E:	db	00
L093F:	db	'"I thought so!"'
L094E:	db	00
L094F:	db	'Fellowship'
L0959:	db	00
L095A:	db	'murders'
L0961:	db	00
L0962:	db	'"Just askin'! Thou dost not have to take any offense!"'
L0998:	db	00
L0999:	db	'Fellowship'
L09A3:	db	00
L09A4:	db	'murders'
L09AB:	db	00
L09AC:	db	'sawmill'
L09B3:	db	00
L09B4:	db	'Hook'
L09B8:	db	00
L09B9:	db	'"I know him! He be a pirate who lives in Buccaneer's Den. Th'
	db	'ey say Hook is so mean he'd kill his own mudder for the righ'
	db	't price, an' I would wager they's right.~~"Why, I got into a'
	db	' fight with this Hook once. I was lucky and I escaped losin''
	db	' only my right arm and still with one good eye left. It was '
	db	'somewhere around that time that I started having second thou'
	db	'ghts about my career as a pirate and now here I be.'
L0B54:	db	00
L0B55:	db	'"I have not seen him recently, but the description of the mu'
	db	'rder scene certainly sounds like his handiwork!"'
L0BC1:	db	00
L0BC2:	db	'Hook'
L0BC6:	db	00
L0BC7:	db	'Crown Jewel'
L0BD2:	db	00
L0BD3:	db	'"That ship was, indeed, here of late. In fact, 'twas the nig'
	db	'ht of the murders! Could there be a connection? Hmmm..."'
L0C47:	db	00
L0C48:	db	'Crown Jewel'
L0C53:	db	00
L0C54:	db	'Fellowship'
L0C5E:	db	00
L0C5F:	db	'"Thank goodness that with all the town at each others' throa'
	db	'ts in recent weeks we have the Fellowship tryin' to hold the'
	db	' town together. I be no member or nothin', but I just a'hear'
	db	'ed of all the good things they done. Feedin' the poor an' su'
	db	'ch."'
L0D53:	db	00
L0D54:	db	'Fellowship'
L0D5E:	db	00
L0D5F:	db	'monument'
L0D67:	db	00
L0D68:	db	'"Oh, thou must mean thet statuer they are goin' ta build of '
	db	'our shipwright. His name is Owen, a local boy. I understan' '
	db	'it is to be as tall as a man on horseback and shows Owen gaz'
	db	'in' through a telerscope or some such thing like that."'
L0E53:	db	00
L0E54:	db	'monument'
L0E5C:	db	00
L0E5D:	db	'bye'
L0E60:	db	00
L0E61:	db	'"I shall see thee later... At least I will if thou dost stay'
	db	' in the front o' me good eye."*'
L0EBC:	db	00
