		.data
L0000:	db	'bye'
L0003:	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
L0007:	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
L000C:	db	00
L000D:	db	'Margareta'
L0016:	db	00
L0017:	db	'hourglass'
L0020:	db	00
L0021:	db	'You see a swarthy gypsy with soulful eyes, dressed in colorf'
	db	'ul clothes. He looks as if he has the weight of the world on'
	db	' his shoulders.'
L00A8:	db	00
L00A9:	db	'"Greetings vonce again," Jergi says as he bows, making a swi'
	db	'rling gesture with his hand.'
L0101:	db	00
L0102:	db	'name'
L0106:	db	00
L0107:	db	'"I am Jergi. Pleased to make thine acqvaintance."'
L0138:	db	00
L0139:	db	'name'
L013D:	db	00
L013E:	db	'job'
L0141:	db	00
L0142:	db	'"I am the King ov the Gypsies."'
L0161:	db	00
L0162:	db	'gypsies'
L0169:	db	00
L016A:	db	'gypsies'
L0171:	db	00
L0172:	db	'"My people have almost completely died out in this vorld. No'
	db	'w that I am their leader I am making their velfare my sole r'
	db	'esponsibility. Soon I vill decide if ve vill leave Minoc."'
L0224:	db	00
L0225:	db	'gypsies'
L022C:	db	00
L022D:	db	'Minoc'
L0232:	db	00
L0233:	db	'died out'
L023B:	db	00
L023C:	db	'died out'
L0244:	db	00
L0245:	db	'"Ve gypsies are a people who live to vander. But there are f'
	db	'ewer and fewer places vhere ve are velcome. Ve are victimize'
	db	'd by the ancient hatreds that have plagued our kind since th'
	db	'e days ov ancient Sosaria."'
L0314:	db	00
L0315:	db	'died out'
L031D:	db	00
L031E:	db	'Minoc'
L0323:	db	00
L0324:	db	'"Our people came here because ve thought ve vould be accepte'
	db	'd. It seemed for a very long time that ve vere. But after th'
	db	'ese savage murders it looks like it is time for us to roam v'
	db	'once again."'
L03E4:	db	00
L03E5:	db	'Minoc'
L03EA:	db	00
L03EB:	db	'murders'
L03F2:	db	00
L03F3:	db	'accepted'
L03FB:	db	00
L03FC:	db	'accepted'
L0404:	db	00
L0405:	db	'"Ve have alvays been subject to the prejudices ov others! Ve'
	db	' are called thieves and vorse! But ve are a people that only'
	db	' vish to play our music, and dance, and live in peace. I tho'
	db	'ught the people here understood this."'
L04DF:	db	00
L04E0:	db	'accepted'
L04E8:	db	00
L04E9:	db	'murders'
L04F0:	db	00
L04F1:	db	'"Frederico vas mine only brother, and no vone loved Tania mo'
	db	're than I did, save for Frederico himself. Vhat happened to '
	db	'them vas unspeakable. I vish I could tell thee more. If thou'
	db	' vishest thou may speak to Sasha, but only briefly. Now is t'
	db	'he time for him to mourn."'
L05FB:	db	00
L05FC:	db	'murders'
L0603:	db	00
L0604:	db	'Sasha'
L0609:	db	00
L060A:	db	'Tania'
L060F:	db	00
L0610:	db	'Frederico'
L0619:	db	00
L061A:	db	'Frederico'
L0623:	db	00
L0624:	db	'"Some thought ov my brother Frederico as a harsh man, but th'
	db	'ose ov us who knew him could see that he vas simply governed'
	db	' by the same prides and passions that rule all gypsies."'
L06D4:	db	00
L06D5:	db	'Frederico'
L06DE:	db	00
L06DF:	db	'Tania'
L06E4:	db	00
L06E5:	db	'"She vas the most beautiful voman I had ever seen. Both my b'
	db	'rother and I vere in love vith her. Ve both tried to vin her'
	db	' heart. I failed and thought that I vould spend the rest ov '
	db	'my life vith no vone. It vas not until last year that my vif'
	db	'e Margareta and I vere married and my secretly broken heart '
	db	'vas mended."'
L081D:	db	00
L081E:	db	'Tania'
L0823:	db	00
L0824:	db	'Sasha'
L0829:	db	00
L082A:	db	'"He is the son ov Frederico and Tania. He left us to learn m'
	db	'ore about The Fellowship. Ov course, he feels responsible fo'
	db	'r vhat happened..."'
L08B5:	db	00
L08B6:	db	'Sasha'
L08BB:	db	00
L08BC:	db	'Fellowship'
L08C6:	db	00
L08C7:	db	'responsible'
L08D2:	db	00
L08D3:	db	'responsible'
L08DE:	db	00
L08DF:	db	'"Ve do not blame Sasha for vhat happened. Ve vill not punish'
	db	' him."'
L0921:	db	00
L0922:	db	'responsible'
L092D:	db	00
L092E:	db	'Fellowship'
L0938:	db	00
L0939:	db	'"Sasha vill have to decide if he vants to stay vith his peop'
	db	'le or return to The Fellowship. I believe he vill make the r'
	db	'ight choice."'
L09BE:	db	00
L09BF:	db	'Fellowship'
L09C9:	db	00
L09CA:	db	'Margareta'
L09D3:	db	00
L09D4:	db	'"My vife is a vise voman who has some ov the necessary talen'
	db	'ts to see the future. Thou shouldst speak vith her."'
L0A44:	db	00
L0A45:	db	'Margareta'
L0A4E:	db	00
L0A4F:	db	'hourglass'
L0A58:	db	00
L0A59:	db	'"I do not know vhat thou art talking about. I know nothing o'
	db	'f a mage named Nicodemus, nor of his hourglass. Be vary -- m'
	db	'ages are quite mad these days!"'
L0AF0:	db	00
L0AF1:	db	'hourglass'
L0AFA:	db	00
L0AFB:	db	'bye'
L0AFE:	db	00
L0AFF:	db	'"Mayest thou have much fortune in thine endeavors."*'
L0B33:	db	00
