		.data
L0000:	db	'bye'
L0003:	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
L0007:	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
L000C:	db	00
L000D:	db	'Time Lord'
L0016:	db	00
L0017:	db	'hourglass'
L0020:	db	00
L0021:	db	'enchant'
L0028:	db	00
L0029:	db	'Your old friend Nicodemus has a far away look in his eyes.'
L0063:	db	00
L0064:	db	'"Who art thou?" Nicodemus asks. "Oh, I remember. Remember de'
	db	'member! Ha ha ha!"'
L00B2:	db	00
L00B3:	db	'"Hello again, '
L00C1:	db	00
L00C2:	db	'," says Nicodemus.'
L00D4:	db	00
L00D5:	db	'name'
L00D9:	db	00
L00DA:	db	'"That is a very good question. Some days I can actually reme'
	db	'mber. Let's see... today... Yes! I am Nicodemus! Nicodomus! '
	db	'Nicodimus! Nico-nico-kukodamus! Ha ha ha!"'
L017C:	db	00
L017D:	db	'"Thou art addressing Nicodemus."'
L019D:	db	00
L019E:	db	'name'
L01A2:	db	00
L01A3:	db	'job'
L01A6:	db	00
L01A7:	db	'"To go absolutely mad! For that is indeed what is happening!'
	db	' My magic no longer works! Every time I attempt to change so'
	db	'mething into a drake, it only becomes a newt! Oh, newty-wewt'
	db	'y scooty-booty!" He speaks to an imaginary creature beside h'
	db	'im. "Who asked thee? Away with thee!" He turns to you. "Sorr'
	db	'y. That bloody newt keeps trying to undermine my conversatio'
	db	'n. Anyway... I suppose I can sell thee some reagents, potion'
	db	's, or spells. I must make a living somecow. I mean somehow! '
	db	'That was Some Cow! Ha ha ha!"'
L03A4:	db	00
L03A5:	db	'potions'
L03AC:	db	00
L03AD:	db	'magic'
L03B2:	db	00
L03B3:	db	'"Why, to perform magic! It seems that the disturbance in the'
	db	' ether has been repaired! I can also sell thee some reagents'
	db	' or spells."'
L0437:	db	00
L0438:	db	'reagents'
L0440:	db	00
L0441:	db	'spells'
L0447:	db	00
L0448:	db	'magic'
L044D:	db	00
L044E:	db	'"Magic? What magic!? All the magic in the world has gone com'
	db	'pletely topsy-turvy! Oh, blurpsy-flurpsy! Ha ha ha! Those ar'
	db	'e silly words, are they not? 'Tis a pity they are not magica'
	db	'l! Ha ha ha!"'
L050F:	db	00
L0510:	db	'"The ether is repaired. The mages of the world are indebted '
	db	'to thee."'
L0555:	db	00
L0556:	db	'magic'
L055B:	db	00
L055C:	db	'spells'
L0562:	db	00
L0563:	db	'"Dost thou wish to buy some spells?"'
L0587:	db	00
L0588:	db	'"Never mind, then!"'
L059B:	db	00
L059C:	db	'reagents'
L05A4:	db	00
L05A5:	db	'"Dost thou wish to buy some reagents?"'
L05CB:	db	00
L05CC:	db	'"Never mind, then!"'
L05DF:	db	00
L05E0:	db	'potions'
L05E7:	db	00
L05E8:	db	'"Potions? What makes thee think I have potions? Art thou sur'
	db	'e thou dost not want Lotions? I certainly have lotions! Otio'
	db	'ns, slotions, motions, votions! Ha ha ha! Wait! Oh, yes! I d'
	db	'o have potions! I told thee so, didn't I! Let us see... I ha'
	db	've this black potion here. I am not sure what it does exactl'
	db	'y, but I am quite sure it turns one invisible.'
L0742:	db	00
L0743:	db	'"Yes, I have potions. Well, I have this black one. It is an '
	db	'invisibility potion.'
L0793:	db	00
L0794:	db	'"Dost thou want it for, say, 75 gold?"'
L07BA:	db	00
L07BB:	db	'"Here is the potion."'
L07D0:	db	00
L07D1:	db	'"Thou dost not have enough room to carry the potion!"'
L0806:	db	00
L0807:	db	'"Art thou trying to cheat me? Thou dost not have enough gold'
	db	'!"'
L0845:	db	00
L0846:	db	'"Then why didst thou mention it? Leave me alone!"'
L0877:	db	00
L0878:	db	'potions'
L087F:	db	00
L0880:	db	'Time Lord'
L0889:	db	00
L088A:	db	'"Timey Limey Lord? Hmmm. I don't know him. Wait! Yes I do. D'
	db	'oes he have a big black mustache and three pairs of pants? N'
	db	'o! I know who he is. He's the fellow who came to fix my sund'
	db	'ial the other day, right?"'
L0958:	db	00
L0959:	db	'"I thought so! Tell him that bloody thing still doesn't work'
	db	'! It gives me three shadows! Dadows badows whoopeee! Ha ha h'
	db	'a!"'
L09D4:	db	00
L09D5:	db	'"He's not? Hmmm. Then he must be the man I am not thinking o'
	db	'f!"'
L0A14:	db	00
L0A15:	db	'"Wait! I remember! He is my Knight's Bridge opponent! We pla'
	db	'y on my Knight's Bridge court just north of mine house."'
L0A89:	db	00
L0A8A:	db	'"I have not spoken to the Time Lord in months! How is the ol'
	db	'd codger? Give him my regards. Tell him I miss our Knight's '
	db	'Bridge games!"'
L0B10:	db	00
L0B11:	db	'Time Lord'
L0B1A:	db	00
L0B1B:	db	'Knight's Bridge'
L0B2A:	db	00
L0B2B:	db	'Knight's Bridge'
L0B3A:	db	00
L0B3B:	db	'"'Tis a life-size board game. I have a book around here some'
	db	'where which contains the rules."'
L0B97:	db	00
L0B98:	db	'Knight's Bridge'
L0BA7:	db	00
L0BA8:	db	'hourglass'
L0BB1:	db	00
L0BB2:	db	'"Yes, I just enchanted it."'
L0BCD:	db	00
L0BCE:	db	'"This Time Lord told thee what? An hourglass! I have no blin'
	db	'king hourglass! Glassy wassy hoursplassy! Ha ha ha! Wait! An'
	db	' enchanted hourglass? That does ring a bell. Clang Clang Cla'
	db	'ng! Ha ha ha! Wait! I remember. I had an hourglass. I sold i'
	db	't. To a gypsy. Or was it an antique dealer? I think I might '
	db	'have sold it to a gypsy antique dealer in Britain. Or Paws. '
	db	'Somewhere on that side of the land. But if my memory serves '
	db	'me correctly, that hourglass used up its enchantment, which '
	db	'is why I sold it. I suppose if the ether is repaired, I coul'
	db	'd possibly re-enchant it. Bring it to me and we'll see what '
	db	'we can do. I know! We can play a rousing game of chess! But '
	db	'only if I can deal at all times. I do not trust thee."'
L0E98:	db	00
L0E99:	db	'"Mine old hourglass! Of course I remember it! I believe I so'
	db	'ld it to an antique dealer in Paws. I might be able to re-en'
	db	'chant it if thou wouldst bring it to me."'
L0F3A:	db	00
L0F3B:	db	'"What's this? An hourglass of some kind? Wait! It looks vagu'
	db	'ely familiar! Thief!! This is mine hourglass! I have been lo'
	db	'oking for it for years! Where didst thou get it, scoundrel? '
	db	'I shall turn thee into a duck!"~~Nicodemus intones some spel'
	db	'l and points at you, but nothing happens.~~"Zounds! Thou art'
	db	' no more a quacker than I am. Nothing works anymore. Quacker'
	db	' slacker wacker flacker! Ha ha ha!"'
L10C6:	db	00
L10C7:	db	'"Mine old hourglass! I suppose I could revitalize the enchan'
	db	'tment upon it."'
L1112:	db	00
L1113:	db	'hourglass'
L111C:	db	00
L111D:	db	'enchant'
L1124:	db	00
L1125:	db	'"Enchant? Thou dost want me to enchant this wretched thing? '
	db	'Thou must have the brain of a toad! Toady woady bloady coady'
	db	'! Ha ha ha!~~"Do me a favor, Mister Avatar. Repair the blink'
	db	'ing ether, wilt thou? Do that and I can enchant thy glourbla'
	db	'ss. I mean floursass. I mean hourglass. Tell that to thy 'Ti'
	db	'me Lord'. Thou canst also tell him he needs a bath."'
L1285:	db	00
L1286:	db	'"I would be most happy to enchant the hourglass. After freei'
	db	'ng the ether, I am most indebted to thee. Let me see it..."'
L12FD:	db	00
L12FE:	db	'Nicodemus takes the hourglass and studies it a moment. He se'
	db	'ts it on a table and closes his eyes, concentrating. He into'
	db	'nes a few words, throws some reagents into the air, and pass'
	db	'es his hand over the artifact.~~"That should do it." He hand'
	db	's the hourglass back to you.'
L140A:	db	00
L140B:	db	'"Where is it? Thou dost not have the hourglass!"'
L143B:	db	00
L143C:	db	'enchant'
L1443:	db	00
L1444:	db	'bye'
L1447:	db	00
L1448:	db	'"Bye bye booby booby bye bye! Ha ha ha!"*'
L1471:	db	00
L1472:	db	'"Goodbye, '
L147C:	db	00
L147D:	db	'."*'
