L0000:	db	'bye'
L0003:	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
L0007:	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
L000C:	db	00
L000D:	db	'The man greets you with stern, suspicious eyes.'
L003C:	db	00
L003D:	db	'"What is thy business, '
L0054:	db	00
L0055:	db	'?"'
L0057:	db	00
L0058:	db	'name'
L005C:	db	00
L005D:	db	'"I am Sir Jeff, '
L006D:	db	00
L006E:	db	'."'
L0070:	db	00
L0071:	db	'name'
L0075:	db	00
L0076:	db	'job'
L0079:	db	00
L007A:	db	'"I am the High Court official at the prison here in the Abbe'
	db	'y."'
L00B9:	db	00
L00BA:	db	'Abbey'
L00BF:	db	00
L00C0:	db	'official'
L00C8:	db	00
L00C9:	db	'official'
L00D1:	db	00
L00D2:	db	'"I am the judiciary part of Britannia's government. It is my'
	db	' job to see that criminals are brought to justice."'
L0141:	db	00
L0142:	db	'criminals'
L014B:	db	00
L014C:	db	'official'
L0154:	db	00
L0155:	db	'criminals'
L015E:	db	00
L015F:	db	'"We have two prisoners already, but there are many scoundrel'
	db	's who still roam free."'
L01B2:	db	00
L01B3:	db	'scoundrels'
L01BD:	db	00
L01BE:	db	'prisoners'
L01C7:	db	00
L01C8:	db	'criminals'
L01D1:	db	00
L01D2:	db	'prisoners'
L01DB:	db	00
L01DC:	db	'"Thou, of course, hast never met them," he says, his brow na'
	db	'rrowing, "but we have a pirate, and," he pauses, "a troll. I'
	db	'f thou dost wish to see them, speak with Goth, the jailer."'
L028F:	db	00
L0290:	db	'Goth'
L0294:	db	00
L0295:	db	'prisoners'
L029E:	db	00
L029F:	db	'scoundrels'
L02A9:	db	00
L02AA:	db	'"See for thyself, the posted bills for known villains are in'
	db	' the log book in the courtroom."'
L0306:	db	00
L0307:	db	'scoundrels'
L0311:	db	00
L0312:	db	'Goth'
L0316:	db	00
L0317:	db	'"He has only been working here for a few weeks, but I alread'
	db	'y know he is not trustworthy. There is something obviously u'
	db	'nscrupulous about him. He is not a friend of thine, is he?"'
L03CA:	db	00
L03CB:	db	'"I suspected as much." He turns away from you.*'
L03FA:	db	00
L03FB:	db	'"No," he says, watching you closely, "of course he is not."'
L0436:	db	00
L0437:	db	'Goth'
L043B:	db	00
L043C:	db	'Abbey'
L0441:	db	00
L0442:	db	'"The monks live and study there, but they do little more tha'
	db	'n winemaking. Well, I know one of them tends the garden."'
L04B7:	db	00
L04B8:	db	'Abbey'
L04BD:	db	00
L04BE:	db	'bye'
L04C1:	db	00
L04C2:	db	'"Keep thine heart and mind on the straight path, '
L04F3:	db	00
L04F4:	db	'."'
L04F6:	db	00
