L0008:	db	'name'
L000C:	db	00
L000D:	db	'You see an unkempt, yet dapper man talking to himself.'
L0043:	db	00
L0044:	db	'"Eh, wot's that? Oh, it's you, '
L0063:	db	00
L0064:	db	'."'
L0066:	db	00
L0067:	db	'name'
L006B:	db	00
L006C:	db	'"M'name's Tiery, '
L007D:	db	00
L007E:	db	'."'
L0080:	db	00
L0081:	db	'name'
L0085:	db	00
L0086:	db	'job'
L0089:	db	00
L008A:	db	'"Eh, 'ow's that? Oh, m'job. Why, Oi take good care o' me bud'
	db	'dies in the graveyard 'ere in Empath Abbey, Oi do."'
L00F9:	db	00
L00FA:	db	'buddies'
L0101:	db	00
L0102:	db	'Empath Abbey'
L010E:	db	00
L010F:	db	'Empath Abbey'
L011B:	db	00
L011C:	db	'"What do ye mean did Oi 'umpeth Abby. 'Course Oi didn't. Oi '
	db	'never went anywhere near Abby. 'Oo told ye that?"'
L0189:	db	00
L018A:	db	''Umpeth Abby'
L0196:	db	00
L0197:	db	'Empath Abbey'
L01A3:	db	00
L01A4:	db	''Umpeth Abby'
L01B0:	db	00
L01B1:	db	'"Empath Abbey? Why, this 'ere's Empath Abbey, '
L01DF:	db	00
L01E0:	db	'. Oi don't mean to pry, but if ye knowest not where ye be, w'
	db	'hy 'ave ye come 'ere?" He shakes his head. "It's just as Oi '
	db	'was tellin' Darek the other day, `If ye never want to be los'
	db	't,' Oi said, `don't ever go nowheres.'"'
L02BB:	db	00
L02BC:	db	''Umpeth Abby'
L02C8:	db	00
L02C9:	db	'buddies'
L02D0:	db	00
L02D1:	db	'"What wrong with the bodies? Oi don' do nothing more than bu'
	db	'ry 'em! A fellow could get in lots o' trouble spreading rumo'
	db	'rs like that."'
L0357:	db	00
L0358:	db	'bodies'
L035E:	db	00
L035F:	db	'bury'
L0363:	db	00
L0364:	db	'buddies'
L036B:	db	00
L036C:	db	'bury'
L0370:	db	00
L0371:	db	'"Barry? Oh, 'im. Oi don't know what ye's talkin' about. Oi n'
	db	'ever met Barry's woife! 'Twas just a lie they's spreadin' ab'
	db	'out me."'
L03F1:	db	00
L03F2:	db	'bury'
L03F6:	db	00
L03F7:	db	'Barry'
L03FC:	db	00
L03FD:	db	'Barry'
L0402:	db	00
L0403:	db	'"Oi already told ye that's m'job."'
L0425:	db	00
L0426:	db	'Barry'
L042B:	db	00
L042C:	db	'bodies'
L0432:	db	00
L0433:	db	'"That's right. M'buddies! Oi bury 'em. It's m'job." He squin'
	db	'ts at you. "Unless, '
L0483:	db	00
L0484:	db	', yer askin' about the people 'ere?"'
L04A8:	db	00
L04A9:	db	'people'
L04AF:	db	00
L04B0:	db	'bodies'
L04B6:	db	00
L04B7:	db	'people'
L04BD:	db	00
L04BE:	db	'"No! Of course Oi don't use peep holes. What sort o' questio'
	db	'n is that to ask a fellow, '
L0515:	db	00
L0516:	db	'?"'
L0518:	db	00
L0519:	db	'peep hole'
L0522:	db	00
L0523:	db	'people'
L0529:	db	00
L052A:	db	'peep hole'
L0533:	db	00
L0534:	db	'"Well, Oi only know a few people 'ere, but Oi'll try an' 'el'
	db	'p as best as Oi am able. 'Oo do ye want to know about? My tw'
	db	'o best friends are Garth an' Darek, but Oi often talk to Nin'
	db	'a an' Bart when Oi get the chance.~~'
L060C:	db	00
L060D:	db	'"Recently, that Perrin fellow from across the way 'as been s'
	db	'pendin' some toime with me. 'E's a real nice chap. A l'ttle '
	db	'brainy, perhaps, '
L0696:	db	00
L0697:	db	', but Oi like 'im just the same. Anyone else ye'd like to kn'
	db	'ow about?"'
L06DD:	db	00
L06DE:	db	'"Well, that Perrin fellow'd be a better one to ask than Oi'd'
	db	' be, '
L071F:	db	00
L0720:	db	'. 'E knows a lot, that one does."'
L0741:	db	00
L0742:	db	'"All right then, glad Oi could introduce ye to a few o' my f'
	db	'riends."'
L0786:	db	00
L0787:	db	'peep hole'
L0790:	db	00
L0791:	db	'bye'
L0794:	db	00
L0795:	db	'"G'day, '
L079D:	db	00
L079E:	db	'. 'Ave a pleasant journey. Oi'll tell Malc 'allo for ye."*'
L07D8:	db	00
