		.funcnumber	046BH
		.data
L0000:	db	'Avatar'
L0006:	db	00
L0007:	db	'You see a large cyclops. It looks at you and blinks its eye '
	db	'in irritation.'
L0051:	db	00
L0052:	db	'"What dost thou want?" says Iskander.'
L0077:	db	00
L0078:	db	'bye'
L007B:	db	00
L007C:	db	'job'
L007F:	db	00
L0080:	db	'name'
L0084:	db	00
L0085:	db	'Eiko and Amanda'
L0094:	db	00
L0095:	db	'name'
L0099:	db	00
L009A:	db	'"I am of the clan Ironheart, the eleventh son of Valador. Th'
	db	'ey call me Iskander."'
L00EB:	db	00
L00EC:	db	'name'
L00F0:	db	00
L00F1:	db	'job'
L00F4:	db	00
L00F5:	db	'"My cyclopean people say I am a hero. Many of you humans say'
	db	' I am a monster. No doubt, the truth is somewhere in between'
	db	'."'
L016F:	db	00
L0170:	db	'monster'
L0177:	db	00
L0178:	db	'hero'
L017C:	db	00
L017D:	db	'hero'
L0181:	db	00
L0182:	db	'"One hundred and eighty-nine years ago I slew the seven Gaze'
	db	'r Princes when they used their magic to steal the eye from t'
	db	'he leader of our tribe, but such things are now ancient hist'
	db	'ory and are no longer of any consequence."'
L0260:	db	00
L0261:	db	'hero'
L0265:	db	00
L0266:	db	'ancient history'
L0275:	db	00
L0276:	db	'eye'
L0279:	db	00
L027A:	db	'tribe'
L027F:	db	00
L0280:	db	'monster'
L0287:	db	00
L0288:	db	'"On numerous occasions I have caused the unpleasant end of h'
	db	'uman interlopers who mistakenly believed our race was fit fo'
	db	'r nothing save to be plundered. But I have no quarrel with t'
	db	'hee." He pauses to scrutinize you. "For the moment."'
L0370:	db	00
L0371:	db	'monster'
L0378:	db	00
L0379:	db	'thee'
L037D:	db	00
L037E:	db	'thee'
L0382:	db	00
L0383:	db	'"Thou dost know my name, but I still do not know the name of'
	db	' thee. I like to know to whom I am speaking. What is thy nam'
	db	'e?"'
L03FE:	db	00
L03FF:	db	'"I have heard of thee, Avatar. Thou hast come into conflict '
	db	'against our kind before, I know. But I have also heard the t'
	db	'ales of thine heroic and spiritual quests and I believe thee'
	db	' to be a just and noble man. Thou mayest call me friend."'
L04EC:	db	00
L04ED:	db	'"A pleasure to meet thee, '
L0507:	db	00
L0508:	db	'."'
L050A:	db	00
L050B:	db	'thee'
L050F:	db	00
L0510:	db	'tribe'
L0515:	db	00
L0516:	db	'"Those of my tribe are a quiet people. They farm the rocky s'
	db	'oil, but are also very good tool makers. I was sent to find '
	db	'them a new homeland."'
L05A3:	db	00
L05A4:	db	'tribe'
L05A9:	db	00
L05AA:	db	'homeland'
L05B2:	db	00
L05B3:	db	'eye'
L05B6:	db	00
L05B7:	db	'"The eye of a cyclops is considered quite a delicacy to some'
	db	' of the less genteel races of Britannia. Twice have foul cre'
	db	'atures tried to take mine, and twice have I dined on their h'
	db	'earts."'
L0672:	db	00
L0673:	db	'eye'
L0676:	db	00
L0677:	db	'ancient history'
L0686:	db	00
L0687:	db	'"Then they called me 'Wonder Boy'. For nearly a hundred year'
	db	's that was the nickname by which I was known. I was most gra'
	db	'teful when they stopped doing that!"'
L0723:	db	00
L0724:	db	'ancient history'
L0733:	db	00
L0734:	db	'Wonder Boy'
L073E:	db	00
L073F:	db	'Wonder Boy'
L0749:	db	00
L074A:	db	'Iskander squints his eye at you. "Do not start that again!"'
L0785:	db	00
L0786:	db	'Wonder Boy'
L0790:	db	00
L0791:	db	'homeland'
L0799:	db	00
L079A:	db	'"My village lies a great many days' journey away. The people'
	db	' there desire a place where they can live in peace with thei'
	db	'r surroundings. I have not found such a place yet, but I wil'
	db	'l search everywhere until I do."'
L086E:	db	00
L086F:	db	'homeland'
L0877:	db	00
L0878:	db	'everywhere'
L0882:	db	00
L0883:	db	'peace'
L0888:	db	00
L0889:	db	'peace'
L088E:	db	00
L088F:	db	'"While I am two hundred and six, not long in years for one o'
	db	'f my race, I already have the heart of an old man. A hero's '
	db	'adventures have no more attraction for me. I long to settle '
	db	'down with my people and spend my days tending the fields or '
	db	'in my workshop building things."'
L099F:	db	00
L09A0:	db	'peace'
L09A5:	db	00
L09A6:	db	'everywhere'
L09B0:	db	00
L09B1:	db	'"My searches have brought me to this dreadful place. I incor'
	db	'rectly surmised that since magic does not work it would be r'
	db	'elatively safe. It is here that I have been perplexed by a t'
	db	'errible riddle."'
L0A75:	db	00
L0A76:	db	'everywhere'
L0A80:	db	00
L0A81:	db	'riddle'
L0A87:	db	00
L0A88:	db	'magic'
L0A8D:	db	00
L0A8E:	db	'riddle'
L0A94:	db	00
L0A95:	db	'"Standing at the doorway of one room in this place, I saw an'
	db	' enormous image of a tetrahedron. As I tried to near it a wa'
	db	've of amnesia passed over me. Once more I was standing in th'
	db	'e doorway. I could remember nothing more."'
L0B73:	db	00
L0B74:	db	'riddle'
L0B7A:	db	00
L0B7B:	db	'amnesia'
L0B82:	db	00
L0B83:	db	'tetrahedron'
L0B8E:	db	00
L0B8F:	db	'tetrahedron'
L0B9A:	db	00
L0B9B:	db	'"I believe that is word you humans use to describe a polyhed'
	db	'ron with four faces."'
L0BEC:	db	00
L0BED:	db	'tetrahedron'
L0BF8:	db	00
L0BF9:	db	'amnesia'
L0C00:	db	00
L0C01:	db	'"This same wave of amnesia struck me every time I tried to a'
	db	'pproach the tetrahedron. I do not know what sort of foul mag'
	db	'ic this is."'
L0C85:	db	00
L0C86:	db	'amnesia'
L0C8D:	db	00
L0C8E:	db	'foul magic'
L0C98:	db	00
L0C99:	db	'foul magic'
L0CA3:	db	00
L0CA4:	db	'"Now that thou hast destroyed the mysterious tetrahedron I w'
	db	'ill complete mine exploration of this place. I have a feelin'
	db	'g that the homeland I seek is very far away but one never kn'
	db	'ows where the next clue will be that shall lead me to it."'
L0D92:	db	00
L0D93:	db	'"Perhaps thou shalt be able to solve this mystery. I have be'
	db	'en unable to as of yet. But I shall remain here until its se'
	db	'cret is revealed."'
L0E1D:	db	00
L0E1E:	db	'"I warn thee that this place is not safe. It holds unknown p'
	db	'erils. Perhaps thou wouldst do better to leave this place."'
L0E95:	db	00
L0E96:	db	'foul magic'
L0EA0:	db	00
L0EA1:	db	'magic'
L0EA6:	db	00
L0EA7:	db	'"Surely, thou dost know that magic no longer functions as it'
	db	' once did. There are those who say that the age of magic is '
	db	'over. If that is so, then I fear that there may be no place '
	db	'left in this world for my people."'
L0F7D:	db	00
L0F7E:	db	'"Of course, now that thou hast destroyed the tetrahedron all'
	db	' magic has been restored. I congratulate thee for thine hero'
	db	'ic deed!"'
L0FFF:	db	00
L1000:	db	'magic'
L1005:	db	00
L1006:	db	'Eiko and Amanda'
L1015:	db	00
L1016:	db	'"Yes, I have heard those names before. Those are the names o'
	db	'f two warriors who have been after me for revenge. They say '
	db	'I killed their father and I must admit to thee that it is tr'
	db	'ue. I did kill their father."'
L10E7:	db	00
L10E8:	db	'Eiko and Amanda'
L10F7:	db	00
L10F8:	db	'killed their father'
L110B:	db	00
L110C:	db	'revenge'
L1113:	db	00
L1114:	db	'revenge'
L111B:	db	00
L111C:	db	'"I know that Eiko and Amanda have been after me for some tim'
	db	'e looking for vengeance. I say let them come. I will not sta'
	db	'nd still for them nor shall I run from them. When they find '
	db	'me they are welcome to try and take their justice from me. I'
	db	'f they win then it was meant to be. If they do not I will ha'
	db	've no regrets."'
L1257:	db	00
L1258:	db	'revenge'
L125F:	db	00
L1260:	db	'killed their father'
L1273:	db	00
L1274:	db	'"Their father's name was Kalideth. He suffered from the mage'
	db	' madness. His attack on me was unprovoked. For some reason h'
	db	'e blamed the failure of magic upon my people. His own magics'
	db	' were still quite potent and I barely survived the encounter'
	db	'. I killed Kalideth in self-defense, but I did not want to k'
	db	'ill him. I wish there to still be some magic left in this wo'
	db	'rld and I mourned his passing as much as anyone."'
