		.data
L0000:	db	'bye'
L0003:	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
L0007:	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
L000C:	db	00
L000D:	db	'garden'
L0013:	db	00
L0014:	db	'The monk pulls back her cowl far enough for you to see her f'
	db	'ace.'
L0054:	db	00
L0055:	db	'"Greetings, '
L0061:	db	00
L0062:	db	'. I hope thy days are full of beauty."'
L0088:	db	00
L0089:	db	'name'
L008D:	db	00
L008E:	db	'"Thou mayest call me Aimi, '
L00A9:	db	00
L00AA:	db	'."'
L00AC:	db	00
L00AD:	db	'garden'
L00B3:	db	00
L00B4:	db	'name'
L00B8:	db	00
L00B9:	db	'job'
L00BC:	db	00
L00BD:	db	'"As a monk, I am not sure how to answer thy question. I ofte'
	db	'n help to make wine. However, '
L0117:	db	00
L0118:	db	', in my spare time I paint or tend my garden here at the Abb'
	db	'ey."'
L0158:	db	00
L0159:	db	'Abbey'
L015E:	db	00
L015F:	db	'garden'
L0165:	db	00
L0166:	db	'paint'
L016B:	db	00
L016C:	db	'Kreg'
L0170:	db	00
L0171:	db	'Abbey'
L0176:	db	00
L0177:	db	'"I have spent little time with others in the area. Thou maye'
	db	'st wish to speak with Taylor, for he knows much more about t'
	db	'he people, animals, and sights in this area than I do."'
L0226:	db	00
L0227:	db	'Taylor'
L022D:	db	00
L022E:	db	'Abbey'
L0233:	db	00
L0234:	db	'Taylor'
L023A:	db	00
L023B:	db	'"He is a fellow monk. He spends his time studying the plants'
	db	', animals, and geography of Britannia."'
L029E:	db	00
L029F:	db	'Taylor'
L02A5:	db	00
L02A6:	db	'paint'
L02AB:	db	00
L02AC:	db	'"Yes," she blushes, "I have long admired those who are able '
	db	'to express themselves visually. Sadly," she says, laughing, '
	db	'"I am not very good. However, I also collect art. In fact, I'
	db	' have an original Sterling hanging in my room. Perhaps thou '
	db	'couldst see it sometime."'
L03B5:	db	00
L03B6:	db	'paint'
L03BB:	db	00
L03BC:	db	'garden'
L03C2:	db	00
L03C3:	db	'"My garden? I have been tending it for years now. I am a fir'
	db	'm believer in the value of aesthetics, so I plant only flowe'
	db	'rs. Sometimes I sell them in bouquets when people want them,'
	db	' but I do that very rarely."'
L0493:	db	00
L0494:	db	'buy'
L0497:	db	00
L0498:	db	'aesthetics'
L04A2:	db	00
L04A3:	db	'garden'
L04A9:	db	00
L04AA:	db	'aesthetics'
L04B4:	db	00
L04B5:	db	'"It refers to the practice or study of all things beautiful.'
	db	'"'
L04F2:	db	00
L04F3:	db	'aesthetics'
L04FD:	db	00
L04FE:	db	'buy'
L0501:	db	00
L0502:	db	'"Thou wishest to buy a bouquet?"'
L0522:	db	00
L0523:	db	'"Dost thou have anyone to give these flowers to?"'
L0554:	db	00
L0555:	db	'You tell her about the passing away of Reyna's mother.~"Ah, '
	db	'yes. I had heard of Reyna's loss. That is a noble reason. Pl'
	db	'ease take these flowers and give them to her."'
L05FB:	db	00
L05FC:	db	'"Good. 'Tis always best to have someone to receive flowers. '
	db	'The flowers will cost 10 gold. Dost thou still want them?"'
L0672:	db	00
L0673:	db	'"I think thou wilt find these to be exceptionally beautiful.'
	db	'"'
L06B0:	db	00
L06B1:	db	'"It appears thou dost not have room for my flowers. A pity."'
L06ED:	db	00
L06EE:	db	'"I am sorry, '
L06FB:	db	00
L06FC:	db	'. Thou dost not have the gold."'
L071B:	db	00
L071C:	db	'"I understand, '
L072B:	db	00
L072C:	db	'. Free flowers are indeed the best. And wild flowers are qui'
	db	'te free. For now, '
L077A:	db	00
L077B:	db	', do no more than promise me thou wilt take the time to enjo'
	db	'y my garden."'
L07C4:	db	00
L07C5:	db	'"That is indeed unfortunate, '
L07E2:	db	00
L07E3:	db	'. 'Tis always best to have someone to receive flowers."'
L081A:	db	00
L081B:	db	'"Perhaps next time, thou mightest be interested. For now, '
L0855:	db	00
L0856:	db	', do no more than promise me thou wilt take the time to enjo'
	db	'y my garden."'
L089F:	db	00
L08A0:	db	'buy'
L08A3:	db	00
L08A4:	db	'Kreg'
L08A8:	db	00
L08A9:	db	'"I am afraid I do not know of such a person."'
L08D6:	db	00
L08D7:	db	'Kreg'
L08DB:	db	00
L08DC:	db	'bye'
L08DF:	db	00
L08E0:	db	'"Fare thee well, '
L08F1:	db	00
L08F2:	db	'. May the sweet scent of beauty never pass thee by."*'
L0927:	db	00
