L0000:	db	'bye'
L0003:	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
L0007:	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
L000C:	db	00
L000D:	db	'Resting an axe on his shoulder, a tall, broad-chested man sm'
	db	'iles and nods at you.'
L005E:	db	00
L005F:	db	'"'ello, '
L0067:	db	00
L0068:	db	'. Good day, ay?"'
L0078:	db	00
L0079:	db	'name'
L007D:	db	00
L007E:	db	'"Thou kin call me Ben, '
L0095:	db	00
L0096:	db	'. I live 'ere in the forest of Yew."'
L00BA:	db	00
L00BB:	db	'name'
L00BF:	db	00
L00C0:	db	'forest'
L00C6:	db	00
L00C7:	db	'Yew'
L00CA:	db	00
L00CB:	db	'job'
L00CE:	db	00
L00CF:	db	'"I be a logger, '
L00DF:	db	00
L00E0:	db	'. 'Tis what I have done all my life. In fact, '
L010E:	db	00
L010F:	db	', 'tis what my father did. And 'is father before 'im. And so'
	db	' on. We have been doin' this for more than ten generations."'
L0187:	db	00
L0188:	db	'Silverleaf'
L0192:	db	00
L0193:	db	'Yew'
L0196:	db	00
L0197:	db	'"It was once a large town, but now, 'tis but a smattering of'
	db	' cottages livin' throughout the woods."'
L01FA:	db	00
L01FB:	db	'Yew'
L01FE:	db	00
L01FF:	db	'forest'
L0205:	db	00
L0206:	db	'"I am afraid, '
L0214:	db	00
L0215:	db	', that I know no one in this area. But," he adds proudly, "I'
	db	' do know 'oo runs the sawmill in Minoc. I also know that mon'
	db	'ks reside in the abbey, next to the high court."'
L02BD:	db	00
L02BE:	db	'high court'
L02C8:	db	00
L02C9:	db	'sawmill'
L02D0:	db	00
L02D1:	db	'forest'
L02D7:	db	00
L02D8:	db	'sawmill'
L02DF:	db	00
L02E0:	db	'"The sawyer there is named William."'
L0304:	db	00
L0305:	db	'sawmill'
L030C:	db	00
L030D:	db	'high court'
L0317:	db	00
L0318:	db	'"'Tis in the building just northeast of the Brotherhood. I k'
	db	'now they keep prisoners there."'
L0373:	db	00
L0374:	db	'high court'
L037E:	db	00
L037F:	db	'Silverleaf'
L0389:	db	00
L038A:	db	'"Why, yes, '
L0395:	db	00
L0396:	db	', I cut down Silverleaf trees. They only grow in one area, s'
	db	'o I 'afta travel quite a distance when I needs some of their'
	db	' wood. Why dost thou ask, '
L0428:	db	00
L0429:	db	'?~~"Oh, I see," he grins, "Thou wants some for thyself, ay?"'
L0465:	db	00
L0466:	db	'"I am sorry, '
L0473:	db	00
L0474:	db	', I do not know 'ow to prepare it. Perhaps thou shouldst try'
	db	' a pub."'
L04B8:	db	00
L04B9:	db	'"Thou'st got another reason for askin'?"'
L04E1:	db	00
L04E2:	db	'Emps'
L04E6:	db	00
L04E7:	db	'"All right, '
L04F3:	db	00
L04F4:	db	'," he shrugs.'
L0501:	db	00
L0502:	db	'one area'
L050A:	db	00
L050B:	db	'Silverleaf'
L0515:	db	00
L0516:	db	'one area'
L051E:	db	00
L051F:	db	'"They mainly populate the east part o' the Great Forest, way'
	db	' on the other side."'
L056F:	db	00
L0570:	db	'one area'
L0578:	db	00
L0579:	db	'Emps'
L057D:	db	00
L057E:	db	'"What in the bloody 'ell are emps?"~~After you quickly expla'
	db	'in the Silverleaf Tree situation to him, he exclaims, "Oh, w'
	db	'ell, that's 'orrible. I did not realize anyone -- er -- any '
	db	'other creature used the Silverleaf trees. What	kin I do abou'
	db	't it?"'
L0674:	db	00
L0675:	db	'sign contract'
L0682:	db	00
L0683:	db	'Emps'
L0687:	db	00
L0688:	db	'sign contract'
L0695:	db	00
L0696:	db	'"Why, o' course I'll sign. No more Silverleaf trees for me."'
L06D2:	db	00
L06D3:	db	'He takes the contract from you and signs it.'
L06FF:	db	00
L0700:	db	'He turns to Trellek. "Please apologize to thy kindred for me'
	db	'. I never meant to destroy thine 'omes. Friends, ay?"~~ Trel'
	db	'lek smiles and nods.'
L078C:	db	00
L078D:	db	'"And please apologize to the Emps for me, '
L07B7:	db	00
L07B8:	db	'. I never meant to destroy their 'omes."'
L07E0:	db	00
L07E1:	db	'"Well, I would sign it, but it seems thou hast lost it. If t'
	db	'hou dost find it again I will be more than happy to help the'
	db	'e and the Emps."'
L0869:	db	00
L086A:	db	'sign contract'
L0877:	db	00
L0878:	db	'bye'
L087B:	db	00
L087C:	db	'"G'bye, '
L0884:	db	00
L0885:	db	'. Pleasant journeys, ay."*'
