		.data
L0000:	db	'bye'
L0003:	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
L0007:	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
L000C:	db	00
L000D:	db	'Sprellic'
L0015:	db	00
L0016:	db	'false flag'
L0020:	db	00
L0021:	db	'You see a battle-scarred old soldier.'
L0046:	db	00
L0047:	db	'"Greetings!" says Kliftin. "Hast thou gotten into any scrape'
	db	's lately?"'
L008D:	db	00
L008E:	db	'name'
L0092:	db	00
L0093:	db	'"I am Kliftin."'
L00A2:	db	00
L00A3:	db	'name'
L00A7:	db	00
L00A8:	db	'job'
L00AB:	db	00
L00AC:	db	'"In my day I was a pretty damned good soldier. Now I am the '
	db	'master of the Armoury here in Jhelom."'
L010E:	db	00
L010F:	db	'buy'
L0112:	db	00
L0113:	db	'Jhelom'
L0119:	db	00
L011A:	db	'Armoury'
L0121:	db	00
L0122:	db	'soldier'
L0129:	db	00
L012A:	db	'buy'
L012D:	db	00
L012E:	db	'"I sell armour and weapons here. I have something to meet th'
	db	'ine every need. Dost thou wish to see armour or weapons?"'
L01A3:	db	00
L01A4:	db	'weapons'
L01AB:	db	00
L01AC:	db	'armour'
L01B2:	db	00
L01B3:	db	'"My shop is presently closed for business, but do return aga'
	db	'in, '
L01F3:	db	00
L01F4:	db	'."'
L01F6:	db	00
L01F7:	db	'buy'
L01FA:	db	00
L01FB:	db	'armour'
L0201:	db	00
L0202:	db	'weapons'
L0209:	db	00
L020A:	db	'soldier'
L0211:	db	00
L0212:	db	'"Surely thou dost not want to listen to old war stories?! I '
	db	'have seen my share of death and destruction. Leave it at tha'
	db	't."'
L028D:	db	00
L028E:	db	'soldier'
L0295:	db	00
L0296:	db	'Armoury'
L029D:	db	00
L029E:	db	'"I sell and collect weapons of all types. Business is always'
	db	' excellent, although my best customers keep getting killed i'
	db	'n duels!"'
L031F:	db	00
L0320:	db	'Armoury'
L0327:	db	00
L0328:	db	'buy'
L032B:	db	00
L032C:	db	'duels'
L0331:	db	00
L0332:	db	'Jhelom'
L0338:	db	00
L0339:	db	'"Jhelom is a rough place. If thou dost not like trouble then'
	db	' I can think of many better places for thee to be than here.'
	db	'"'
L03B2:	db	00
L03B3:	db	'Jhelom'
L03B9:	db	00
L03BA:	db	'duels'
L03BF:	db	00
L03C0:	db	'"Every day at noon in the Town Square people come to settle '
	db	'their differences. They fight to the blood or to the death. '
	db	'It is a madness! Like that Sprellic fellow for instance."'
L0471:	db	00
L0472:	db	'duels'
L0477:	db	00
L0478:	db	'Sprellic'
L0480:	db	00
L0481:	db	'Sprellic'
L0489:	db	00
L048A:	db	'"Sprellic, our rather mild-mannered innkeeper, stole the hon'
	db	'or flag from the wall of the Library of Scars and refused to'
	db	' return it. Now he must fight three of our best local fighte'
	db	'rs in a duel to the death."'
L0559:	db	00
L055A:	db	'fighters'
L0562:	db	00
L0563:	db	'You relate Sprellic's story to the old man who listens inten'
	db	'tly. "It sounds to me like the work of Sullivan, the Trickst'
	db	'er. He is a legendary thief and swindler who has never once '
	db	'been caught! Indeed, few even believe he actually exists. Th'
	db	'ou shalt not be able to dissuade the duellists with a tale l'
	db	'ike that."'
L0699:	db	00
L069A:	db	'dissuade'
L06A2:	db	00
L06A3:	db	'"It is good of thee to help that poor Sprellic fellow in his'
	db	' hour of need."'
L06EE:	db	00
L06EF:	db	'Sprellic'
L06F7:	db	00
L06F8:	db	'fighters'
L0700:	db	00
L0701:	db	'"Thou canst ask about the entire matter at the pub if thou d'
	db	'ost wish to know more about it."'
L075D:	db	00
L075E:	db	'fighters'
L0766:	db	00
L0767:	db	'dissuade'
L076F:	db	00
L0770:	db	'"The only thing that can dissuade them from wanting to kill '
	db	'poor Sprellic is to return the honor flag! It must have been'
	db	' taken away by Sullivan, but the duellists do not know that!'
	db	' If we had a duplicate of the honor flag we could give them '
	db	'that instead!"'
L086E:	db	00
L086F:	db	'dissuade'
L0877:	db	00
L0878:	db	'duplicate'
L0881:	db	00
L0882:	db	'duplicate'
L088B:	db	00
L088C:	db	'"In my day I was fairly handy at stitching wounds... Hmmm, p'
	db	'erhaps I can make a duplicate of the honor flag. The decepti'
	db	'on only has to work long enough for them to formally call of'
	db	'f the duel."'
L094C:	db	00
L094D:	db	'duplicate'
L0956:	db	00
L0957:	db	'sewing'
L095D:	db	00
L095E:	db	'deception'
L0967:	db	00
L0968:	db	'sewing'
L096E:	db	00
L096F:	db	'"I stitched so many of my comrades back together after all t'
	db	'he battles I fought in. Now that I am retired, sewing has so'
	db	'rt of become mine hobby." He looks at you with a little emba'
	db	'rrassment. "There is nothing wrong with that!"'
L0A51:	db	00
L0A52:	db	'sewing'
L0A58:	db	00
L0A59:	db	'deception'
L0A62:	db	00
L0A63:	db	'"Even if they notice that it is not their true honor flag th'
	db	'ey would never admit it. To do so would make them look fooli'
	db	'sh. They would rather simply challenge anyone who might say '
	db	'it is not their honor flag to yet another	duel! But let us d'
	db	'eal with one duel at a time here."'
L0B75:	db	00
L0B76:	db	'deception'
L0B7F:	db	00
L0B80:	db	'honor flag'
L0B8A:	db	00
L0B8B:	db	'honor flag'
L0B95:	db	00
L0B96:	db	'"Dost thou want me to make an honor flag that can be given t'
	db	'o the Library of Scars so the duels can be stopped?"'
L0C06:	db	00
L0C07:	db	'"Then thou must be sure to come pick it up from me before th'
	db	'ou dost go to the Duelling Area. It is the area outside my s'
	db	'hop next to the Library of Scars. I had best get busy if I a'
	db	'm to have it finished in time! Please return to my shop in a'
	db	' few hours."*'
L0D04:	db	00
L0D05:	db	'"Then thou must be sure to come pick it up from me before Sp'
	db	'rellic goes to the Duelling Area. I had best get busy if I a'
	db	'm to have it finished in time. Please return to my shop in a'
	db	' few hours."*'
L0DC6:	db	00
L0DC7:	db	'"Thou dost wish to deal with the Library of Scars personally'
	db	'? Very well then, but be warned -- the only type of honor th'
	db	'ey believe in is victory."'
L0E59:	db	00
L0E5A:	db	'"How canst thou have the key to saving Sprellic's life in th'
	db	'ine hand and do nothing as he faces certain death?!"'
L0ECA:	db	00
L0ECB:	db	'honor flag'
L0ED5:	db	00
L0ED6:	db	'false flag'
L0EE0:	db	00
L0EE1:	db	'"Disturb me not! The flag is not finished! Come to my shop l'
	db	'ater."'
L0F23:	db	00
L0F24:	db	'"Here is the imitation I have made of the Library of Scars' '
	db	'honor flag."'
L0F6C:	db	00
L0F6D:	db	'"The time for the duels must be drawing near. Good luck to S'
	db	'prellic, and to thee as well!"'
L0FC7:	db	00
L0FC8:	db	'"Thou must put something down if thou art to carry the flag!'
	db	'"'
L1005:	db	00
L1006:	db	'false flag'
L1010:	db	00
L1011:	db	'bye'
L1014:	db	00
L1015:	db	'"Good day."*'
L1021:	db	00
L1022:	db	'@Fine arms and armour for sale!@'
L1042:	db	00
L1043:	db	'@Just look at this fine armoury!@'
L1064:	db	00
L1065:	db	'@I have the fiercest weapons!@'
L1083:	db	00
L1084:	db	'@I have the strongest armour!@'
L10A2:	db	00
