L000C:	db	00
L000D:	db	'A pretty woman gives you a friendly grin and then coyly turn'
	db	's her eyes away from you.'
L0062:	db	00
L0063:	db	'"I bid thee welcome once again, '
L0083:	db	00
L0084:	db	'," says Ophelia.'
L0094:	db	00
L0095:	db	'Cosmo'
L009A:	db	00
L009B:	db	'Sprellic'
L00A3:	db	00
L00A4:	db	'winnings'
L00AC:	db	00
L00AD:	db	'Sprellic dead'
L00BA:	db	00
L00BB:	db	'Sprellic'
L00C3:	db	00
L00C4:	db	'name'
L00C8:	db	00
L00C9:	db	'"My name is Ophelia, '
L00DE:	db	00
L00DF:	db	'."'
L00E1:	db	00
L00E2:	db	'name'
L00E6:	db	00
L00E7:	db	'job'
L00EA:	db	00
L00EB:	db	'"I am a barmaid. I do most of the work at The Bunk and Stool'
	db	' here in Jhelom."'
L0138:	db	00
L0139:	db	'Jhelom'
L013F:	db	00
L0140:	db	'Bunk and Stool'
L014E:	db	00
L014F:	db	'work'
L0153:	db	00
L0154:	db	'work'
L0158:	db	00
L0159:	db	'"Ever since Sprellic, the owner, was challenged to those due'
	db	'ls by the three students at the Library of Scars, he has bee'
	db	'n busy preparing himself. I have been running the place all '
	db	'by myself... although Daphne has been helping me, I suppose.'
	db	'"'
L024A:	db	00
L024B:	db	'work'
L024F:	db	00
L0250:	db	'Daphne'
L0256:	db	00
L0257:	db	'Library'
L025E:	db	00
L025F:	db	'Sprellic'
L0267:	db	00
L0268:	db	'Daphne'
L026E:	db	00
L026F:	db	'"Honestly, I cannot imagine why thou wouldst be interested i'
	db	'n her." She lets out a throaty laugh.*'
L02D1:	db	00
L02D2:	db	'"I heard that, Ophelia. Thou art a spiteful wench!"*'
L0306:	db	00
L0307:	db	'"Now, now, Daphne. Temper, Temper! We don't want to scare of'
	db	'f the patrons with a poor disposition in addition to a poor '
	db	'face!"*'
L0386:	db	00
L0387:	db	'"Witch!"*'
L0390:	db	00
L0391:	db	'Daphne'
L0397:	db	00
L0398:	db	'Bunk and Stool'
L03A6:	db	00
L03A7:	db	'"'Tis said that indeed many strange things happen at this ba'
	db	'r. As of late, in addition to being an inn and a pub, where '
	db	'thou mayest buy fine food and drink, it has become a betting'
	db	' parlor."'
L0464:	db	00
L0465:	db	'Bunk and Stool'
L0473:	db	00
L0474:	db	'betting'
L047B:	db	00
L047C:	db	'room'
L0480:	db	00
L0481:	db	'food'
L0485:	db	00
L0486:	db	'strange'
L048D:	db	00
L048E:	db	'Jhelom'
L0494:	db	00
L0495:	db	'"It is a pretty rough place to work, but," she whispers to y'
	db	'ou in confidence, "I must confess I find myself attracted to'
	db	' the type of men that live here."'
L052E:	db	00
L052F:	db	'Jhelom'
L0535:	db	00
L0536:	db	'Library'
L053D:	db	00
L053E:	db	'"Surely thou hast heard of our famous school for fighters by'
	db	' now! What kind of a world traveller art thou? Do not answer'
	db	'. 'Twas a rhetorical question," she sniffs.'
L05E1:	db	00
L05E2:	db	'Library'
L05E9:	db	00
L05EA:	db	'food'
L05EE:	db	00
L05EF:	db	'"Thou shalt have to see Daphne about that. Thou wouldst not '
	db	'expect me to have to go into the kitchen?" Ophelia laughs.'
L0665:	db	00
L0666:	db	'food'
L066A:	db	00
L066B:	db	'room'
L066F:	db	00
L0670:	db	'"For naught more than 5 gold thou canst get a lovely room. D'
	db	'ost thou wish to stay the night?"'
L06CD:	db	00
L06CE:	db	'"Here is thy key. Be warned, 'twill only work in this establ'
	db	'ishment, and only for one use."'
L0729:	db	00
L072A:	db	'"Sorry, '
L0732:	db	00
L0733:	db	', thou must lose some weight, er, some bundles, before I can'
	db	' give thee the room key."'
L0788:	db	00
L0789:	db	'"I am truly sorry, '
L079C:	db	00
L079D:	db	', but the rooms cost more gold than thou hast."'
L07CC:	db	00
L07CD:	db	'"Our rooms are not good enough, I suppose," she says, scowli'
	db	'ng.'
L080C:	db	00
L080D:	db	'"Right now I am not at work so please do not address me as i'
	db	'f I were."'
L0853:	db	00
L0854:	db	'room'
L0858:	db	00
L0859:	db	'Sprellic'
L0861:	db	00
L0862:	db	'"No one knows old Sprellic better than myself. Although he d'
	db	'oes not look it, he may well be the deadliest fighting maste'
	db	'r in all of Britannia."'
L08F1:	db	00
L08F2:	db	'Sprellic'
L08FA:	db	00
L08FB:	db	'master'
L0901:	db	00
L0902:	db	'master'
L0908:	db	00
L0909:	db	'"After he defeats the fighters of the Library of Scars, he m'
	db	'ay open his own school teaching his own unique style of figh'
	db	'ting."'
L0987:	db	00
L0988:	db	'master'
L098E:	db	00
L098F:	db	'school'
L0995:	db	00
L0996:	db	'school'
L099C:	db	00
L099D:	db	'"It will be a great fighting school. Already, fighting men a'
	db	'nd women are coming to Jhelom to become Sprellic's students.'
	db	' They all long to know the secret that I can tell thee right'
	db	' now."'
L0A57:	db	00
L0A58:	db	'school'
L0A5E:	db	00
L0A5F:	db	'secret'
L0A65:	db	00
L0A66:	db	'secret'
L0A6C:	db	00
L0A6D:	db	'Ophelia motions you closer to her. She whispers to you. "Spr'
	db	'ellic is really the Avatar returned to us after all these ye'
	db	'ars." She nods solemnly.'
L0AFD:	db	00
L0AFE:	db	'Ophelia motions you closer to her. She whispers to you. "Spr'
	db	'ellic can call upon the Avatar to come and be his champion."'
	db	' She nods solemnly.'
L0B89:	db	00
L0B8A:	db	'secret'
L0B90:	db	00
L0B91:	db	'strange'
L0B98:	db	00
L0B99:	db	'"In case thou hast not noticed, this is a rough town. We see'
	db	' all types of odd characters in this place." She looks you o'
	db	'ver carefully.'
L0C1F:	db	00
L0C20:	db	'strange'
L0C27:	db	00
L0C28:	db	'betting'
L0C2F:	db	00
L0C30:	db	'"Sorry, all bets are off, due to the... er, unfortunate pass'
	db	'ing on of one or more of the parties involved."'
L0C9B:	db	00
L0C9C:	db	'"I am taking wagers on Sprellic's duels. Wouldst thou like t'
	db	'o place a bet?"'
L0CE7:	db	00
L0CE8:	db	'"How much wouldst thou like to bet that Sprellic defeats all'
	db	' three of his challengers?"'
L0D3F:	db	00
L0D40:	db	'"Perhaps thou art not truly serious about thy convictions. M'
	db	'ayhaps Daphne will take thy line of bets."'
L0DA6:	db	00
L0DA7:	db	'"Thou wouldst bet '
L0DB9:	db	00
L0DBA:	db	' gold that Sprellic will win?"'
L0DD8:	db	00
L0DD9:	db	'"Very well. How much wouldst thou like to bet?"'
L0E08:	db	00
L0E09:	db	'"Very well. Let me give thee markers for thy gold. Each one '
	db	'is worth 10 gold coins. If Sprellic wins, thou mayest come c'
	db	'ollect twice that amount of gold from me.~~"Should he lose, '
L0EBD:	db	00
L0EBE:	db	', thy markers are, of course, worthless."'
L0EE7:	db	00
L0EE8:	db	'"I shall soon see thee again, '
L0F06:	db	00
L0F07:	db	'." You notice she is suppressing a tiny giggle. "When thou d'
	db	'ost return to collect thy winnings." For a moment it seems s'
	db	'he cannot make eye contact with you.'
L0FA3:	db	00
L0FA4:	db	'"Thou must return later when thou hast enough room in thy pa'
	db	'ck for these markers."'
L0FF6:	db	00
L0FF7:	db	'"Thou hast not the amount of gold thou dost want to bet! Art'
	db	' thou trying to swindle me?"'
L104F:	db	00
L1050:	db	'"Then if thou wouldst like to bet against Sprellic, thou may'
	db	'est see Daphne, but I warn thee thou wilt be throwing thy mo'
	db	'ney away!"'
L10D2:	db	00
L10D3:	db	'betting'
L10DA:	db	00
L10DB:	db	'winnings'
L10E3:	db	00
L10E4:	db	'"I see thou hast returned to collect thy winnings." She shru'
	db	'gs and pays them to you.'
L1138:	db	00
L1139:	db	'"Thou cannot carry that much gold! Return later when thou ca'
	db	'nst take all thy winnings at one time!"'
L119C:	db	00
L119D:	db	'"Thou hast already collected thy winnings!"'
L11C8:	db	00
L11C9:	db	'winnings'
L11D1:	db	00
L11D2:	db	'Cosmo'
L11D7:	db	00
L11D8:	db	'"Who? Oh, he is a local boy who comes in here and moons over'
	db	' me on occasion. Do not concern thyself with him. I do not."'
L1250:	db	00
L1251:	db	'"Why what kind of way is that to speak of he who will soon b'
	db	'ecome thy betrothed! Finally, I can make thee move out of mi'
	db	'ne house! Every moment of sharing my life with thee has been'
	db	' intolerable!"*'
L1314:	db	00
L1315:	db	'"Do not get thine hopes up yet, my dear Daphne! I have put a'
	db	' condition on our marriage and poor Cosmo will never be able'
	db	' to fulfill it!"'
L139D:	db	00
L139E:	db	'"Thou dost never know! The thought of thee in thy wedding go'
	db	'wn with thy groom Cosmo at thy side is simply delicious! Per'
	db	'haps he is the man who will finally teach thee to be a lady '
	db	'at last!"'
L145B:	db	00
L145C:	db	'Cosmo'
L1461:	db	00
L1462:	db	'Sprellic dead'
L146F:	db	00
L1470:	db	'"Hmpf! If thou didst bet against him, then I suppose thou sh'
	db	'alt be rich! I wouldst bet that thou wert the one who killed'
	db	' him, too!"'
