L001D:	db	00
L001E:	db	'"Art thou ready to pay thy bill?"'
L003F:	db	00
L0040:	db	'"Goodbye, then!"*'
L0051:	db	00
L0052:	db	'You see a leering, ill-postured man who chortles to himself.'
L008E:	db	00
L008F:	db	'"Well if it isn't Dupre! -Sir- Dupre now, is it?"'
L00C0:	db	00
L00C1:	db	'"That it is, Boris."'
L00D5:	db	00
L00D6:	db	'"Hmmm-- it seems to me thou dost have a tab still going here'
	db	'? Yes?"'
L0119:	db	00
L011A:	db	'"Oh? Do I?"'
L0125:	db	00
L0126:	db	'"Yes indeed! Let me see... I believe the total that thou dos'
	db	't owe is 74 gold pieces. I am afraid that thou must pay up b'
	db	'efore I can speak with thee or anyone else with thee."'
L01D4:	db	00
L01D5:	db	'Dupre looks embarrassed. He turns to you. "My friend, wilt t'
	db	'hou help me out?"'
L0222:	db	00
L0223:	db	'"I thank thee, Avatar."'
L023A:	db	00
L023B:	db	'You hand the gold over to Boris.'
L025B:	db	00
L025C:	db	'"'Tis a pleasure to do business with thee, Sir Dupre! And we'
	db	'lcome to my pub!"'
L02A9:	db	00
L02AA:	db	'"Hmmm, where did our gold go?"*'
L02C9:	db	00
L02CA:	db	'"I am afraid are pockets are too empty!"*'
L02F3:	db	00
L02F4:	db	'"Well, I wilt not be serving thee or speaking to thee until '
	db	'thy bill is paid!"*'
L0343:	db	00
L0344:	db	'"Hello again," says Boris.'
L035E:	db	00
L035F:	db	'name'
L0363:	db	00
L0364:	db	'"Call me Boris."'
L0374:	db	00
L0375:	db	'name'
L0379:	db	00
L037A:	db	'job'
L037D:	db	00
L037E:	db	'"I run The Modest Damsel, here in New Magincia."'
L03AE:	db	00
L03AF:	db	'New Magincia'
L03BB:	db	00
L03BC:	db	'Modest Damsel'
L03C9:	db	00
L03CA:	db	'Modest Damsel'
L03D7:	db	00
L03D8:	db	'"It is a little inn and tavern. I am the owner, along with m'
	db	'y wife, Magenta. Wouldst thou like something to eat or drink'
	db	', or perhaps a room?"'
L0465:	db	00
L0466:	db	'room'
L046A:	db	00
L046B:	db	'eat or drink'
L0477:	db	00
L0478:	db	'Magenta'
L047F:	db	00
L0480:	db	'"The Modest Damsel is now closed for business. But do please'
	db	' return during business hours."'
L04DB:	db	00
L04DC:	db	'Modest Damsel'
L04E9:	db	00
L04EA:	db	'Magenta'
L04F1:	db	00
L04F2:	db	'"She became the mayor of New Magincia after the death of the'
	db	' old mayor, her father, several years ago. She has done such'
	db	' a good job that no one has opposed her for the position yet'
	db	'."'
L05A8:	db	00
L05A9:	db	'Magenta'
L05B0:	db	00
L05B1:	db	'eat or drink'
L05BD:	db	00
L05BE:	db	'"I am certain thou wilt enjoy our food and drink."'
L05F0:	db	00
L05F1:	db	'room'
L05F5:	db	00
L05F6:	db	'"Why dost thou not stay the night? For but 3 gold thou canst'
	db	' let one of our rooms. Dost thou wish to stay the night?"'
L066B:	db	00
L066C:	db	'"Here is thy room key. 'Twill only work in this inn."'
L06A1:	db	00
L06A2:	db	'"Sorry, '
L06AA:	db	00
L06AB:	db	', thou must remove some of thy load before I can give thee t'
	db	'he room key."'
L06F4:	db	00
L06F5:	db	'"Thou hast not enough gold for my rooms."'
L071E:	db	00
L071F:	db	'"Some other evening, perhaps."'
L073D:	db	00
L073E:	db	'room'
L0742:	db	00
L0743:	db	'New Magincia'
L074F:	db	00
L0750:	db	'"In all of Britannia thou shalt not find a place that change'
	db	's so little. Even the people always seem the same."'
L07BF:	db	00
L07C0:	db	'people'
L07C6:	db	00
L07C7:	db	'New Magincia'
L07D3:	db	00
L07D4:	db	'people'
L07DA:	db	00
L07DB:	db	'"There are merchants and laborers, as well as a few new folk'
	db	's."'
L081A:	db	00
L081B:	db	'new folks'
L0824:	db	00
L0825:	db	'laborers'
L082D:	db	00
L082E:	db	'merchants'
L0837:	db	00
L0838:	db	'people'
L083E:	db	00
L083F:	db	'merchants'
L0848:	db	00
L0849:	db	'"They would be Russell, the shipwright; Henry, the peddler; '
	db	'and Sam, the flower man."'
L089E:	db	00
L089F:	db	'Sam'
L08A2:	db	00
L08A3:	db	'Henry'
L08A8:	db	00
L08A9:	db	'Russell'
L08B0:	db	00
L08B1:	db	'merchants'
L08BA:	db	00
L08BB:	db	'laborers'
L08C3:	db	00
L08C4:	db	'"They would be Katrina, the shepherd, and Constance, the wat'
	db	'er carrier."'
L090C:	db	00
L090D:	db	'Constance'
L0916:	db	00
L0917:	db	'Katrina'
L091E:	db	00
L091F:	db	'laborers'
L0927:	db	00
L0928:	db	'new folks'
L0931:	db	00
L0932:	db	'"Except for the three strangers, the only relatively new per'
	db	'son on the island is Alagner, the sage."'
L0996:	db	00
L0997:	db	'strangers'
L09A0:	db	00
L09A1:	db	'Alagner'
L09A8:	db	00
L09A9:	db	'new folks'
L09B2:	db	00
L09B3:	db	'Alagner'
L09BA:	db	00
L09BB:	db	'"Alagner is not from New Magincia, of course, but has settle'
	db	'd here after studying the world, for he well knows the value'
	db	' of our peace and solitude."'
L0A4F:	db	00
L0A50:	db	'Alagner'
L0A57:	db	00
L0A58:	db	'Russell'
L0A5F:	db	00
L0A60:	db	'"A brilliant artist and craftsman, Russell cares little for '
	db	'wealth or notoriety. He is content simply building his fine '
	db	'ships and watching them sail."'
L0AF6:	db	00
L0AF7:	db	'Russell'
L0AFE:	db	00
L0AFF:	db	'Katrina'
L0B06:	db	00
L0B07:	db	'"Katrina has come to the aid of the people of this town on m'
	db	'ore than one occasion. She gets an interesting smile on her '
	db	'face whenever thy name is mentioned."'
L0BA4:	db	00
L0BA5:	db	'"That is because the Avatar is one my dearest friends."'
L0BDC:	db	00
L0BDD:	db	'"Am I not one of thy dearest friends, Katrina?"'
L0C0C:	db	00
L0C0D:	db	'"Thou art a flirt, Boris! Dost Magenta know how thou dost wa'
	db	'nt to be dearest friends with the other women living on the '
	db	'island?"'
L0C8D:	db	00
L0C8E:	db	'"Thou dost torture me, Katrina!" He laughs.'
L0CB9:	db	00
L0CBA:	db	'Katrina'
L0CC1:	db	00
L0CC2:	db	'Henry'
L0CC7:	db	00
L0CC8:	db	'"Henry's parents were so poor it is a wonder he did not star'
	db	've to death. I think Constance kept him going. He has loved '
	db	'her since they were children."'
L0D5E:	db	00
L0D5F:	db	'Henry'
L0D64:	db	00
L0D65:	db	'Constance'
L0D6E:	db	00
L0D6F:	db	'"Constance is an orphan who was raised mostly by Katrina. He'
	db	'r innocence is surpassed only by her beauty. She is loved by'
	db	' all." Boris stares off into space for a few seconds before '
	db	'coming to his senses.'
L0E38:	db	00
L0E39:	db	'Constance'
L0E42:	db	00
L0E43:	db	'Sam'
L0E46:	db	00
L0E47:	db	'Boris laughs. "Thou wouldst have to meet Sam for thyself. He'
	db	' is an incredible person who is perfecting the art of enjoyi'
	db	'ng life."'
L0EC8:	db	00
L0EC9:	db	'Sam'
L0ECC:	db	00
L0ECD:	db	'strangers'
L0ED6:	db	00
L0ED7:	db	'"A shipwreck has brought three strangers to our island. Rumo'
	db	'r has it one of them is a monied gentleman from Buccaneer's '
	db	'Den, and the other two are his hired swords. They were in he'
	db	're drinking one night. They are not the sort of crowd I woul'
	db	'd wish to serve at mine establishment."'
L0FEE:	db	00
L0FEF:	db	'strangers'
L0FF8:	db	00
L0FF9:	db	'locket'
L0FFF:	db	00
L1000:	db	'"I do not wish to hear of that locket ever again! Do not spe'
	db	'ak to me of it!"'
L104C:	db	00
L104D:	db	'"I am quite certain I have never seen such a locket. I shall'
	db	' be happy to keep mine eyes open, though."'
L10B3:	db	00
L10B4:	db	'You tell Boris what you had heard from the pirate, Battles. '
	db	'He breaks out into a cold sweat. "Thou hast seen through my '
	db	'deception. I shall hand it over to thee." He opens a secret '
	db	'panel from behind the bar and looks inside. When he looks ba'
	db	'ck to you his face has lost all color. "The locket is gone! '
	db	'I swear to thee, I know not where it is!"'
L1209:	db	00
L120A:	db	'"I still have not been able to find the locket!" Boris looks'
	db	' as if he is about to tear his hair out, "But I will keep lo'
	db	'oking until I find it!"'
L1299:	db	00
L129A:	db	'locket'
L12A0:	db	00
L12A1:	db	'bye'
L12A4:	db	00
L12A5:	db	'"Good journey!"*'
L12B5:	db	00
