		.data
L0000:	db	'bye'
L0003:	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
L0007:	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
L000C:	db	00
L000D:	db	'strangers'
L0016:	db	00
L0017:	db	'scoundrels'
L0021:	db	00
L0022:	db	'locket found'
L002E:	db	00
L002F:	db	'You see an angelic young woman who gives you a smile of comp'
	db	'lete innocence.'
L007A:	db	00
L007B:	db	'"'
L007C:	db	00
L007D:	db	'!" says a wide-eyed Constance, "What may I do for thee?"'
L00B5:	db	00
L00B6:	db	'name'
L00BA:	db	00
L00BB:	db	'"My name, '
L00C5:	db	00
L00C6:	db	', is Constance." She shyly lowers her eyes.'
L00F1:	db	00
L00F2:	db	'name'
L00F6:	db	00
L00F7:	db	'job'
L00FA:	db	00
L00FB:	db	'"I carry water from the well of humility to all of the homes'
	db	' here in New Magincia."'
L014E:	db	00
L014F:	db	'New Magincia'
L015B:	db	00
L015C:	db	'well of humility'
L016C:	db	00
L016D:	db	'well of humility'
L017D:	db	00
L017E:	db	'"The water from the well is pure and cool. If thou wouldst l'
	db	'ike I will pour thee some."'
L01D5:	db	00
L01D6:	db	'With a big smile Constance takes a	dipper and submerges it i'
	db	'n the cool water of her bucket. She draws out the dipper and'
	db	' hands it to you. You drink and find the water delicious and'
	db	' very refreshing.'
L029B:	db	00
L029C:	db	'"Actually, I feel quite parched myself. Might I have some as'
	db	' well?" Constance nods yes, and hands him a	dipper of water.'
	db	' He drinks with loud gulping sounds.*'
L0339:	db	00
L033A:	db	'"I, too, am feeling dry. Wouldst thou share thy water with m'
	db	'e, milady?" Constance fills the dipper with water for Shamin'
	db	'o and he drinks until water runs down his chin.*'
L03E2:	db	00
L03E3:	db	'You see Shamino nudge Dupre. "Art thou not going to have a d'
	db	'rink?"'
L0425:	db	00
L0426:	db	'"I shall wait until we find something a bit stronger than wa'
	db	'ter to quench my thirst."*'
L047C:	db	00
L047D:	db	'Constance hands Spark a dipper full of water. He drinks it d'
	db	'own in one long slurp. Upon finishing it, he burps. With an	'
	db	'embarrassed grin he bows	apologetically to Constance	as he h'
	db	'ands her back the dipper.'
L054A:	db	00
L054B:	db	'"If thou wouldst ever change thy mind thou needest only let '
	db	'me know."'
L0590:	db	00
L0591:	db	'well of humility'
L05A1:	db	00
L05A2:	db	'strangers'
L05AB:	db	00
L05AC:	db	'"There are three strangers on the island! They have been shi'
	db	'pwrecked here! I have met them. Their leader's name is Robin'
	db	'."'
L0626:	db	00
L0627:	db	'Robin'
L062C:	db	00
L062D:	db	'strangers'
L0636:	db	00
L0637:	db	'New Magincia'
L0643:	db	00
L0644:	db	'"I was born in New Magincia and I have lived here mine entir'
	db	'e life. But now I wish to leave for mine heart hath been bro'
	db	'ken."'
L06C1:	db	00
L06C2:	db	'New Magincia'
L06CE:	db	00
L06CF:	db	'heart'
L06D4:	db	00
L06D5:	db	'heart'
L06DA:	db	00
L06DB:	db	'"Once I was in love with Henry, the peddler, but then I lear'
	db	'ned he is a liar and a cad. Perhaps soon mine heart shall be'
	db	'long to another."'
L0764:	db	00
L0765:	db	'another'
L076C:	db	00
L076D:	db	'You tell Constance of Robin's plans for her. She gives you a'
	db	' shocked look. "Many thanks. I now know that my rightful pla'
	db	'ce is with Henry."'
L07F7:	db	00
L07F8:	db	'heart'
L07FD:	db	00
L07FE:	db	'locket found'
L080A:	db	00
L080B:	db	'You tell Constance of how you have returned the locket that '
	db	'has been stolen from Henry. "Oh, how could I ever have doubt'
	db	'ed my dear darling Henry?" she frowns. "I thank thee for tel'
	db	'ling me the truth."'
L08D2:	db	00
L08D3:	db	'"Constance, I am sorry that things ran afoul as they did, bu'
	db	't if thou wilt, I would like thee to have this locket as a s'
	db	'ymbol of my love."*'
L095E:	db	00
L095F:	db	'"My sweet Henry, mine heart belongs to only thee."*'
L0992:	db	00
L0993:	db	'locket found'
L099F:	db	00
L09A0:	db	'another'
L09A7:	db	00
L09A8:	db	'"There is a charming and mysterious stranger on the island n'
	db	'amed Robin. He says one day he may show me the world and buy'
	db	' me many fine things." Constance sighs. "He even gave me som'
	db	'e lovely flowers."'
L0A6E:	db	00
L0A6F:	db	'another'
L0A76:	db	00
L0A77:	db	'Robin'
L0A7C:	db	00
L0A7D:	db	'Robin'
L0A82:	db	00
L0A83:	db	'"He is a wealthy man and his two friends are big, strong men'
	db	'. They have been telling me about a very wonderful-sounding '
	db	'place called Buccaneer's Den."'
L0B19:	db	00
L0B1A:	db	'Robin'
L0B1F:	db	00
L0B20:	db	'Buccaneer's Den'
L0B2F:	db	00
L0B30:	db	'friends'
L0B37:	db	00
L0B38:	db	'friends'
L0B3F:	db	00
L0B40:	db	'"Their names were Battles and Leavell. Both of them treated '
	db	'me like proper gentlemen."'
L0B96:	db	00
L0B97:	db	'friends'
L0B9E:	db	00
L0B9F:	db	'Leavell'
L0BA6:	db	00
L0BA7:	db	'Battles'
L0BAE:	db	00
L0BAF:	db	'Buccaneer's Den'
L0BBE:	db	00
L0BBF:	db	'"Buccaneer's Den must be a wonderland. There is a spinning w'
	db	'heel that gives thee money! Canst thou imagine! And opulent,'
	db	' luxurious baths."'
L0C49:	db	00
L0C4A:	db	'Buccaneer's Den'
L0C59:	db	00
L0C5A:	db	'baths'
L0C5F:	db	00
L0C60:	db	'spinning wheel'
L0C6E:	db	00
L0C6F:	db	'Battles'
L0C76:	db	00
L0C77:	db	'"Battles was quiet at first. I thought he was mean-looking, '
	db	'but he is nice once thou dost get to know him. He told me of'
	db	' the various monsters he fought, and exciting stories of how'
	db	' he raided ships in the south seas."'
L0D4F:	db	00
L0D50:	db	'Battles'
L0D57:	db	00
L0D58:	db	'Leavell'
L0D5F:	db	00
L0D60:	db	'"Leavell was charming and witty. He can always make me laugh'
	db	'."'
L0D9E:	db	00
L0D9F:	db	'Leavell'
L0DA6:	db	00
L0DA7:	db	'spinning wheel'
L0DB5:	db	00
L0DB6:	db	'"Well, they certainly have nothing like that in New Magincia'
	db	'. I had never even heard of such a thing before!"'
L0E23:	db	00
L0E24:	db	'spinning wheel'
L0E32:	db	00
L0E33:	db	'baths'
L0E38:	db	00
L0E39:	db	'"Doth that not sound nice?"'
L0E54:	db	00
L0E55:	db	'baths'
L0E5A:	db	00
L0E5B:	db	'scoundrels'
L0E65:	db	00
L0E66:	db	'You gently explain to Constance that Robin, Battles and Leav'
	db	'ell were scoundrels with intent to do her great harm. She is'
	db	' quite alarmed. Then you explain that they will not be troub'
	db	'ling her anymore. She thanks you.'
L0F3B:	db	00
L0F3C:	db	'scoundrels'
L0F46:	db	00
L0F47:	db	'bye'
L0F4A:	db	00
L0F4B:	db	'"It was a pleasure speaking with thee, '
L0F72:	db	00
L0F73:	db	'."*'
L0F76:	db	00
