		.data
L0000:	db	'bye'
L0003:	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
L0007:	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
L000C:	db	00
L000D:	db	'locket'
L0013:	db	00
L0014:	db	'show locket'
L001F:	db	00
L0020:	db	'Fellowship'
L002A:	db	00
L002B:	db	'You see a roguish man dressed in what appears to be some nob'
	db	'leman's ratty hand-me-downs.'
L0083:	db	00
L0084:	db	'strangers'
L008D:	db	00
L008E:	db	'"Greetings, and how may I be of service to thee?" asks Robin'
	db	'.'
L00CB:	db	00
L00CC:	db	'name'
L00D0:	db	00
L00D1:	db	'"My name, '
L00DB:	db	00
L00DC:	db	', is Robin. A pleasure to meet thee. I have come to New Magi'
	db	'ncia only recently."'
L012C:	db	00
L012D:	db	'name'
L0131:	db	00
L0132:	db	'New Magincia'
L013E:	db	00
L013F:	db	'job'
L0142:	db	00
L0143:	db	'"My father, a well-respected nobleman whose name I will not '
	db	'defame by mentioning, bastardized and disowned me. But he di'
	db	'd teach me mine occupation."'
L01D7:	db	00
L01D8:	db	'occupation'
L01E2:	db	00
L01E3:	db	'occupation'
L01ED:	db	00
L01EE:	db	'"Why, that most glamorous and respected of occupations, '
L0226:	db	00
L0227:	db	'. Winning at games of chance."'
L0245:	db	00
L0246:	db	'occupation'
L0250:	db	00
L0251:	db	'New Magincia'
L025D:	db	00
L025E:	db	'"I am not from here. My colleagues and I had to quickly leav'
	db	'e Buccaneer's Den after a dispute with the casino owner. And'
	db	' a rough voyage it was, too."'
L02F3:	db	00
L02F4:	db	'voyage'
L02FA:	db	00
L02FB:	db	'dispute'
L0302:	db	00
L0303:	db	'Buccaneer's Den'
L0312:	db	00
L0313:	db	'colleagues'
L031D:	db	00
L031E:	db	'New Magincia'
L032A:	db	00
L032B:	db	'colleagues'
L0335:	db	00
L0336:	db	'"My friends are Battles and Leavell. Their job is to protect'
	db	' me and my winnings. In exchange they share in my profits."'
L03AD:	db	00
L03AE:	db	'Leavell'
L03B5:	db	00
L03B6:	db	'Battles'
L03BD:	db	00
L03BE:	db	'colleagues'
L03C8:	db	00
L03C9:	db	'Battles'
L03D0:	db	00
L03D1:	db	'"I rescued him from his captain who was about to make him wa'
	db	'lk the plank. I diced with that Captain for the lad's life. '
	db	'Later, Battles led a mutiny that took the ship, and... well,'
	db	' that is another story."'
L049D:	db	00
L049E:	db	'Battles'
L04A5:	db	00
L04A6:	db	'Leavell'
L04AD:	db	00
L04AE:	db	'"I rescued him from a gaggle of angry noblemen's daughters w'
	db	'ho had just discovered he was courting all of them simultane'
	db	'ously. If not for me he would have certainly perished! But I'
	db	' am ahead of myself."'
L0577:	db	00
L0578:	db	'Leavell'
L057F:	db	00
L0580:	db	'Buccaneer's Den'
L058F:	db	00
L0590:	db	'"It is where we live most of the year. There are a lot of ro'
	db	'ugh characters there and it is not a place to be seen carryi'
	db	'ng large amounts of money."'
L0623:	db	00
L0624:	db	'rough characters'
L0634:	db	00
L0635:	db	'Buccaneer's Den'
L0644:	db	00
L0645:	db	'dispute'
L064C:	db	00
L064D:	db	'"I won a vulgar amount of the casino's gold and 'The Mister''
	db	' of the place, Gordy, accused me of cheating. He sent his le'
	db	'gbreaker, Sintag, after us. Pirates do not like to lose!"'
L06FE:	db	00
L06FF:	db	'dispute'
L0706:	db	00
L0707:	db	'The Mister'
L0711:	db	00
L0712:	db	'The Mister'
L071C:	db	00
L071D:	db	'"Do not ask me why he is called that! Everyone there calls h'
	db	'im that, though!"'
L076A:	db	00
L076B:	db	'The Mister'
L0775:	db	00
L0776:	db	'voyage'
L077C:	db	00
L077D:	db	'"We took the first ship out, but before we got back to the m'
	db	'ainland it had sunk. The three of us barely managed to make '
	db	'it to New Magincia with our lives. Now we are marooned here.'
	db	'"'
L0832:	db	00
L0833:	db	'voyage'
L0839:	db	00
L083A:	db	'marooned'
L0842:	db	00
L0843:	db	'strangers'
L084C:	db	00
L084D:	db	'"I do not know of any. I only just arrived here myself."'
L0885:	db	00
L0886:	db	'strangers'
L088F:	db	00
L0890:	db	'rough characters'
L08A0:	db	00
L08A1:	db	'"One rough character in particular to stay away from is a ma'
	db	'n called Hook. He would kill thee for a trifle. Thou canst t'
	db	'ell him by the hook he has for a hand."'
L0940:	db	00
L0941:	db	'Hook'
L0945:	db	00
L0946:	db	'rough characters'
L0956:	db	00
L0957:	db	'Hook'
L095B:	db	00
L095C:	db	'"I know nothing more. If thou thinkest that I would willingl'
	db	'y cross paths with the likes of him thou must have me mistak'
	db	'en for someone else!"'
L09E9:	db	00
L09EA:	db	'Hook'
L09EE:	db	00
L09EF:	db	'locket'
L09F5:	db	00
L09F6:	db	'"We are trying to return to Buccaneer's Den. I was hoping to'
	db	' sell a gold locket which came into my possession to buy our'
	db	' passage back, but I fear it is lost. If thou dost come acro'
	db	'ss it be sure to let me know."'
L0AC8:	db	00
L0AC9:	db	'locket'
L0ACF:	db	00
L0AD0:	db	'Fellowship'
L0ADA:	db	00
L0ADB:	db	'"Thou art a member of The Fellowship! For years I have been '
	db	'seeing Fellowship members winning heavy stakes at the House '
	db	'of Games. Canst thou tell me their secret?"'
L0B7E:	db	00
L0B7F:	db	'"Of course thou canst. But I do not suspect that thou wilt."'
	db	' Robin shrugs his shoulders.'
L0BD7:	db	00
L0BD8:	db	'"Forgive me if I do not believe thee."'
L0BFE:	db	00
L0BFF:	db	'Fellowship'
L0C09:	db	00
L0C0A:	db	'marooned'
L0C12:	db	00
L0C13:	db	'"That is right. We cannot afford the stinking ship sold by t'
	db	'he shipwright.'
L0C5D:	db	00
L0C5E:	db	'"But say, thou must have gotten here in some manner! Dost th'
	db	'ou have some manner of ship on which we could leave the isla'
	db	'nd?"'
L0CDA:	db	00
L0CDB:	db	'"I could pay thee well if thou wouldst	take us back to Bucca'
	db	'neer's Den."'
L0D23:	db	00
L0D24:	db	'pay'
L0D27:	db	00
L0D28:	db	'"If thou shouldst come across a way off this island please p'
	db	'ermit us to leave with thee."'
L0D81:	db	00
L0D82:	db	'marooned'
L0D8A:	db	00
L0D8B:	db	'pay'
L0D8E:	db	00
L0D8F:	db	'"Of course, I cannot pay thee right now at this moment.	But '
	db	'when we reach Buccaneer's Den, I promise thee, I shall be ab'
	db	'le to get mine hands on a lot of money."'
L0E2F:	db	00
L0E30:	db	'pay'
L0E33:	db	00
L0E34:	db	'money'
L0E39:	db	00
L0E3A:	db	'money'
L0E3F:	db	00
L0E40:	db	'"Yes, money! For I have found something here in New Magincia'
	db	' that will be worth more than gold in Buccaneer's Den."'
L0EB3:	db	00
L0EB4:	db	'money'
L0EB9:	db	00
L0EBA:	db	'something'
L0EC3:	db	00
L0EC4:	db	'something'
L0ECD:	db	00
L0ECE:	db	'"Before I tell thee what it is, wilt thou promise to take me'
	db	' and my mates back to Buccaneer's Den?"'
L0F31:	db	00
L0F32:	db	'Robin looks you in the eye. "Thou art truly a kind friend. I'
	db	' suppose then I should tell thee what it is we are planning '
	db	'on bringing back from New Magincia."'
L0FCE:	db	00
L0FCF:	db	'bringing back'
L0FDC:	db	00
L0FDD:	db	'"Then I cannot trust thee enough to tell thee of my plans. G'
	db	'o away."'
L1021:	db	00
L1022:	db	'something'
L102B:	db	00
L102C:	db	'bringing back'
L1039:	db	00
L103A:	db	'"Since thou art truly a friend then I know that I can ask a '
	db	'favor of thee. Why dost thou not bring back that lost locket'
	db	' to me and we shall speak of these things some more." He fla'
	db	'shes you a wicked grin.'
L1105:	db	00
L1106:	db	'"Since thou hast brought my locket back here, I suppose that'
	db	' I can trust thee. I intend to take Constance back with us a'
	db	'nd sell her to the operator of the baths."'
L11A8:	db	00
L11A9:	db	'bringing back'
L11B6:	db	00
L11B7:	db	'show locket'
L11C2:	db	00
L11C3:	db	'"Now that I know I can trust thee, I can let thee in on our '
	db	'plan. I intend to take another passenger in thy boat back wi'
	db	'th us to Buccaneer's Den. Her name is Constance and she shou'
	db	'ld fetch a goodly price from Glenno, operator of the baths. '
	db	'Enough to pay my debts, pay thee for passage and still have '
	db	'plenty left over for another go at the House of Games!"'
L1326:	db	00
L1327:	db	'boat'
L132B:	db	00
L132C:	db	'show locket'
L1337:	db	00
L1338:	db	'boat'
L133C:	db	00
L133D:	db	'"Thou must get thy boat ready to leave this place immediatel'
	db	'y. My lads and I shall get Constance and then we shall join '
	db	'thee. But wilt thou tell me where thy boat is located?"'
L13EC:	db	00
L13ED:	db	'You give Robin the location of your boat. He slowly breaks i'
	db	'nto an evil laugh. "I thank thee, friend. All that is left f'
	db	'or us is to eliminate one remaining loose end. Now that we k'
	db	'now where thy boat is we will collect more on our investment'
	db	' by simply killing thee and taking it."*'
L1505:	db	00
L1506:	db	'"Thou hast lost thy stomach for our game, eh? If that is the'
	db	' case then my lads and I have no choice but to kill thee dea'
	db	'd to protect our secret!"*'
L1598:	db	00
L1599:	db	'bye'
L159C:	db	00
L159D:	db	'"It has been a pleasure speaking with thee, '
L15C9:	db	00
L15CA:	db	'."*'
L15CD:	db	00
