		.data
L0000:	db	'bye'
L0003:	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
L0007:	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
L000C:	db	00
L000D:	db	'locket'
L0013:	db	00
L0014:	db	'The man before you examines you with shifty eyes. He has a s'
	db	'lightly crouched posture as if constantly poised to strike o'
	db	'ut at the world around him.'
L00A7:	db	00
L00A8:	db	'strangers'
L00B1:	db	00
L00B2:	db	'"What?" asks Battles.'
L00C7:	db	00
L00C8:	db	'name'
L00CC:	db	00
L00CD:	db	'"Battles. M'self, I be a stranger to New Magincia."'
L0100:	db	00
L0101:	db	'New Magincia'
L010D:	db	00
L010E:	db	'name'
L0112:	db	00
L0113:	db	'job'
L0116:	db	00
L0117:	db	'"I be hired as a bodyguard for Master Robin, as is me partne'
	db	'r, Leavell. The pay be good."'
L0170:	db	00
L0171:	db	'Leavell'
L0178:	db	00
L0179:	db	'Robin'
L017E:	db	00
L017F:	db	'Robin'
L0184:	db	00
L0185:	db	'"Robin be a high stakes gamblin' gent who makes his living i'
	db	'nna casino at Buccaneer's Den."'
L01E0:	db	00
L01E1:	db	'"A living that would not have been anything near as profitab'
	db	'le if not for thy good works, Battles."*'
L0245:	db	00
L0246:	db	'"Thank yer, Milord."*'
L025B:	db	00
L025C:	db	'Robin'
L0261:	db	00
L0262:	db	'casino'
L0268:	db	00
L0269:	db	'gamblin' gent'
L0276:	db	00
L0277:	db	'gamblin' gent'
L0284:	db	00
L0285:	db	'"Gamblin' is how Robin makes his living. I do not think he h'
	db	'as had a regular post in all of his life!"'
L02EB:	db	00
L02EC:	db	'"Why, I thank thee for the compliment, Battles!"*'
L031D:	db	00
L031E:	db	'gamblin' gent'
L032B:	db	00
L032C:	db	'casino'
L0332:	db	00
L0333:	db	'"The casino in Buccaneer's Den is called the House of Games '
	db	'and it the most fabulous place I have ever seen in me life. '
	db	'I shall never forget the first time Robin took me there. He '
	db	'walked away with a hundred gold pieces for less than an hour'
	db	''s work!"'
L042C:	db	00
L042D:	db	'casino'
L0433:	db	00
L0434:	db	'Leavell'
L043B:	db	00
L043C:	db	'"He's a lady's man, he is. But do not be thinkin' he cannot '
	db	'handle hissel' inna fight. T'would be yer last mistake."'
L04B0:	db	00
L04B1:	db	'"I can near out wrestle thee, Battles, ye old dog!"*'
L04E5:	db	00
L04E6:	db	'"Har! Har! Har! Har!"'
L04FB:	db	00
L04FC:	db	'Leavell'
L0503:	db	00
L0504:	db	'fight'
L0509:	db	00
L050A:	db	'lady's man'
L0514:	db	00
L0515:	db	'lady's man'
L051F:	db	00
L0520:	db	'"Why, I reckon Leavell has broken near as many hearts as I h'
	db	'ave made stop beating!"'
L0573:	db	00
L0574:	db	'"So many!"*'
L057F:	db	00
L0580:	db	'lady's man'
L058A:	db	00
L058B:	db	'fight'
L0590:	db	00
L0591:	db	'"Just the practice Leavell has had in fending off jealous hu'
	db	'sbands 'twould make any man a master combatant!"'
L05FD:	db	00
L05FE:	db	'fight'
L0603:	db	00
L0604:	db	'strangers'
L060D:	db	00
L060E:	db	'"Strangers? ~~Thou must mean us!" Battles snorts loudly.'
L0646:	db	00
L0647:	db	'strangers'
L0650:	db	00
L0651:	db	'New Magincia'
L065D:	db	00
L065E:	db	'"We be looking to get off this boring rock, New Magincia, an'
	db	'd back to Buccaneer's Den. If ye have a way to get us there,'
	db	' and away from these peasant knaves, Master Robin shall pay '
	db	'ye well."'
L071B:	db	00
L071C:	db	'New Magincia'
L0728:	db	00
L0729:	db	'peasant knaves'
L0737:	db	00
L0738:	db	'boring rock'
L0743:	db	00
L0744:	db	'boring rock'
L074F:	db	00
L0750:	db	'"Canst thou imagine spending thine entire life here with not'
	db	'hing happening day after day after day? 'Tis enough to drive'
	db	' a man mad!"'
L07D4:	db	00
L07D5:	db	'boring rock'
L07E0:	db	00
L07E1:	db	'peasant knaves'
L07EF:	db	00
L07F0:	db	'"The people here are so lacking in education that they never'
	db	' even heard of gamblin' before! Never heard of gamblin'? Tha'
	db	't is what life is all about!"'
L0885:	db	00
L0886:	db	'peasant knaves'
L0894:	db	00
L0895:	db	'locket'
L089B:	db	00
L089C:	db	'"I sar a locket jus' like the one thou be describin' in the '
	db	'possession o' Master Robin. The last time I sar it was... Le'
	db	'ssee... It was right before the three of us went drinkin' at'
	db	' the Modest Damsel."'
L0964:	db	00
L0965:	db	'locket'
L096B:	db	00
L096C:	db	'bye'
L096F:	db	00
L0970:	db	'"Be seein' ye."*'
L0980:	db	00
