		.data
L0000:	db	'Avatar'
L0006:	db	00
L0007:	db	'bye'
L000A:	db	00
L000B:	db	'job'
L000E:	db	00
L000F:	db	'name'
L0013:	db	00
L0014:	db	'strangers'
L001D:	db	00
L001E:	db	'locket'
L0024:	db	00
L0025:	db	'Robin'
L002A:	db	00
L002B:	db	'Battles'
L0032:	db	00
L0033:	db	'Leavell'
L003A:	db	00
L003B:	db	'You see a content-looking bearded man, with deep-set laugh l'
	db	'ines in his face and gentle eyes.'
L0098:	db	00
L0099:	db	'"Hey there, how are things with thee?" says Sam.'
L00C9:	db	00
L00CA:	db	'name'
L00CE:	db	00
L00CF:	db	'"My name is Sam. I am the Flower Man. And what is thy name?"'
L010B:	db	00
L010C:	db	'"It is nice to meet thee."'
L0126:	db	00
L0127:	db	'"Fine. If thou dost wish to be the Avatar, I will not argue.'
	db	' Thou canst be the Avatar if thou dost want to be."'
L0196:	db	00
L0197:	db	'name'
L019B:	db	00
L019C:	db	'job'
L019F:	db	00
L01A0:	db	'"The way I perceive it I do not really have a job. I sell fl'
	db	'owers to the people of New Magincia. Although I am paid for '
	db	'it, it is something I enjoy doing very much. I wonder, does '
	db	'that still qualify as a job?" He scratches his chin thoughtf'
	db	'ully.'
L0295:	db	00
L0296:	db	'New Magincia'
L02A2:	db	00
L02A3:	db	'flowers'
L02AA:	db	00
L02AB:	db	'flowers'
L02B2:	db	00
L02B3:	db	'"I grow all of the flowers that I sell in a greenhouse which'
	db	' is also mine home. I sell a lot of red roses but I have man'
	db	'y varieties. If thou art interested in buying some, please s'
	db	'ay so!"'
L036E:	db	00
L036F:	db	'buy'
L0372:	db	00
L0373:	db	'greenhouse'
L037D:	db	00
L037E:	db	'flowers'
L0385:	db	00
L0386:	db	'greenhouse'
L0390:	db	00
L0391:	db	'"I built my greenhouse by hand. When I am not selling flower'
	db	's I am engaged in various studies of plants and nature there'
	db	'. I find it fascinating. As thou mayest have noticed, I pref'
	db	'er to grow them big!"'
L045A:	db	00
L045B:	db	'greenhouse'
L0465:	db	00
L0466:	db	'big'
L0469:	db	00
L046A:	db	'studies'
L0471:	db	00
L0472:	db	'studies'
L0479:	db	00
L047A:	db	'"Presently I am studying possible uses and applications of w'
	db	'heatgrass. One day soon I shall begin compiling my notes but'
	db	' it will require a long effort for there is much that I have'
	db	' learned. It is mostly to support my work that I operate my '
	db	'flower wagon."'
L0578:	db	00
L0579:	db	'wagon'
L057E:	db	00
L057F:	db	'studies'
L0586:	db	00
L0587:	db	'big'
L058A:	db	00
L058B:	db	'"It is because of what I learn in my studies that I may grow'
	db	' my flowers to be so large and healthy."'
L05EF:	db	00
L05F0:	db	'big'
L05F3:	db	00
L05F4:	db	'wagon'
L05F9:	db	00
L05FA:	db	'"Actually my business does quite well and I do like the way '
	db	'my flowers brighten the whole place. But who really cares ab'
	db	'out business anyway, so why shouldst thou ask? Suffice it to'
	db	' say that life is sweet!"'
L06C7:	db	00
L06C8:	db	'wagon'
L06CD:	db	00
L06CE:	db	'life'
L06D2:	db	00
L06D3:	db	'life'
L06D7:	db	00
L06D8:	db	'"Thou hast enough money as long as thou dost have a place to'
	db	' live and can afford food, so I consider myself a wealthy ma'
	db	'n. I enjoy a good drink and round of song at the Modest Dams'
	db	'el nightly. I have a thriving business and stimulating work.'
	db	' I consider every resident of this island a good friend. I f'
	db	'eel anger towards no one and do not desire anything more. I '
	db	'have never had reason to feel lonely, worried or bored. What'
	db	' else is there? Life is good!"'
L089A:	db	00
L089B:	db	'life'
L089F:	db	00
L08A0:	db	'buy'
L08A3:	db	00
L08A4:	db	'"There are many pretty ladies on this island and they are in'
	db	' the habit of receiving flowers from the gentlemen they meet'
	db	'. It would cause a dreadful embarrassment if thou didst not '
	db	'have any!'
L0961:	db	00
L0962:	db	'"The gentlemen of this island have a peculiarity in their ta'
	db	'ste in women. They cannot refuse anything of a woman who wea'
	db	'rs flowers. If thou dost not wear any they will simply ignor'
	db	'e thee!'
L0A1D:	db	00
L0A1E:	db	'"Surely thou dost wish to purchase some?"'
L0A47:	db	00
L0A48:	db	'"A bouquet costs 12 gold. Art thou still interested?"'
L0A7D:	db	00
L0A7E:	db	'"The bouquet is thine!"'
L0A95:	db	00
L0A96:	db	'"Thine hands are too full to take the bouquet!"'
L0AC5:	db	00
L0AC6:	db	'"Thou dost not have the money to buy flowers. But take heart'
	db	', whenever thou canst afford them, I shall still be selling '
	db	'them."'
L0B44:	db	00
L0B45:	db	'"Perhaps next time, '
L0B59:	db	00
L0B5A:	db	'," he responds, smiling.'
L0B72:	db	00
L0B73:	db	'"Perhaps another time then."'
L0B8F:	db	00
L0B90:	db	'"I am afraid that my shop is now closed, but if thou wilt re'
	db	'turn during business hours, I shall provide the solution to '
	db	'thine apparent floral emergency."'
L0C29:	db	00
L0C2A:	db	'buy'
L0C2D:	db	00
L0C2E:	db	'strangers'
L0C37:	db	00
L0C38:	db	'"There are three strangers on this island that have washed a'
	db	'shore in a shipwreck. Perhaps thou shalt meet them."'
L0CA8:	db	00
L0CA9:	db	'strangers'
L0CB2:	db	00
L0CB3:	db	'locket'
L0CB9:	db	00
L0CBA:	db	'"Yes, I saw Henry walking past my shop with that locket look'
	db	'ing for Constance. It must have been shortly after he receiv'
	db	'ed it from Katrina. I remember it because I gave him a flowe'
	db	'r to give to Constance. Poor fellow, by the time he found he'
	db	'r it was all he had to give her."'
L0DCB:	db	00
L0DCC:	db	'locket'
L0DD2:	db	00
L0DD3:	db	'Robin'
L0DD8:	db	00
L0DD9:	db	'"Why, he sounds like one of those three strangers! I have me'
	db	't him. He talked as if he wanted to buy some flowers but he '
	db	'just walked away. Later I noticed a bouquet of flowers was m'
	db	'issing from my wagon. The scoundrel must have pilfered them!'
	db	'"'
L0ECA:	db	00
L0ECB:	db	'Robin'
L0ED0:	db	00
L0ED1:	db	'Battles'
L0ED8:	db	00
L0ED9:	db	'"He must be one of those shipwrecked visitors we have on our'
	db	' island. Yes, when the three of them came up to my wagon he '
	db	'gave me a stare that sent a chill through my blood. I did my'
	db	' best to ignore him. I absolutely abhor violence."'
L0FBF:	db	00
L0FC0:	db	'Battles'
L0FC7:	db	00
L0FC8:	db	'Leavell'
L0FCF:	db	00
L0FD0:	db	'"So that is the name of one of our uninvited guests! When th'
	db	'e three of them came to my wagon earlier, he was very friend'
	db	'ly while talking to me, but I saw through him. He mentioned '
	db	'noticing Constance, but the others gestured for him to be qu'
	db	'iet."'
L10C5:	db	00
L10C6:	db	'Leavell'
L10CD:	db	00
L10CE:	db	'New Magincia'
L10DA:	db	00
L10DB:	db	'"I was not born here. I came here as a young man. My father '
	db	'was a nobleman who was more interested in my counting gold t'
	db	'han devoting myself to my studies. For a time I travelled th'
	db	'e world until I landed here. It is a special place unlike an'
	db	'y other in all of Britannia. So while thou art here please h'
	db	'elp us take good care of it."'
L1224:	db	00
L1225:	db	'New Magincia'
L1231:	db	00
L1232:	db	'bye'
L1235:	db	00
L1236:	db	'"Enjoy thy life, friend."*'
L1250:	db	00
L1251:	db	'@Beautiful flowers!@'
L1265:	db	00
L1266:	db	'@I have pretty flowers!@'
L127E:	db	00
L127F:	db	'@Who will buy these lovely flowers?@'
L12A3:	db	00
L12A4:	db	'@Thou dost need beautiful flowers!@'
L12C7:	db	00
