L0000:	db	'Iriale'
L0006:	db	00
L0007:	db	'You see a familiar face, a stern-looking bearded warrior who'
	db	'm you have met on one of your previous journeys to Britannia'
	db	'.'
L0080:	db	00
L0081:	db	'"Ho, Avatar!" says Gorn. "Thou dost vish to speak mit me?"'
L00BB:	db	00
L00BC:	db	'"De voice ov Brom has told me not to trust thee, Avatar," sa'
	db	'ys Gorn. "I tought dat ve vere friends and I do not vish to '
	db	'cause thee harm. But I varn thee, do not speak mit me anymor'
	db	'e!"*'
L0174:	db	00
L0175:	db	'bye'
L0178:	db	00
L0179:	db	'job'
L017C:	db	00
L017D:	db	'name'
L0181:	db	00
L0182:	db	'name'
L0186:	db	00
L0187:	db	'The warrior's eyes narrow. "I am Gorn, as if thou didst not '
	db	'remember! It is good to see thee again." He laughs and slaps'
	db	' you on the shoulder.'
L0214:	db	00
L0215:	db	'name'
L0219:	db	00
L021A:	db	'job'
L021D:	db	00
L021E:	db	'"My job is a never-ending qvest of high adventure. Ever sinc'
	db	'e I vas a child und vas taken from mine homeland of Balema, '
	db	'I haf spent my life in search of heroic deeds to perform."'
L02D0:	db	00
L02D1:	db	'heroic deeds'
L02DD:	db	00
L02DE:	db	'Balema'
L02E4:	db	00
L02E5:	db	'Balema'
L02EB:	db	00
L02EC:	db	'"Yah, Balema is vere I vas born. I vas a child dere. It is a'
	db	' vonderland ov snow-covered mountains und dark forests. It v'
	db	'as not an easy life, but it vas a place dat made young boys '
	db	'into strong heroic men. Dat vas long before I came to Britan'
	db	'nia."'
L03E1:	db	00
L03E2:	db	'Balema'
L03E8:	db	00
L03E9:	db	'Britannia'
L03F2:	db	00
L03F3:	db	'Britannia'
L03FC:	db	00
L03FD:	db	'"Yah! I came to Britannia t'rough vone ov de Moongates, de s'
	db	'ame as thee. Dat vas many, many years ago."'
L0464:	db	00
L0465:	db	'Britannia'
L046E:	db	00
L046F:	db	'heroic deeds'
L047B:	db	00
L047C:	db	'"I perform heroic deeds in honor ov Brom. Everyting I do is '
	db	'in service to him."'
L04CB:	db	00
L04CC:	db	'heroic deeds'
L04D8:	db	00
L04D9:	db	'Brom'
L04DD:	db	00
L04DE:	db	'Brom'
L04E2:	db	00
L04E3:	db	'"He is my master, und de master ov all ov de people ov Balem'
	db	'a. Brom is all powerful und if I am strong he vill aid me. S'
	db	'ometimes I hear de voice ov Brom inside ov mine head."'
L0591:	db	00
L0592:	db	'Brom'
L0596:	db	00
L0597:	db	'voice'
L059C:	db	00
L059D:	db	'master'
L05A3:	db	00
L05A4:	db	'master'
L05AA:	db	00
L05AB:	db	'"Ya! Brom he is my master. If he vishes me to do someting, I'
	db	' must do it! If he does not vant me to do someting, I must n'
	db	'ot do it!"'
L062D:	db	00
L062E:	db	'master'
L0634:	db	00
L0635:	db	'voice'
L063A:	db	00
L063B:	db	'"Ya! Only recently I haf begun to hear his voice in mine hea'
	db	'd. His voice tells me vat to do! As I came tovard dis cave d'
	db	'e voice ov Brom became clearer."'
L06D3:	db	00
L06D4:	db	'voice'
L06D9:	db	00
L06DA:	db	'clearer'
L06E1:	db	00
L06E2:	db	'cave'
L06E6:	db	00
L06E7:	db	'what to do'
L06F1:	db	00
L06F2:	db	'what to do'
L06FC:	db	00
L06FD:	db	'"Vhen I first heard de voice ov Brom, he told me dat I shoul'
	db	'd follow him. But how does one follow de voice ov someone da'
	db	't thou cannot see vhen de voice is coming from inside ov thi'
	db	'ne head?"'
L07BA:	db	00
L07BB:	db	'what to do'
L07C5:	db	00
L07C6:	db	'follow'
L07CC:	db	00
L07CD:	db	'follow'
L07D3:	db	00
L07D4:	db	'"Dis vas very, very difficult for me but after a vhile I vas'
	db	' able to figure out how to do it. Vhen I came nearer to da c'
	db	'amp surrounding dis cave da voice vould get louder. Vhen I v'
	db	'ould move avay de voice vould be qvieter."'
L08B2:	db	00
L08B3:	db	'follow'
L08B9:	db	00
L08BA:	db	'camp'
L08BE:	db	00
L08BF:	db	'camp'
L08C3:	db	00
L08C4:	db	'"It vas very simple for a trained varrior like myself to sli'
	db	'p into de camp ov dose who are holding Brom prisoner. Dey po'
	db	'sed no threat vatsoever. So dat means dat de danger must be '
	db	'vaiting down here. But I cannot find it!"'
L09A1:	db	00
L09A2:	db	'"I can see by dat medallion thou dost vear dat thou hast snu'
	db	'ck into dis place by disguising thyself as vone of dem. Very'
	db	' clever, Avatar!"'
L0A2B:	db	00
L0A2C:	db	'Iolo whispers to you, "This fellow is quite sharp, is he not'
	db	'?"*'
L0A6B:	db	00
L0A6C:	db	'camp'
L0A70:	db	00
L0A71:	db	'danger'
L0A77:	db	00
L0A78:	db	'danger'
L0A7E:	db	00
L0A7F:	db	'"Zo far de only danger I haf found down here has been a fema'
	db	'le fighter. She vas beautiful. Vhen I vent to talk to her sh'
	db	'e hit me over de head mit her svord. Vhen I voke up she vas '
	db	'gone. I bet she tought she had killed me but mine head is ha'
	db	'rder dan dat. I vas not even vounded."'
L0B95:	db	00
L0B96:	db	'Shamino whispers to you. "Luckily, Gorn was hit in the one s'
	db	'pot where he has no feeling whatsoever -- his head!"*'
L0C07:	db	00
L0C08:	db	'"Hey, vhat are you vhispering about over dere?"*'
L0C38:	db	00
L0C39:	db	'"Oh, nothing. Nothing at all."*'
L0C58:	db	00
L0C59:	db	'danger'
L0C5F:	db	00
L0C60:	db	'cave'
L0C64:	db	00
L0C65:	db	'"I know dat Brom is somevhere down in dis cave, und I vill n'
	db	'ot leave dis place until I find him!"'
L0CC6:	db	00
L0CC7:	db	'cave'
L0CCB:	db	00
L0CCC:	db	'find Brom'
L0CD5:	db	00
L0CD6:	db	'clearer'
L0CDD:	db	00
L0CDE:	db	'"The nearer I haf come to dis cave, the more times I haf bee'
	db	'n hearing de voice ov Brom. But lately he has been saying ti'
	db	'ngs to me dat are very, very strange!"'
L0D7C:	db	00
L0D7D:	db	'clearer'
L0D84:	db	00
L0D85:	db	'strange'
L0D8C:	db	00
L0D8D:	db	'strange'
L0D94:	db	00
L0D95:	db	'"De first strange ting dat he says to me is "Strive For Unit'
	db	'y". I say, yah, dat is vhy I am performing mine heroic deeds'
	db	'. Den Brom says someting else dat is strange."'
L0E3B:	db	00
L0E3C:	db	'strange'
L0E43:	db	00
L0E44:	db	'something else strange'
L0E5A:	db	00
L0E5B:	db	'something else strange'
L0E71:	db	00
L0E72:	db	'"Next de voice ov Brom says to me "Trust My Brothers". Dis i'
	db	's strange because all ov my brothers are back in Balema, und'
	db	' I vould never trust dem anyvays. Dey vere all bigger den me'
	db	' and vere alvays beating me. But even dat vas not as strange'
	db	' as da next strange ting."'
L0F7C:	db	00
L0F7D:	db	'something else strange'
L0F93:	db	00
L0F94:	db	'next strange thing'
L0FA6:	db	00
L0FA7:	db	'next strange thing'
L0FB9:	db	00
L0FBA:	db	'"De voice ov Brom tells me dat "Worldliness Receives Avard".'
	db	' I haf been tinking about dat von for a long time und I stil'
	db	'l haf not figured it out. But I vill not give up until I fin'
	db	'd Brom."'
L1076:	db	00
L1077:	db	'"A mysterious voice speaking inside someone's head, suggesti'
