L0786:	db	'Over my dead body!'
L0798:	db	00
L0799:	db	'"Why, '
L079F:	db	00
L07A0:	db	'. I thought that was understood. It will be my pleasure to h'
	db	'elp thee enter the realm of the dead."'
L0802:	db	00
L0803:	db	'Fine!'
L0808:	db	00
L0809:	db	'"Yes, I thought thou wouldst see the wisdom of my vision." H'
	db	'e looks at you like a cat toying with a mouse.'
L0873:	db	00
L0874:	db	'Lord British'
L0880:	db	00
L0881:	db	'`Evil' is a mild word for the sneer that appears on the Lich'
	db	'e's cracked lips. "It has recently come to my attention that'
	db	' a certain ore found in the Britannian surface can, if fashi'
	db	'oned properly, become the bane of the vaunted Lord British.~'
	db	'~"I know this ore and have used it	before for other purposes'
	db	'. I will use it once again to destroy that so-called Lord."'
