L0B36:	db	'job'
L0B39:	db	00
L0B3A:	db	'A harsh cackle escapes his dry throat. "I am the illustrious'
	db	' Lord of the Dead, soon to be Lord of all Britannia. Dost th'
	db	'ou have any idea of the number of dead people and creatures '
	db	'there are? I thought not.~~"The dead of the ages are mine to'
	db	' summon and control. The graves of beloved ancestors will sp'
	db	'ew forth their contents into an army. A special treat for th'
	db	'e living, mine undead monsters will be. Imagine a skeletal d'
	db	'ragon that cannot be killed. Consider a cabal of everliving '
	db	'mages eternally enthralled to me.~~"And the most beautiful p'
	db	'art of my plot is that, as the living die in these battles, '
	db	'and they will die, they will swell the ranks of the undead h'
	db	'ost. I will rule supreme -- a world of the dead!" A terrifyi'
	db	'ng glimpse of his sick and twisted future causes you to shiv'
	db	'er	ever so slightly.~~"And I will have a queen, the lovely R'
	db	'owena."'
L0E89:	db	00
L0E8A:	db	'Rowena'
L0E90:	db	00
L0E91:	db	'"Yes, my Lord. I must be the happiest Lady in all the land."'
	db	' Her gaze never wanders from the horrid face of the Liche.'
L0F07:	db	00
L0F08:	db	'Rowena'
L0F0E:	db	00
L0F0F:	db	'"Is she not the most beautiful lady thou hast seen? ~~"She s'
	db	'hall have eternal beauty at my side, and we shall rule toget'
	db	'her."'
L0F8C:	db	00
L0F8D:	db	'"She is the most beautiful lady I have been witness to. She '
	db	'shall have eternal beauty at my side, and we shall rule toge'
	db	'ther." After hearing him speak of his plans for the future, '
	db	'you find this a very unlikely statement.'
