		.funcnumber	048FH
		.data
L0000:	db	'The old, ghostly woman hums the tune to an ancient ballad an'
	db	'd smiles up at you. This old woman brings to mind every gran'
	db	'dmother you've ever seen.~~Apparently she is not entirely ob'
	db	'livious to your presence. However, when you speak to her, it'
	db	' seems as if your words fall on deaf ears. She looks puzzled'
	db	' for a moment, then moves her arms in magical passes. You re'
	db	'cognize the words to be a variant of the Seance spell.'
L019E:	db	00
L019F:	db	'The old, ghostly woman looks very strange. Her eyes are open'
	db	', but she doesn't seem to be awake, or at least not aware of'
	db	' her surroundings.*'
L022A:	db	00
L022B:	db	'"I am sorry, '
L0238:	db	00
L0239:	db	'. Do not take offense, but I must rest before we speak furth'
	db	'er. I thank thee for thy patience, young one." She looks ver'
	db	'y weary as she turns away.*'
L02CC:	db	00
L02CD:	db	'ingredients'
L02D8:	db	00
L02D9:	db	'sacrifice'
L02E2:	db	00
L02E3:	db	'"Hello, '
L02EB:	db	00
L02EC:	db	'. Thou mayest call me Mistress Mordra." She peers at you clo'
	db	'sely.~~"And thou must be '
L0341:	db	00
L0342:	db	', the Avatar." She looks you over thoroughly.'
L036F:	db	00
L0370:	db	'"Greetings once again, '
L0387:	db	00
L0388:	db	'."'
L038A:	db	00
L038B:	db	'She lifts up her arms and in one of them you see an ankh. Wo'
	db	'rds which you vaguely recognize flow from her lips and the a'
	db	'nkh glows brightly. She stops chanting and the ankh dims. Af'
	db	'ter her analysis of your condition is complete, "Ah, it is g'
	db	'ood to see that the world has been treating thee well. How m'
	db	'ay I serve thee, 'O Virtuous One?"'
L04D9:	db	00
L04DA:	db	'bye'
L04DD:	db	00
L04DE:	db	'job'
L04E1:	db	00
L04E2:	db	'name'
L04E6:	db	00
L04E7:	db	'cage made'
L04F0:	db	00
L04F1:	db	'name'
L04F5:	db	00
L04F6:	db	'She smiles at you. "Thou art quite forgetful, '
L0524:	db	00
L0525:	db	'. As I have told thee, I am known as Mordra."'
L0552:	db	00
L0553:	db	'name'
L0557:	db	00
L0558:	db	'job'
L055B:	db	00
L055C:	db	'"I was the healer of this town before the fire erupted that '
	db	'shattered the lives of those here. I also dabbled in secret '
	db	'magical arts for a while." She winks at you slyly.'
L0606:	db	00
L0607:	db	'magical arts'
L0613:	db	00
L0614:	db	'fire'
L0618:	db	00
L0619:	db	'lives'
L061E:	db	00
L061F:	db	'ingredients'
L062A:	db	00
L062B:	db	'"If I tell thee, thou must be sure to get them right. Otherw'
	db	'ise, what happened when I told that blasted mayor will happe'
	db	'n again. And, while we here in Skara Brae have no more lives'
	db	' to lose, thou hast quite a valuable one! ~~"The ingredients'
	db	' necessary for the concoction to dissolve the liche are a po'
	db	'tion of invisibility, a dose of a potion of curing, and one	'
	db	'vial of the essence of mandrake -- I have one set aside some'
	db	'where in mine house. Remember, only -one- vial of the mandra'
	db	'ke!"'
L080F:	db	00
L0810:	db	'ingredients'
L081B:	db	00
L081C:	db	'cage made'
L0825:	db	00
L0826:	db	'cage made'
L082F:	db	00
L0830:	db	'"The Soul Cage must be empowered with the might of the dead.'
	db	' The way to accomplish this is to go to the back of the Dark'
	db	' Tower, to the Well of Souls. Thou must lower the cage into '
	db	'the well, where the souls trapped there will lose a little o'
	db	'f themselves to imbue it with the required power.~~"I know t'
	db	'his sounds harsh, but it is a necessary evil if thou wouldst'
	db	' see them freed." She looks at you sharply.~~"The next step '
	db	'is to wait until midnight, then clap the cage upon the recum'
	db	'bent form of the Liche. This is the period of time in which '
	db	'he drains the spirits of the townsfolk in his Black Service.'
	db	'"~~After a brief moment, she continues. "Finally, thou must '
	db	'pour a magical formula upon the Liche within the cage. This '
	db	'formula is the same substance that destroyed the town.~~"Do '
	db	'be careful when procuring it from the alchemist, Caine."'
L0B74:	db	00
L0B75:	db	'Black Service'
L0B82:	db	00
L0B83:	db	'Well of Souls'
L0B90:	db	00
L0B91:	db	'Dark Tower'
L0B9B:	db	00
L0B9C:	db	'formula'
L0BA3:	db	00
L0BA4:	db	'formula'
L0BAB:	db	00
L0BAC:	db	'"Thou must have Caine's assistance in creating the formula, '
	db	'but I can give thee the ingredients."'
L0C0D:	db	00
L0C0E:	db	'formula'
L0C15:	db	00
L0C16:	db	'ingredients'
L0C21:	db	00
L0C22:	db	'Dark Tower'
L0C2C:	db	00
L0C2D:	db	'"The Dark Tower lies on the northwestern point of Skara Brae'
	db	'. There is something odd about its construction, for I find '
	db	'it very hard to penetrate with my magical senses.~Within it,'
	db	'" she says, "thou wilt find the Well of Souls."'
L0D10:	db	00
L0D11:	db	'Dark Tower'
L0D1B:	db	00
L0D1C:	db	'Well of Souls'
L0D29:	db	00
L0D2A:	db	'Well of Souls'
L0D37:	db	00
L0D38:	db	'"The Well of Souls is a powerful artifact, located beneath t'
	db	'he Dark Tower, from which the Liche draws his power. The sou'
	db	'ls of the dead are incarcerated there, doomed to the torment'
	db	' of Horance's all-consuming appetite." An expression of pain'
	db	' shows in her features.'
L0E3F:	db	00
L0E40:	db	'Well of Souls'
L0E4D:	db	00
L0E4E:	db	'Black Service'
L0E5B:	db	00
L0E5C:	db	'Angrily, Mordra says, "Each night, at the stroke of midnight'
	db	', the spirits of Skara Brae travel to the Dark Tower and are'
	db	' used to infuse Horance with power to continue his dark exis'
	db	'tence. None of the others are aware when this happens, but I'
	db	' feel it without being able to stop myself."'
L0F78:	db	00
L0F79:	db	'Dark Tower'
L0F83:	db	00
L0F84:	db	'"Even though the Liche is gone, we are still drawn to the pl'
	db	'ace of his Black Service. He must have bound us with a geas '
	db	'and tied it to the power of the Well of Souls. Oh, what a cr'
	db	'afty villain he was." Grudging respect for a skilled mage is'
	db	' mixed with disgust in Mordra's expression.'
L109F:	db	00
L10A0:	db	'Well of Souls'
L10AD:	db	00
L10AE:	db	'Black Service'
L10BB:	db	00
L10BC:	db	'lives'
L10C1:	db	00
L10C2:	db	'"Wouldst thou like to know about the townsfolk of Skara Brae'
	db	'?"'
L1100:	db	00
L1101:	db	'"I might have some new information on my fellow townsfolk th'
	db	'at could be of use to thee," she says, adding a smile.'
L1173:	db	00
L1174:	db	'"Very well, '
L1180:	db	00
L1181:	db	'. What wouldst thou care to know about?"'
L11A9:	db	00
L11AA:	db	'lives'
L11AF:	db	00
L11B0:	db	'fire'
L11B4:	db	00
L11B5:	db	'"'Twas the doom of this town, although I place no blame upon'
	db	' the alchemist, Caine. For I was the one who told him the re'
	db	'cipe that I am sure will rid us of Horance the Liche."'
L1263:	db	00
L1264:	db	'fire'
L1268:	db	00
L1269:	db	'Caine'
L126E:	db	00
L126F:	db	'recipe'
L1275:	db	00
L1276:	db	'recipe'
L127C:	db	00
L127D:	db	'"'Twas but a simple mixture of a few ingredients. It should '
	db	'have worked." Her eyes narrow.~~"I expect that mayor of ours'
	db	', Forsythe, fouled things up!"'
L1313:	db	00
L1314:	db	'recipe'
L131A:	db	00
L131B:	db	'mayor'
L1320:	db	00
L1321:	db	'mayor'
L1326:	db	00
L1327:	db	'"That man is a bumbling idiot. It is his fault that the isla'
	db	'nd was destroyed. I gave him the exact portions of the reage'
	db	'nts to be used in the magical formula, and he paraphrased it'
	db	' to the alchemist, Caine. By the size of the fire, I am sure'
	db	' he misquoted the amount of mandrake root by	tenfold. Damn t'
	db	'hat foolish man!"~~Her brow creases and you	can see that thi'
	db	's is a subject that she likes to avoid.'
L14B6:	db	00
L14B7:	db	'mayor'
L14BC:	db	00
L14BD:	db	'Caine'
L14C2:	db	00
L14C3:	db	'Caine'
L14C8:	db	00
L14C9:	db	'"Now those who reside here call him `the Tortured One.' That'
	db	' is because he is in eternal pain, caused by searing flames '
	db	'licking at his flesh.~~The pain is imagined, but to him, 'ti'
	db	's as real as thou or I... or, at least, as real as	thou art!'
	db	'"'
L15BA:	db	00
L15BB:	db	'Caine'
L15C0:	db	00
L15C1:	db	'magical arts'
L15CD:	db	00
L15CE:	db	'Her eyes twinkle mischievously. "If I were to reveal them to'
	db	' thee, they wouldn't be secret any longer, now would they?"'
L1645:	db	00
L1646:	db	'magical arts'
L1652:	db	00
L1653:	db	'sacrifice'
L165C:	db	00
L165D:	db	'She smiles at first, then turns serious. "I have tied my spi'
	db	'rit to powers beyond the realm of this mortal world. Were I '
	db	'to enter the Well of Souls, this entire island and a good bi'
	db	't of the mainland would be destroyed in a magical discharge.'
	db	' Wouldst thou lose the town of Skara Brae for all eternity?"'
L1789:	db	00
L178A:	db	'"Thou knowest full well that I cannot. If thou wouldst	see m'
	db	'ass destruction, thou shalt have to cause it thyself." She t'
	db	'urns away quickly for a woman of her age.*'
L182C:	db	00
L182D:	db	'sacrifice'
L1836:	db	00
L1837:	db	'bye'
L183A:	db	00
L183B:	db	'"Goodbye, young '
L184B:	db	00
L184C:	db	'. Take care of thyself, but should ill befall thee, I hope t'
	db	'hat thou wilt come back here and let me minister to thine ai'
	db	'lments." She smiles kindly as you leave.*'
