L0000:	db	'bye'
L0003:	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
L0007:	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
L000C:	db	00
L000D:	db	'Tortured One'
L0019:	db	00
L001A:	db	'The lovely apparition goes about her tasks without offering '
	db	'any response.*'
L0064:	db	00
L0065:	db	'The lovely barmaid stares off into oblivion, completely unaw'
	db	'are of her location and position.*'
L00C3:	db	00
L00C4:	db	'The pretty barmaid looks as if she's about to fall over for '
	db	'a moment, then quickly rights herself. "Oh, I feel a bit... '
	db	'faint." She turns away, distracted.*'
L0160:	db	00
L0161:	db	'"Go away! Thou art cruel and mean-hearted." She turns away, '
	db	'but not before you see the tears in her eyes.*'
L01CB:	db	00
L01CC:	db	'Paulette perks up as she sees Rowena.~~"Hello, milady. 'Tis '
	db	'good to see thee again. How art thou?"*'
L022F:	db	00
L0230:	db	'"I am fine, Paulette. I thank thee for thy concern."*'
L0265:	db	00
L0266:	db	'"'Tis good news indeed, milady."'
L0286:	db	00
L0287:	db	'"Hello, Mayor. It has been quite a while since we've seen th'
	db	'ee in our tavern. There was a time, I remember, when we coul'
	db	'dn't keep thee away."*'
L0315:	db	00
L0316:	db	'The mayor becomes quickly embarrassed as he tries to quiet t'
	db	'he rather friendly Paulette.~~"I, er, used to be a wine conn'
	db	'oisseur of sorts," he says to you.*'
L03B1:	db	00
L03B2:	db	'"'Tis not all thou wert a connoisseur of," adds Paulette, ey'
	db	'es twinkling. "I seem to remember thou had quite a taste for'
	db	' redheads."'
L0435:	db	00
L0436:	db	'sacrifice'
L043F:	db	00
L0440:	db	'You see a pretty, ghostly girl with long black hair. "Hello,'
	db	' '
L047D:	db	00
L047E:	db	'. I am called Paulette. How may I help thee?"'
L04AB:	db	00
L04AC:	db	'Standing before you, with a hand on her hip, is a lovely, yo'
	db	'ung woman with long black hair. "Ooooh... Thou art a big one'
	db	', '
L0526:	db	00
L0527:	db	'." She traces the line of your bicep.~~"I'd wager thou could'
	db	'st lift me over thine head." She smiles enticingly. However,'
	db	' you doubt that you could even touch her in her ghostly stat'
	db	'e.~~"Thou mayest call me Paulette, gorgeous. What can I do f'
	db	'or thee?" She winks at you.'
L0632:	db	00
L0633:	db	'"Yes, '
L0639:	db	00
L063A:	db	'?", she asks sweetly.'
L064F:	db	00
L0650:	db	'Paulette turns to face you and smiles coquettishly, "I had t'
	db	'hought that thou might return." Her eyes sparkle up at you m'
	db	'ischievously.'
L06D5:	db	00
L06D6:	db	'name'
L06DA:	db	00
L06DB:	db	'"Why, '
L06E1:	db	00
L06E2:	db	', hast thou forgotten already? I am Paulette."'
L0710:	db	00
L0711:	db	'name'
L0715:	db	00
L0716:	db	'job'
L0719:	db	00
L071A:	db	'"Well, '
L0721:	db	00
L0722:	db	', before the fire," she shudders, "I used to be the barmaid '
	db	'here."'
L0764:	db	00
L0765:	db	'"Well, '
L076C:	db	00
L076D:	db	'. I used to clean tables here..." As she says this, she bend'
	db	's over and pretends to wipe a table clean. You notice how lo'
	db	'w the cut of her bodice really is.~~"...and serve people, li'
	db	'ke thyself. Of course, none so handsome." Her ghostly featur'
	db	'es blush prettily.~~"But that was before," she shudders, "th'
	db	'e fire."'
L08A1:	db	00
L08A2:	db	'buy'
L08A5:	db	00
L08A6:	db	'here'
L08AA:	db	00
L08AB:	db	'fire'
L08AF:	db	00
L08B0:	db	'buy'
L08B3:	db	00
L08B4:	db	'"Thou dost wish to purchase something?"'
L08DB:	db	00
L08DC:	db	'"I am sorry, '
L08E9:	db	00
L08EA:	db	'," she giggles, "but all we serve here are... spirits!"*'
L0922:	db	00
L0923:	db	'"That's a good one, wench," laughs the portly ghost.*'
L0958:	db	00
L0959:	db	'"Very well, '
L0965:	db	00
L0966:	db	'."'
L0968:	db	00
L0969:	db	'buy'
L096C:	db	00
L096D:	db	'Tortured One'
L0979:	db	00
L097A:	db	'She appears puzzled for an instant, but then she nods her he'
	db	'ad.~~"Oh, thou must be referring to Caine. He was the alchem'
	db	'ist who was responsible for the fire."'
L0A18:	db	00
L0A19:	db	'Tortured One'
L0A25:	db	00
L0A26:	db	'fire'
L0A2A:	db	00
L0A2B:	db	'fire'
L0A2F:	db	00
L0A30:	db	'"Oh, yes. It was horrible! The tavern caught on fire. I ran '
	db	'to my room, hoping to escape the flames. But then I started '
	db	'coughing. I couldn't breathe." Her chest rises and falls qui'
	db	'ckly as if she's reliving the experience.~~"Finally, I could'
	db	' take it no longer." She brings the back of her hand to her '
	db	'forehead, dramatically. "I fainted. Then I was here again, j'
	db	'ust like thou dost see me now." Her smile is like that of a '
	db	'child.'
L0BDA:	db	00
L0BDB:	db	'fire'
L0BDF:	db	00
L0BE0:	db	'here again'
L0BEA:	db	00
L0BEB:	db	'tavern'
L0BF1:	db	00
L0BF2:	db	'here again'
L0BFC:	db	00
L0BFD:	db	'"Yes, 'twas quite odd. When I awoke, it was as if I had neve'
	db	'r left when the fire began. In fact, were it not for the sco'
	db	'rch marks everywhere, I would doubt the fire ever happened."'
L0CB1:	db	00
L0CB2:	db	'here again'
L0CBC:	db	00
L0CBD:	db	'here'
L0CC1:	db	00
L0CC2:	db	'tavern'
L0CC8:	db	00
L0CC9:	db	' coyly'
L0CCF:	db	00
L0CD0:	db	00
L0CD1:	db	'"Why, 'tis called the Keg O' Spirits. That's a fine name for'
	db	' a tavern, dost thou not agree?" She smiles '
L0D39:	db	00
L0D3A:	db	'.'
L0D3B:	db	00
L0D3C:	db	'tavern'
L0D42:	db	00
L0D43:	db	'here'
L0D47:	db	00
L0D48:	db	'sacrifice'
L0D51:	db	00
L0D52:	db	'"Thou wantest me to... to jump in a well?" Her eyes widen wi'
	db	'th astonishment.'
L0D9E:	db	00
L0D9F:	db	'"Well, thou canst go jump in a lake!" She crosses her arms o'
	db	'n her buxom chest and turns away from you angrily.*'
L0E0E:	db	00
L0E0F:	db	'She recovers her composure, "Oh. For a moment there, I thoug'
	db	'ht that thou wouldst have me be thy... sacrifice."'
L0E7D:	db	00
L0E7E:	db	'"Please, just leave me alone!" she looks as if she's about t'
	db	'o cry.*'
L0EC1:	db	00
L0EC2:	db	'sacrifice'
L0ECB:	db	00
L0ECC:	db	'bye'
L0ECF:	db	00
L0ED0:	db	'"Goodbye, '
L0EDA:	db	00
L0EDB:	db	'." The pretty ghost turns away.*'
L0EFB:	db	00
L0EFC:	db	'Paulette rushes up to you as you say goodbye and gives you a'
	db	' little kiss on the cheek. She backs away slowly, "Farewell,'
	db	' handsome."*'
L0F80:	db	00
