L0484:	db	'Ferryman'
L048C:	db	00
L048D:	db	'The man looks strangely relaxed, almost too relaxed. He also'
	db	' ignores your attempt to converse with him. It would seem th'
	db	'at he is not in control of his actions.*'
L052D:	db	00
L052E:	db	'"No! Back! Please, leave me alone!" The Mayor looks terrifie'
	db	'd. It seems that you must give up trying to get anything use'
	db	'ful out of him for the time being.*'
L05C9:	db	00
L05CA:	db	'You see a middle-aged ghost cowering in the corner of this b'
	db	'urned-out room. He's shaking from head to toe, and, as you a'
	db	'pproach, he jumps out, waving an ankh in your face.~~ "Thou''
	db	'lt not have me, foul beast! Back, back I say! In the name of'
	db	' the Virtues, back!" He slowly notices that this is having n'
	db	'o effect other than to surprise you and looks more closely i'
	db	'n your direction. He looks from you to a picture of you on t'
	db	'he wall. Back and forth he looks, squinting his eyes until t'
	db	'hey go wide with relief.~~"Oh, thank thee for coming. Lord B'
	db	'ritish finally called thee to help us." He's obviously suffe'
	db	'ring from some delusion. "I am Mayor Forsythe. Dost thou thi'
	db	'nk it will take long for thee to defeat the Liche?"'
L0891:	db	00
L0892:	db	'"Ah, hello, '
L089E:	db	00
L089F:	db	'. May I be off assistance to thee?"'
L08C2:	db	00
L08C3:	db	'"Greetings, '
L08CF:	db	00
L08D0:	db	'." The mayor smiles at you half-heartedly.'
L08FA:	db	00
L08FB:	db	00
L08FC:	db	'Is that Liche gone yet? '
L0914:	db	00
L0915:	db	'"Ah yes, good Avatar. 'Tis good to see thee again. '
L0948:	db	00
L0949:	db	'Of what service can I be to one so great as thee?" He bows.'
L0984:	db	00
L0985:	db	'bye'
L0988:	db	00
L0989:	db	'job'
L098C:	db	00
L098D:	db	'name'
L0991:	db	00
L0992:	db	'Liche'
L0997:	db	00
L0998:	db	'name'
L099C:	db	00
L099D:	db	'"As I told thee, my name is Forsythe."'
L09C3:	db	00
L09C4:	db	'name'
L09C8:	db	00
L09C9:	db	'job'
L09CC:	db	00
L09CD:	db	'He seems confused by your question. "Did I not already revea'
	db	'l that? I am the mayor."'
L0A21:	db	00
L0A22:	db	'Tortured One'
L0A2E:	db	00
L0A2F:	db	'Liche'
L0A34:	db	00
L0A35:	db	'"Why yes, the Liche has been a horrible scourge on my poor t'
	db	'own. First he drives away all visitors by raising the dead. '
	db	'Then, in an attempt to stop him, the town is destroyed in a '
	db	'terrible fire. Well, I suppose that is not strictly his faul'
	db	't, but, well, something had to be done about him." Forsythe '
	db	'looks a little flustered.'
L0B7A:	db	00
L0B7B:	db	'Liche'
L0B80:	db	00
L0B81:	db	'his fault'
L0B8A:	db	00
L0B8B:	db	'fire'
L0B8F:	db	00
L0B90:	db	'his fault'
L0B99:	db	00
L0B9A:	db	'"Well, the alchemist is the one who started the fire!"'
L0BD0:	db	00
L0BD1:	db	'his fault'
L0BDA:	db	00
L0BDB:	db	'Tortured One'
L0BE7:	db	00
L0BE8:	db	'"That is what we call Caine. He is the alchemist who created'
	db	' the fire."'
L0C2F:	db	00
L0C30:	db	'fire'
L0C34:	db	00
L0C35:	db	'Tortured One'
L0C41:	db	00
L0C42:	db	'fire'
L0C46:	db	00
L0C47:	db	'He puts his arm around your shoulders and whispers, "Mistres'
	db	's Mordra, our healer, thought she found a way to get rid of '
	db	'Horance once and for all. All we have to do is make a gold c'
	db	'age, or was it an old cage. Well, no matter.~~"We make this '
	db	'cage, and someone..." He smiles at you, "...lowers it into t'
	db	'he Well of Souls to do something or other to it. When this i'
	db	's done, thou shalt catch the Liche off guard late at night a'
	db	'nd snap it tight around him. Sounds easy thus far, yes?~~ "W'
	db	'ell, now. After that, thou needest only pour on him the magi'
	db	'c liquid that the alchemist was making." He pauses here as i'
	db	'f a little embarrassed.~~'
L0EB8:	db	00
L0EB9:	db	'"I apparently got the proportions a bit off when I told the '
	db	'alchemist about the formula. Anyway, it should be as easy as'
	db	' falling off a log, for thee. I guess thou hadst better be r'
	db	'unning along now, Mistress Mordra can tell thee ever so much'
	db	' more about this than can I. Be careful though, she is a dan'
	db	'gerous old wench."'
L0FF7:	db	00
L0FF8:	db	'fire'
L0FFC:	db	00
L0FFD:	db	'"Of course, now thou hast already taken care of all that!" H'
	db	'e smile gracioulsy.'
L104C:	db	00
L104D:	db	'proportions'
L1058:	db	00
L1059:	db	'Mistress Mordra'
L1068:	db	00
L1069:	db	'Horance'
L1070:	db	00
L1071:	db	'proportions'
L107C:	db	00
L107D:	db	'"'Twas so long ago that I barely remember. A smattering of c'
	db	'uring, a dash of a potion of invisibility, and... that's rig'
	db	'ht, a -ton- of the essence of mandrake root!"'
L1122:	db	00
L1123:	db	'proportions'
L112E:	db	00
L112F:	db	'Horance'
L1136:	db	00
L1137:	db	'"Well, if I've got all this Liche lore straight, then, Horan'
	db	'ce, who used to be a good and kindly mage, has become a nast'
	db	'y, horrible, undead mage." He smiles patronizingly. "Now run'
	db	' along. Thou canst ask Mordra if thou needest more informati'
	db	'on."'
L122B:	db	00
L122C:	db	'Horance'
L1233:	db	00
L1234:	db	'Mistress Mordra'
L1243:	db	00
L1244:	db	'"She resides just across the way, and can help thee with eve'
	db	'rything thou mightest need to rid us of the Liche. Thank the'
	db	'e ever so much. It has been nice talking with thee. Goodbye.'
	db	'" He scurries back into his corner and holds his ankh in a p'
	db	'rotective fashion.*'
L1347:	db	00
L1348:	db	'Mistress Mordra'
L1357:	db	00
L1358:	db	'sacrifice'
L1361:	db	00
L1362:	db	'"Oh, goodness no. I do not think I'm the one thou wantest fo'
	db	'r that job. No, I should think not. Maybe thou shouldst ask '
	db	'all of the townsfolk first. If none of them will do it, I mi'
	db	'ght just think about it. Yes, that's right, thou shouldst ju'
	db	'st ask the others, then come back here to tell me who the po'
	db	'or soul is." He smiles at his own cleverness.'
L14BB:	db	00
L14BC:	db	'The Mayor's eyes dart back and forth as you ask him to sacri'
	db	'fice himself for the good of his people. "There is still one'
	db	' thou hast neglected to ask. Go and find '
L155D:	db	00
L155E:	db	'. Then come back and we'll see." Spectral sweat drips from h'
	db	'is ghostly forehead.'
L15AE:	db	00
L15AF:	db	'sacrifice'
L15B8:	db	00
L15B9:	db	'Caine'
L15BE:	db	00
L15BF:	db	'"Just look for the crater near the northeast coast. Thou sha'
	db	'lt find him there."'
L160E:	db	00
L160F:	db	'Rowena'
L1615:	db	00
L1616:	db	'"The town healer said something about Rowena sitting on a th'
	db	'rone in the Dark Tower on the northwestern point."'
L1684:	db	00
L1685:	db	'leave'
L168A:	db	00
L168B:	db	'"As thou wishest!"'
L169D:	db	00
L169E:	db	'Trent'
L16A3:	db	00
L16A4:	db	'"Trent is in the smithy, not far from here, across the road.'
	db	'"'
L16E1:	db	00
L16E2:	db	'Mistress Mordra'
L16F1:	db	00
L16F2:	db	'"She can be found in her house, right across the road."'
L1729:	db	00
L172A:	db	'Quenton'
L1731:	db	00
L1732:	db	'"Quen spends just about all of his time in the Keg Of Spirit'
	db	's tavern, near the ferry dock."'
L178D:	db	00
L178E:	db	'Paulette'
L1796:	db	00
L1797:	db	'"Ah, that lovely girl is the barmaid of the Keg Of Spirits t'
	db	'avern, down by the ferry dock."'
L17F2:	db	00
L17F3:	db	'Markham'
L17FA:	db	00
L17FB:	db	'"That cantankerous man runs the tavern, the Keg Of Spirits. '
	db	'Thou canst find it near the ferry dock."'
L185F:	db	00
L1860:	db	'Ferryman'
L1868:	db	00
L1869:	db	'"Well, now. Just how didst thou come to this island? That is'
	db	' right. -That- ferryman. He is on the ferry of Skara Brae, t'
	db	'o the southeast."'
L18F2:	db	00
L18F3:	db	'bye'
L18F6:	db	00
L18F7:	db	'"Oh, yes, right. If I have forgotten to tell thee something,'
	db	' thou mayest come back and ask, all right." He sighs heavily'
	db	' as you start to leave, then returns to his vigil in the cor'
	db	'ner.*'
L19B0:	db	00
