		.funcnumber	04A6H
		.data
L0000:	db	'bye'
L0003:	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
L0007:	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
L000C:	db	00
L000D:	db	'thief'
L0012:	db	00
L0013:	db	'delivery'
L001B:	db	00
L001C:	db	'Polly'
L0021:	db	00
L0022:	db	'You see a man covered in the sweat of a hard day's work.'
L005A:	db	00
L005B:	db	'"Greetings, '
L0067:	db	00
L0068:	db	'," says Thurston.'
L0079:	db	00
L007A:	db	'name'
L007E:	db	00
L007F:	db	'"I am Thurston."'
L008F:	db	00
L0090:	db	'name'
L0094:	db	00
L0095:	db	'job'
L0098:	db	00
L0099:	db	'"I operate the mill here in Paws."'
L00BB:	db	00
L00BC:	db	'Paws'
L00C0:	db	00
L00C1:	db	'mill'
L00C5:	db	00
L00C6:	db	'mill'
L00CA:	db	00
L00CB:	db	'"The local economy depends upon the mill for flour. So I ens'
	db	'ure that the mill runs. Sometimes, I feel that keeping the w'
	db	'heels turning is the only reason to live."'
L016D:	db	00
L016E:	db	'reason to live'
L017C:	db	00
L017D:	db	'flour'
L0182:	db	00
L0183:	db	'mill'
L0187:	db	00
L0188:	db	'flour'
L018D:	db	00
L018E:	db	'"A sack will cost thee 12 gold. Art thou interested in purch'
	db	'asing some?"'
L01D6:	db	00
L01D7:	db	'"Here it is," he says, handing you the sack. "Wouldst thou w'
	db	'ish another?"*'
L0221:	db	00
L0222:	db	'"Thou hast not the room for this sack."'
L0249:	db	00
L024A:	db	'"Thou hast not the gold for this, '
L026C:	db	00
L026D:	db	'. Perhaps some other time."'
L0288:	db	00
L0289:	db	'"Perhaps next time, '
L029D:	db	00
L029E:	db	'."'
L02A0:	db	00
L02A1:	db	'"The mill is closed at present. If thou wouldst please retur'
	db	'n when it is open again I would gladly sell thee all the flo'
	db	'ur thou canst carry."'
L032E:	db	00
L032F:	db	'flour'
L0334:	db	00
L0335:	db	'Paws'
L0339:	db	00
L033A:	db	'"In case thou hadst not noticed, the people who live here ar'
	db	'e not so well off as their cousins who live in Britain. In f'
	db	'act, we have even had a theft recently."'
L03DA:	db	00
L03DB:	db	'Paws'
L03DF:	db	00
L03E0:	db	'theft'
L03E5:	db	00
L03E6:	db	'theft'
L03EB:	db	00
L03EC:	db	'thief'
L03F1:	db	00
L03F2:	db	'"Indeed, thou shouldst be wary, '
L0412:	db	00
L0413:	db	'. There is a thief in this town! Morfin, a merchant, had sev'
	db	'eral vials of valuable silver snake venom stolen."'
L0481:	db	00
L0482:	db	'thief'
L0487:	db	00
L0488:	db	'theft'
L048D:	db	00
L048E:	db	'snake venom'
L0499:	db	00
L049A:	db	'snake venom'
L04A5:	db	00
L04A6:	db	'"It is procured from the Silver Serpent. I believe Gargoyles'
	db	' used it habitually in the old days. I am not so sure what i'
	db	't might do to a human. Perhaps Morfin can tell thee more."'
L0558:	db	00
L0559:	db	'snake venom'
L0564:	db	00
L0565:	db	'delivery'
L056D:	db	00
L056E:	db	'"I have paid thee once for thy delivery. I shall not do so a'
	db	'gain."'
L05B0:	db	00
L05B1:	db	'You give the sack over to Thurston. He opens it and reaches '
	db	'inside. His hand comes back out filled with wheat. He sifts '
	db	'through it with his fingers. "I know Camille is oft quite bu'
	db	'sy running her farm. Thanks to thee for making the delivery.'
	db	'"'
L06A2:	db	00
L06A3:	db	'"This should compensate thee for thy trouble." He hands you '
	db	'ten gold pieces.'
L06EF:	db	00
L06F0:	db	'"'Tis a puzzlement! Camille promised to make a delivery of w'
	db	'heat to me sometime today and it is late. I wonder where it '
	db	'could be."'
L0772:	db	00
L0773:	db	'delivery'
L077B:	db	00
L077C:	db	'reason to live'
L078A:	db	00
L078B:	db	'"I have no wife or family. I have thought about joining The '
	db	'Fellowship, but I refuse. I have nothing but my work, and a '
	db	'drink at the Salty Dog now and then."'
L0828:	db	00
L0829:	db	'reason to live'
L0837:	db	00
L0838:	db	'Salty Dog'
L0841:	db	00
L0842:	db	'Fellowship'
L084C:	db	00
L084D:	db	'Fellowship'
L0857:	db	00
L0858:	db	'"I know they do good work here in town, but there is just so'
	db	'mething about them that makes me uncomfortable."'
L08C4:	db	00
L08C5:	db	'He notices your Fellowship medallion and hurriedly clears hi'
	db	's throat. "No offense intended, '
L0921:	db	00
L0922:	db	'."'
L0924:	db	00
L0925:	db	'Fellowship'
L092F:	db	00
L0930:	db	'Salty Dog'
L0939:	db	00
L093A:	db	'"In truth, I go there more to be near Polly, the innkeeper, '
	db	'than for the wine. But she is always busy tending bar and ha'
	db	's no time for me, I am sure."'
L09CF:	db	00
L09D0:	db	'"I should go to the Salty Dog and see Polly." Thurston stare'
	db	's off into space for a few moments, his eyes are big and he '
	db	'has a moony expression on his face. Suddenly, he snaps back '
	db	'to reality. "Excuse me, thou wert saying something?"'
L0AB8:	db	00
L0AB9:	db	'Salty Dog'
L0AC2:	db	00
L0AC3:	db	'Polly'
L0AC8:	db	00
L0AC9:	db	'You relate to Thurston what Polly had said about him. He loo'
	db	'ks at you with joyous surprise. "Did Polly really say these '
	db	'things?! It is ridiculous that she believes I am too good fo'
	db	'r her!" Suddenly he forgets his work and starts hurrying aro'
	db	'und in excitement. "For years I have loved this woman from a'
	db	'far. I will begin courting her immediately!"'
L0C21:	db	00
L0C22:	db	'"I want to thank thee for telling me the truth about Polly's'
	db	' feelings about me. I can be such a stick in the mud running'
	db	' this bloody mill all of the time that I would never have no'
	db	'ticed it if she were wearing a sign on her back! This is jus'
	db	't what I needed to help me start enjoying my life!"'
L0D45:	db	00
L0D46:	db	'Polly'
L0D4B:	db	00
L0D4C:	db	'bye'
L0D4F:	db	00
L0D50:	db	'"Good day to thee, '
L0D63:	db	00
L0D64:	db	'."*'
L0D67:	db	00
