		.funcnumber	04B2H
		.data
L0000:	db	'bye'
L0003:	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
L0007:	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
L000C:	db	00
L000D:	db	'thief'
L0012:	db	00
L0013:	db	'venom'
L0018:	db	00
L0019:	db	'You see a sulking lad, who doesn't seem to want to look you '
	db	'in the eye.'
L0060:	db	00
L0061:	db	'"Just what I need. Another Avatar," he mumbles under his bre'
	db	'ath.'
L00A1:	db	00
L00A2:	db	'"Yes, Avatar?" Tobias asks.'
L00BD:	db	00
L00BE:	db	'"What dost thou want?" Tobias asks.'
L00E1:	db	00
L00E2:	db	'name'
L00E6:	db	00
L00E7:	db	'"I am still Tobias!"'
L00FB:	db	00
L00FC:	db	'"I am Tobias. I suppose I am to believe thou art someone imp'
	db	'ortant."'
L0140:	db	00
L0141:	db	'name'
L0145:	db	00
L0146:	db	'job'
L0149:	db	00
L014A:	db	'"I am too young to have a job. I just help my mother on the '
	db	'farm."'
L018C:	db	00
L018D:	db	'farm'
L0191:	db	00
L0192:	db	'mother'
L0198:	db	00
L0199:	db	'mother'
L019F:	db	00
L01A0:	db	'"Her name is Camille. She speaks of thee. Or rather she spea'
	db	'ks of the Avatar, is what I meant to say. Some people in tow'
	db	'n think she is mad because she still believes in the Eight V'
	db	'irtues."'
L025C:	db	00
L025D:	db	'"Thou hast already met her."'
L0279:	db	00
L027A:	db	'"But thanks to thee I have more respect for her beliefs."'
L02B3:	db	00
L02B4:	db	'mother'
L02BA:	db	00
L02BB:	db	'Eight Virtues'
L02C8:	db	00
L02C9:	db	'Avatar'
L02CF:	db	00
L02D0:	db	'Avatar'
L02D6:	db	00
L02D7:	db	'"Art thou truly the Avatar?"'
L02F3:	db	00
L02F4:	db	'"Yes, I do believe thou art the true Avatar." Tobias smiles '
	db	'briefly.'
L0338:	db	00
L0339:	db	'"Thou art no Avatar!" Tobias frowns.'
L035D:	db	00
L035E:	db	'"I think that thou mayest have a little bit of the way of th'
	db	'e Avatar about thee. There is a little bit of the Avatar in '
	db	'everyone, or so my mother says."'
L03F6:	db	00
L03F7:	db	'"I knew that thou wert nothing but an imposter."'
L0427:	db	00
L0428:	db	'Avatar'
L042E:	db	00
L042F:	db	'Eight Virtues'
L043C:	db	00
L043D:	db	'"My mother once took me to the Shrine of Sacrifice when I wa'
	db	's younger. That was soon after my father died so I do not re'
	db	'member it very well.~~I do not think it is there anymore, fo'
	db	'r she never talks about going back.~~I think that perhaps sh'
	db	'e does not want to mention it because there are so many in t'
	db	'own who belong to The Fellowship. And because it makes her s'
	db	'ad."'
L05A9:	db	00
L05AA:	db	'Eight Virtues'
L05B7:	db	00
L05B8:	db	'Fellowship'
L05C2:	db	00
L05C3:	db	'farm'
L05C7:	db	00
L05C8:	db	'"My mother grows grain."'
L05E0:	db	00
L05E1:	db	'"Dost thou not know a farm when thou dost see one?"'
L0614:	db	00
L0615:	db	'"Surely thou canst find the farm. It is just north of the sh'
	db	'elter."'
L0658:	db	00
L0659:	db	'Tobias looks at you as if he thinks you are a bit dim.'
L068F:	db	00
L0690:	db	'farm'
L0694:	db	00
L0695:	db	'shelter'
L069C:	db	00
L069D:	db	'grain'
L06A2:	db	00
L06A3:	db	'grain'
L06A8:	db	00
L06A9:	db	'"She sells grain to Thurston the miller from time to time so'
	db	' that we may go to the pub or buy milk at the dairy every on'
	db	'ce in a while, but we usually just grow crops to keep oursel'
	db	'ves fed."'
L0766:	db	00
L0767:	db	'dairy'
L076C:	db	00
L076D:	db	'Thurston'
L0775:	db	00
L0776:	db	'grain'
L077B:	db	00
L077C:	db	'shelter'
L0783:	db	00
L0784:	db	'"It's that place just south of here. It's run by The Fellows'
	db	'hip."'
L07C5:	db	00
L07C6:	db	'shelter'
L07CD:	db	00
L07CE:	db	'Fellowship'
L07D8:	db	00
L07D9:	db	'Thurston'
L07E1:	db	00
L07E2:	db	'"He is one of the few people in town that I like. He is nice'
	db	' to us."'
L0826:	db	00
L0827:	db	'Thurston'
L082F:	db	00
L0830:	db	'dairy'
L0835:	db	00
L0836:	db	'"The dairy is south of the shelter. Andrew -- the man who ru'
	db	'ns the dairy -- his father was friends with my father."'
L08A9:	db	00
L08AA:	db	'dairy'
L08AF:	db	00
L08B0:	db	'Fellowship'
L08BA:	db	00
L08BB:	db	'For the first time he looks you in the eye. "I hate The Fell'
	db	'owship! The only other person in town mine own age is that c'
	db	'retin Garritt and it is all he ever talks about! He is alway'
	db	's trying to convince my mother to join." He clenches his fis'
	db	't angrily. "Please do not mention them again."'
L09D9:	db	00
L09DA:	db	'mother join?'
L09E6:	db	00
L09E7:	db	'Garritt'
L09EE:	db	00
L09EF:	db	'Fellowship'
L09F9:	db	00
L09FA:	db	'mother join?'
L0A06:	db	00
L0A07:	db	'"Those bloody Fellowship people know that everyone is never '
	db	'more than a meal away from being penniless. They say that th'
	db	'ey want us to join immediately because the shelter is intend'
	db	'ed to help only Fellowship members. If we ever need to live '
	db	'there they may have to turn us away in favor of other Fellow'
	db	'ship members."'
L0B41:	db	00
L0B42:	db	'mother join?'
L0B4E:	db	00
L0B4F:	db	'thief'
L0B54:	db	00
L0B55:	db	'"There is a thief running free in Paws! He stole silver serp'
	db	'ent venom from Morfin, owner of the slaughterhouse. No one k'
	db	'nows who he is."'
L0BDD:	db	00
L0BDE:	db	'thief'
L0BE3:	db	00
L0BE4:	db	'venom'
L0BE9:	db	00
L0BEA:	db	'"I do not know anything about the stolen venom. I am falsely'
	db	' accused!"'
L0C30:	db	00
L0C31:	db	'venom'
L0C36:	db	00
L0C37:	db	'falsely accused'
L0C46:	db	00
L0C47:	db	'falsely accused'
L0C56:	db	00
L0C57:	db	'"That is right! Garritt did it. I just know it. He was in my'
	db	' room the other day when I came in from the fields. He said '
	db	'he was looking for a ball, but I do not believe him. Thou ca'
	db	'nst believe me or not, I do not care. But if thou art truly '
	db	'the Avatar, thou wilt know I am telling the truth."'
L0D7A:	db	00
L0D7B:	db	'falsely accused'
L0D8A:	db	00
L0D8B:	db	'Garritt'
L0D92:	db	00
L0D93:	db	'You tell Tobias how you discovered that Garritt was the thie'
	db	'f. "Thank thee, '
L0DDF:	db	00
L0DE0:	db	', for not believing I was the guilty one. I am not sure if t'
	db	'hou art truly the real Avatar but thou dost certainly have t'
	db	'he way of the Avatar about thee."'
L0E79:	db	00
L0E7A:	db	'"He is the only other boy in town anywhere near mine age. Hi'
	db	's parents do not want him playing with me because they think'
	db	' that 'associating with those kind of people' will 'hamper h'
	db	'is education' or some such rubbish. I cannot stand the littl'
	db	'e bastard. And I hate the way he plays those stinking whistl'
	db	'e panpipes!"'
L0FB2:	db	00
L0FB3:	db	'"That spoiled brat Garritt must have planted the venom in my'
	db	' room! He is usually lounging about, even if his parents dis'
	db	'approve of him playing with me. I know he is up to something'
	db	' no good! Thou shouldst look in HIS room!"'
L1091:	db	00
L1092:	db	'Garritt'
L1099:	db	00
L109A:	db	'bye'
L109D:	db	00
L109E:	db	'"Goodbye, Avatar. Good luck to thee."*'
L10C4:	db	00
L10C5:	db	'"Be on thy way then, o great and wise Avatar."*'
L10F4:	db	00
