L0000:	db	'bye'
L0003:	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
L0007:	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
L000C:	db	00
L000D:	db	'You are greeted with a stern look on this man's face.'
L0042:	db	00
L0043:	db	'"^'
L0045:	db	00
L0046:	db	'." He nods at you.'
L0058:	db	00
L0059:	db	'statue'
L005F:	db	00
L0060:	db	'name'
L0064:	db	00
L0065:	db	'"Thou mayest call me Sir Pendaran."'
L0088:	db	00
L0089:	db	'name'
L008D:	db	00
L008E:	db	'job'
L0091:	db	00
L0092:	db	'"I am a knight here in Serpent's Hold. 'Tis my job to help p'
	db	'rotect the citizens of Britannia."'
L00F0:	db	00
L00F1:	db	'Serpent's Hold'
L00FF:	db	00
L0100:	db	'protect'
L0107:	db	00
L0108:	db	'protect'
L010F:	db	00
L0110:	db	'"Aye, '
L0116:	db	00
L0117:	db	'. Britannia can be a dangerous place outside town boundaries'
	db	'. Especially now that the ruling faction have gone soft!"'
L018C:	db	00
L018D:	db	'protect'
L0194:	db	00
L0195:	db	'soft'
L0199:	db	00
L019A:	db	'ruling faction'
L01A8:	db	00
L01A9:	db	'ruling faction'
L01B7:	db	00
L01B8:	db	'"Well, I mean Lord British and his advisors."'
L01E5:	db	00
L01E6:	db	'ruling faction'
L01F4:	db	00
L01F5:	db	'worthless'
L01FE:	db	00
L01FF:	db	'soft'
L0203:	db	00
L0204:	db	'"Though I'd follow the land's ideals to the ends of the land'
	db	', I find it difficult to accept how poor the conditions are '
	db	'in Britannia. Brigands populate the land, disease overruns t'
	db	'he towns, and corruption fills the councils. Were it not for'
	db	' The Fellowship, I would be hard pressed to avoid falling on'
	db	' mine own blade, despite how dishonorable an act that may se'
	db	'em."'
L0370:	db	00
L0371:	db	'worthless'
L037A:	db	00
L037B:	db	'soft'
L037F:	db	00
L0380:	db	'Fellowship'
L038A:	db	00
L038B:	db	'Fellowship'
L0395:	db	00
L0396:	db	'"A noble group of people who strive to instill a greater sen'
	db	'se of spiritual knowledge throughout all of Britannia. 'Twil'
	db	'l be but a matter of time, '
L0429:	db	00
L042A:	db	', before all people will see the wisdom."'
L0453:	db	00
L0454:	db	'Fellowship'
L045E:	db	00
L045F:	db	'Serpent's Hold'
L046D:	db	00
L046E:	db	'"I live here in the hold with my lady."'
L0495:	db	00
L0496:	db	'lady'
L049A:	db	00
L049B:	db	'Serpent's Hold'
L04A9:	db	00
L04AA:	db	'lady'
L04AE:	db	00
L04AF:	db	'"Her name is Jehanne, '
L04C5:	db	00
L04C6:	db	'," he says suspiciously. "She is the provisioner."'
L04F8:	db	00
L04F9:	db	'lady'
L04FD:	db	00
L04FE:	db	'statue'
L0504:	db	00
L0505:	db	'"Terrible shame, '
L0516:	db	00
L0517:	db	'." He eyes you coldly.'
L052D:	db	00
L052E:	db	'Thou didst do it!'
L053F:	db	00
L0540:	db	'statue'
L0546:	db	00
L0547:	db	'Thou didst do it!'
L0558:	db	00
L0559:	db	'"What! Thou art accusing me! Preposterous. I had nothing to '
	db	'do with it!"'
L05A1:	db	00
L05A2:	db	'Thou didst do it!'
L05B3:	db	00
L05B4:	db	'Lady Jehanne'
L05C0:	db	00
L05C1:	db	'Lady Jehanne'
L05CD:	db	00
L05CE:	db	'He shakes his head.~~"Thou wouldst take the word of a woman '
	db	'over that of a knight of the Hold? Thou art lower than a wor'
	db	'm!" He glares at you for a moment, and then his expression c'
	db	'hanges.~~"All right," he says, "I am the one	who defaced the'
	db	' statue, but only because the government has become so worth'
	db	'less and soft!" He quickly turns away from	you, ashamed.~~"I'
	db	'f thou dost think it best," he sighs, "tomorrow I shall beg '
	db	'forgiveness from my fellow knights."'
L0796:	db	00
L0797:	db	'no need'
L079E:	db	00
L079F:	db	''tis best'
L07A8:	db	00
L07A9:	db	''tis best'
L07B2:	db	00
L07B3:	db	'Nodding his agreement, he sighs again, and turns away.*'
L07EA:	db	00
L07EB:	db	'no need'
L07F2:	db	00
L07F3:	db	'"No, no, '
L07FC:	db	00
L07FD:	db	'. Thou hast shown me the way. I must repent." He turns away '
	db	'from you to reflect on his decision.*'
L085E:	db	00
L085F:	db	'bye'
L0862:	db	00
L0863:	db	'"Good day to thee, '
L0876:	db	00
L0877:	db	'."*'
