		.data
L0000:	db	'bye'
L0003:	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
L0007:	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
L000C:	db	00
L000D:	db	' standing at attention just behind Lord John-Paul.'
L003F:	db	00
L0040:	db	' standing at attention just behind another knight.'
L0072:	db	00
L0073:	db	'.'
L0074:	db	00
L0075:	db	'You see a gargoyle with a very stern expression on his face'
L00B0:	db	00
L00B1:	db	00
L00B2:	db	'"To ask how to be of assistance." His eyes narrow.'
L00E4:	db	00
L00E5:	db	'statue'
L00EB:	db	00
L00EC:	db	'Pendaran did it'
L00FB:	db	00
L00FC:	db	'name'
L0100:	db	00
L0101:	db	'"To be named Horffe."'
L0116:	db	00
L0117:	db	'name'
L011B:	db	00
L011C:	db	'job'
L011F:	db	00
L0120:	db	'"To be the Captain of the guard. To serve and protect the pe'
	db	'ople of Serpent's Hold."'
L0174:	db	00
L0175:	db	'Serpent's Hold'
L0183:	db	00
L0184:	db	'Captain'
L018B:	db	00
L018C:	db	'Captain'
L0193:	db	00
L0194:	db	'"To have been commanded to protect the people who live in Se'
	db	'rpent's Hold and to maintain the general order of the knight'
	db	's."'
L020F:	db	00
L0210:	db	'Captain'
L0217:	db	00
L0218:	db	'knights'
L021F:	db	00
L0220:	db	'people'
L0226:	db	00
L0227:	db	'people'
L022D:	db	00
L022E:	db	'Serpent's Hold'
L023C:	db	00
L023D:	db	'"To direct you to Sir Denton, the tavernkeeper at the Hallow'
	db	'ed Dock. To know more about the Hold and the people than I."'
L02B5:	db	00
L02B6:	db	'Serpent's Hold'
L02C4:	db	00
L02C5:	db	'people'
L02CB:	db	00
L02CC:	db	'Pendaran did it'
L02DB:	db	00
L02DC:	db	'"To thank you for this information. To be pleased to know th'
	db	'e identity of my assailant."'
L0334:	db	00
L0335:	db	'Pendaran did it'
L0344:	db	00
L0345:	db	'knights'
L034C:	db	00
L034D:	db	'"To inform you that many fine warriors take up residence bet'
	db	'ween the Hold's walls. To have little fear of an attack from'
	db	' bandits or vicious animals."'
L03E2:	db	00
L03E3:	db	'knights'
L03EA:	db	00
L03EB:	db	'statue'
L03F1:	db	00
L03F2:	db	'"To know nothing about that!"'
L040F:	db	00
L0410:	db	'blood on fragments'
L0422:	db	00
L0423:	db	'statue'
L0429:	db	00
L042A:	db	'blood on fragments'
L043C:	db	00
L043D:	db	'His rough demeanor softens.~~"To be my blood." He sighs. "Bu'
	db	't to be not the one who defaced the statue! To have been wou'
	db	'nded while trying to stop the vandal."'
L04DB:	db	00
L04DC:	db	'vandal'
L04E2:	db	00
L04E3:	db	'blood on fragments'
L04F5:	db	00
L04F6:	db	'vandal'
L04FC:	db	00
L04FD:	db	'He looks down at his feet.~~"To know not who he was. To have'
	db	' been very dark. To ask you not to tell Sir Richter."'
L056E:	db	00
L056F:	db	'vandal'
L0575:	db	00
L0576:	db	'Sir Richter'
L0581:	db	00
L0582:	db	'dark'
L0586:	db	00
L0587:	db	'dark'
L058B:	db	00
L058C:	db	'"To have been very poor visibility, but to be positive I was'
	db	' scuffling with an armed knight."'
L05E9:	db	00
L05EA:	db	'dark'
L05EE:	db	00
L05EF:	db	'Sir Richter'
L05FA:	db	00
L05FB:	db	'"To know he will not believe one who openly defies The Fello'
	db	'wship."'
L063E:	db	00
L063F:	db	'Sir Richter'
L064A:	db	00
L064B:	db	'Fellowship'
L0655:	db	00
L0656:	db	'Fellowship'
L0660:	db	00
L0661:	db	'"To know little about it. To like little about it."'
L0694:	db	00
L0695:	db	'Fellowship'
L069F:	db	00
L06A0:	db	'bye'
L06A3:	db	00
L06A4:	db	'"To say goodbye."*'
L06B6:	db	00
