L0000:	db	'bye'
L0003:	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
L0007:	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
L000C:	db	00
L000D:	db	'The woman smiles at you compassionately.'
L0035:	db	00
L0036:	db	'Tory smiles and reaches out to you. "Hello, '
L0062:	db	00
L0063:	db	'. I sense thou art troubled."'
L0080:	db	00
L0081:	db	'statue'
L0087:	db	00
L0088:	db	'Riky'
L008C:	db	00
L008D:	db	'name'
L0091:	db	00
L0092:	db	'"I am Lady Tory, '
L00A3:	db	00
L00A4:	db	'."'
L00A6:	db	00
L00A7:	db	'"Mother of Riky," she says, sobbing.'
L00CB:	db	00
L00CC:	db	'Riky'
L00D0:	db	00
L00D1:	db	'name'
L00D5:	db	00
L00D6:	db	'job'
L00D9:	db	00
L00DA:	db	'"My job is to provide counsel for Lord John-Paul and anyone '
	db	'else in need of guidance here at the Hold."'
L0141:	db	00
L0142:	db	'Hold'
L0146:	db	00
L0147:	db	'Lord John-Paul'
L0155:	db	00
L0156:	db	'Riky'
L015A:	db	00
L015B:	db	'"Hast thou found my child?"'
L0176:	db	00
L0177:	db	'"I cannot begin to express my gratitude, '
L01A0:	db	00
L01A1:	db	'. Thank thee ever so much!"~She begins sobbing for joy. "Pl-'
	db	'please set him back gently in the cradle."'
L0207:	db	00
L0208:	db	'"Why, that's not my little Riky, '
L0229:	db	00
L022A:	db	'. Thou hast someone else's child. Oh, where could my boy hav'
	db	'e been taken?" she says, crying.'
L0286:	db	00
L0287:	db	'"But, I see no child with thee. Thine humor is quite dark. P'
	db	'lease return when thou art carrying my baby boy!"*'
L02F5:	db	00
L02F6:	db	'"Please, I beseech thee, continue thine hunt!"'
L0324:	db	00
L0325:	db	'"My poor baby boy. He -- he was taken one night by cruel har'
	db	'pies who wanted a child for their own. I -- I know not where'
	db	' they have taken him, but I have heard some of the knights m'
	db	'ention that a group of the vile women-birds cluster around t'
	db	'he shrine of Honor. But, they have not yet been able to defe'
	db	'at them." She sniffs. "But thou '
L0471:	db	00
L0472:	db	', thou wilt help me get my child back. Oh, please, wilt thou'
	db	'?"'
L04B0:	db	00
L04B1:	db	'"I cannot thank thee enough for helping me!" She appears to '
	db	'have cheered up greatly.'
L0505:	db	00
L0506:	db	'"Thou art a no more than a coward. Get thee gone, coward!"'
L0540:	db	00
L0541:	db	'Riky'
L0545:	db	00
L0546:	db	'statue'
L054C:	db	00
L054D:	db	'"Hmm," she appears thoughtful, "when the incident was brough'
	db	't up to everyone here at the hold, I remember Sir Jordan bec'
	db	'oming a bit nervous. Perhaps thou shouldst speak with him."'
L0600:	db	00
L0601:	db	'statue'
L0607:	db	00
L0608:	db	'Hold'
L060C:	db	00
L060D:	db	'"I sense that thou wishest to know about the residents here '
	db	'at Serpent's Hold. Is this correct?"'
L066D:	db	00
L066E:	db	'"Very well. Come to me if thou changest thy mind."'
L06A0:	db	00
L06A1:	db	'"As counselor for the Hold, I can tell thee about many peopl'
	db	'e. Hast thou met the healer or the provisioner? And, as a wa'
	db	'rrior thyself, thou mayest wish to visit the trainer and the'
	db	' armourer."'
L0760:	db	00
L0761:	db	'Lord John-Paul'
L076F:	db	00
L0770:	db	'provisioner'
L077B:	db	00
L077C:	db	'trainer'
L0783:	db	00
L0784:	db	'armourer'
L078C:	db	00
L078D:	db	'healer'
L0793:	db	00
L0794:	db	'Hold'
L0798:	db	00
L0799:	db	'Lord John-Paul'
L07A7:	db	00
L07A8:	db	'"He is an extraordinary leader. Everyone looks up to him. Th'
	db	'ou hast only to ask his captain."'
L0805:	db	00
L0806:	db	'Lord John-Paul'
L0814:	db	00
L0815:	db	'captain'
L081C:	db	00
L081D:	db	'healer'
L0823:	db	00
L0824:	db	'"Lady Leigh is very skilled as a healer. I have yet to see h'
	db	'er lose a patient."'
L0873:	db	00
L0874:	db	'healer'
L087A:	db	00
L087B:	db	'armourer'
L0883:	db	00
L0884:	db	'"Hmmm. Well, Sir Richter has changed much recently -- ever s'
	db	'ince he joined The Fellowship. He seems a little less compas'
	db	'sionate."'
L0905:	db	00
L0906:	db	'Fellowship'
L0910:	db	00
L0911:	db	'armourer'
L0919:	db	00
L091A:	db	'tavernkeeper'
L0926:	db	00
L0927:	db	'"Sir Denton is the most astute man I have ever met. He is th'
	db	'e only one I cannot sense. And I have never seen him remove '
	db	'his armour...." She shrugs.'
L09BA:	db	00
L09BB:	db	'tavernkeeper'
L09C7:	db	00
L09C8:	db	'trainer'
L09CF:	db	00
L09D0:	db	'"I know Menion least of all. He is very quiet, spending most'
	db	' of his spare time weaponsmithing. The tavernkeeper may know'
	db	' more about him."'
L0A59:	db	00
L0A5A:	db	'tavernkeeper'
L0A66:	db	00
L0A67:	db	'trainer'
L0A6E:	db	00
L0A6F:	db	'provisioner'
L0A7A:	db	00
L0A7B:	db	'"Her name is Lady Jehanne. She is the Lady of Sir Pendaran,"'
	db	' she says with a gleam in her eye.'
L0AD9:	db	00
L0ADA:	db	'Sir Pendaran'
L0AE6:	db	00
L0AE7:	db	'provisioner'
L0AF2:	db	00
L0AF3:	db	'captain'
L0AFA:	db	00
L0AFB:	db	'"The Captain of the guard, Sir Horffe, is a gargoyle. He was'
	db	' found by two humans who raised him to be a valiant knight. '
	db	'He is a very dedicated warrior, and rarely leaves Lord John-'
	db	'Paul's side."'
L0BBC:	db	00
L0BBD:	db	'Gargish accent'
L0BCB:	db	00
L0BCC:	db	'captain'
L0BD3:	db	00
L0BD4:	db	'Gargish accent'
L0BE2:	db	00
L0BE3:	db	'"Despite his human upbringing, Horffe has struggled to maint'
	db	'ain his Gargish identity. By speaking in the same manner as '
	db	'his brethren, he feels he can better hold on to his backgrou'
	db	'nd."'
L0C9B:	db	00
L0C9C:	db	'Gargish accent'
L0CAA:	db	00
L0CAB:	db	'Sir Pendaran'
L0CB7:	db	00
L0CB8:	db	'"He is a brave and hearty fighter, and," she smiles, "he is '
	db	'also a bit on the attractive side."'
L0D17:	db	00
L0D18:	db	'Sir Pendaran'
L0D24:	db	00
L0D25:	db	'Fellowship'
L0D2F:	db	00
L0D30:	db	'"The Fellowship does not have a branch here, but two of our '
	db	'knights are members: Sir Richter and Sir Pendaran. I know th'
	db	'ey are interested in having Sir Jordan join as well."'
L0DDD:	db	00
L0DDE:	db	'Fellowship'
L0DE8:	db	00
L0DE9:	db	'Sir Jordan'
L0DF3:	db	00
L0DF4:	db	'Sir Jordan'
L0DFE:	db	00
L0DFF:	db	'"He is a wonder. Despite his blindness, he fights with amazi'
	db	'ng deftness. In fact, he also enjoys toying with mechanical '
	db	'items, and his loss of eyesight does not seem to affect that'
	db	', either.~~"However, I sense in him a very recent change, re'
	db	'markably like that in Sir Richter. He would be an interestin'
	db	'g one to speak with. Thou mayest find him at Iolo's South."*'
L0F67:	db	00
L0F68:	db	'Iolo smiles proudly.~~"My shop has, er, grown a bit since th'
	db	'ou wert here last, '
L0FB7:	db	00
L0FB8:	db	'."'
L0FBA:	db	00
L0FBB:	db	'Sir Jordan'
L0FC5:	db	00
L0FC6:	db	'bye'
L0FC9:	db	00
L0FCA:	db	'"I sense thou hast pressing engagements elsewhere. I bid the'
	db	'e farewell."*'
L1013:	db	00
