L0000:	db	'the Avatar'
L000A:	db	00
L000B:	db	'bye'
L000E:	db	00
L000F:	db	'job'
L0012:	db	00
L0013:	db	'name'
L0017:	db	00
L0018:	db	'"Ah, me good friend, Dupre. What kinna do fer ye this fine d'
	db	'ay?"'
L0058:	db	00
L0059:	db	'"Ah, master Yongi, always ready to offer a tankard of thy fi'
	db	'nest."'
L009B:	db	00
L009C:	db	'Tending the bar is a jovial-looking man. "Welcome ta the Gil'
	db	'ded Lizard."'
L00E4:	db	00
L00E5:	db	'"Welcome back ta the Gilded Lizard. What may I do fer ye?" a'
	db	'sks Yongi.'
L012B:	db	00
L012C:	db	'name'
L0130:	db	00
L0131:	db	'"Me name is Yongi, '
L0144:	db	00
L0145:	db	'."'
L0147:	db	00
L0148:	db	'name'
L014C:	db	00
L014D:	db	'"And ye are?"'
L015A:	db	00
L015B:	db	'"Aye, '
L0161:	db	00
L0162:	db	'. Right ye are. If ye dinna care ta tell me, I don't mind a '
	db	'bit." He winks.'
L01AD:	db	00
L01AE:	db	'"Welcome ta me tavern, '
L01C5:	db	00
L01C6:	db	'."'
L01C8:	db	00
L01C9:	db	'"Right ye are, '
L01D8:	db	00
L01D9:	db	'. There's no need ta tell anyone yer name."'
L0204:	db	00
L0205:	db	'job'
L0208:	db	00
L0209:	db	'"Why, I tend me bar. And lend me ear ta the customers," he a'
	db	'dds, touching his right ear for emphasis.'
L026E:	db	00
L026F:	db	'buy'
L0272:	db	00
L0273:	db	'customers'
L027C:	db	00
L027D:	db	'Vesper'
L0283:	db	00
L0284:	db	'"Why, I wouldna wanna live anyplace else. 'Course, this town'
	db	' would be a better place if we could rid ourselves of those '
	db	'jackals, the gargoyles."'
L0314:	db	00
L0315:	db	'gargoyles'
L031E:	db	00
L031F:	db	'Vesper'
L0325:	db	00
L0326:	db	'gargoyles'
L032F:	db	00
L0330:	db	'"Gargoyles! What about them? They be the vilest, evilest, cr'
	db	'uelest, most despicable things ever ta crawl upon this great'
	db	' land. I kinna tell ye too well ta stay away from them. I ki'
	db	'n only imagine whata fine town this'd be if there weren't na'
	db	' more gargoyles. 'Course, I know those dogs are probably say'
	db	'in' the same about us. Everybody knows they're gonna come an'
	db	'' kill allus in our sleep one evenin'."'
L04BF:	db	00
L04C0:	db	'"Why, only the other day one attacked Blorn. G'won, ask him '
	db	'about it."'
L0506:	db	00
L0507:	db	'Blorn'
L050C:	db	00
L050D:	db	'gargoyles'
L0516:	db	00
L0517:	db	'customers'
L0520:	db	00
L0521:	db	'"Well, all I really know in Vesper are me regulars: Cador, M'
	db	'ara, and Blorn. Ye might be wantin' ta talk to Auston, the m'
	db	'ayor, or his clerk, Liana. Ah, now there's a fine, young las'
	db	's." He winks at you.'
L05E9:	db	00
L05EA:	db	'Vesper'
L05F0:	db	00
L05F1:	db	'Blorn'
L05F6:	db	00
L05F7:	db	'Mara'
L05FB:	db	00
L05FC:	db	'Cador'
L0601:	db	00
L0602:	db	'customers'
L060B:	db	00
L060C:	db	'Cador'
L0611:	db	00
L0612:	db	'"He used ta come here every night, 'til he was killed in a b'
	db	'rawl." The bartender's eyes narrow as he talks.'
L067D:	db	00
L067E:	db	'"He be in here every night after work. Good man, hard worker'
	db	'."'
L06BC:	db	00
L06BD:	db	'Cador'
L06C2:	db	00
L06C3:	db	'Mara'
L06C7:	db	00
L06C8:	db	'"She worked with Cador at the mines. She was more man than m'
	db	'ost men, that one was. An' she died like it, too -- in a bra'
	db	'wl here at the tavern!" He says, eyeing you suspiciously.'
L0779:	db	00
L077A:	db	'"She works with Cador at the mines. Hard as stone, that one.'
	db	' She be more man than most of the men in town."'
L07E5:	db	00
L07E6:	db	'Mara'
L07EA:	db	00
L07EB:	db	'Blorn'
L07F0:	db	00
L07F1:	db	'"There be one who knows what's what. He knows what be wrong '
	db	'with this town! Gargoyles! That is what be wrong. He hates ''
	db	'em, 'e does."'
L0876:	db	00
L0877:	db	'"He was even accosted by one of those jackals not too long a'
	db	'go. Ask 'im about it, why don't ye."'
