L0026:	db	00
L0027:	db	'You see before you a young girl with a carefree expression. '
	db	'As she notices you, her eyes grow wide as she exclaims, "Tho'
	db	'u art the person in one of For... one of -my- story books! T'
	db	'hou art the Avatar!"'
L00EF:	db	00
L00F0:	db	'"How dost thou do, '
L0103:	db	00
L0104:	db	' Avatar?" She curtseys.'
L011B:	db	00
L011C:	db	'name'
L0120:	db	00
L0121:	db	'"My name is Catherine, '
L0138:	db	00
L0139:	db	' Avatar."'
L0142:	db	00
L0143:	db	'name'
L0147:	db	00
L0148:	db	'job'
L014B:	db	00
L014C:	db	'"I have no job, '
L015C:	db	00
L015D:	db	' Avatar. I live with my father and mother here in Vesper."'
L0197:	db	00
L0198:	db	'Vesper'
L019E:	db	00
L019F:	db	'mother'
L01A5:	db	00
L01A6:	db	'father'
L01AC:	db	00
L01AD:	db	'father'
L01B3:	db	00
L01B4:	db	'"He is the overseer at the mines, '
L01D6:	db	00
L01D7:	db	' Avatar."'
L01E0:	db	00
L01E1:	db	'"Of course, he's gone now..." She looks down at her feet.'
L021A:	db	00
L021B:	db	'father'
L0221:	db	00
L0222:	db	'mother'
L0228:	db	00
L0229:	db	'"Yes, '
L022F:	db	00
L0230:	db	' Avatar. She is there right now." She points, apparently ind'
	db	'icating her house.'
L027E:	db	00
L027F:	db	'mother'
L0285:	db	00
L0286:	db	'Vesper'
L028C:	db	00
L028D:	db	'"That is the name of our city, '
L02AC:	db	00
L02AD:	db	' Avatar. If thou art lost, thou mayest wish to speak with th'
	db	'e town clerk."'
L02F7:	db	00
L02F8:	db	'Vesper'
L02FE:	db	00
L02FF:	db	'gargoyle'
L0307:	db	00
L0308:	db	'"I'm sorry, '
L0314:	db	00
L0315:	db	' Avatar, my mother told me never to speak with strangers." S'
	db	'he quickly turns away.*'
L0368:	db	00
L0369:	db	'For-Lem'
L0370:	db	00
L0371:	db	'A tear glistens as it rolls gently down her cheek. "He is no'
	db	' more. My -- my father killed him for talking to me, and -- '
	db	'and 'tis all thy fault!" She turns away, sobbing.*'
L041B:	db	00
L041C:	db	'bye'
L041F:	db	00
L0420:	db	'"Goodbye, '
L042A:	db	00
L042B:	db	' Avatar."*'
