L0000:	db	'"Go away, bee killers!"*'
L0018:	db	00
L0019:	db	'bye'
L001C:	db	00
L001D:	db	'job'
L0020:	db	00
L0021:	db	'name'
L0025:	db	00
L0026:	db	'You see a naked man who looks a bit wild. He is not in the l'
	db	'east concerned that he has on no clothes.'
L008B:	db	00
L008C:	db	'"Huh?" asks Papa.'
L009D:	db	00
L009E:	db	'name'
L00A2:	db	00
L00A3:	db	'"I am Murray."'
L00B1:	db	00
L00B2:	db	'"Me Papa!" The man grins, revealing several missing teeth. H'
	db	'e nonchalantly scratches his behind.'
L0112:	db	00
L0113:	db	'name'
L0117:	db	00
L0118:	db	'Where are thy clothes?'
L012E:	db	00
L012F:	db	'job'
L0132:	db	00
L0133:	db	'"Hey, what job? I am having a great time here. Leave me alon'
	db	'e!"'
L0172:	db	00
L0173:	db	'The man looks confused. "Job? Me no job. Me live. Me live he'
	db	're with Mama. No need job. Cave provides all."'
L01DD:	db	00
L01DE:	db	'cave'
L01E2:	db	00
L01E3:	db	'Mama'
L01E7:	db	00
L01E8:	db	'Where are thy clothes?'
L01FE:	db	00
L01FF:	db	'"They make me itch so I do not wear any."'
L0228:	db	00
L0229:	db	'"Clothes?!" The man laughs heartily and slaps his belly. "No'
	db	' clothes, no clothes," he assures you, still chuckling.'
L029C:	db	00
L029D:	db	'Where are thy clothes?'
L02B3:	db	00
L02B4:	db	'Mama'
L02B8:	db	00
L02B9:	db	'"Quite a lady, is she not?" He nudges you and winks.'
L02ED:	db	00
L02EE:	db	'"Mmm. Mama! Me Papa. She Mama. We make zug-zug. Maybe someda'
	db	'y make Boy or Girl!"'
L033E:	db	00
L033F:	db	'Mama'
L0343:	db	00
L0344:	db	'cave'
L0348:	db	00
L0349:	db	'"We love the cave. The bees do not bother us. When they slee'
	db	'p we get our honey. We cook mice on the campfire. They are r'
	db	'eally not bad. Thou shouldst try them!"'
L03E8:	db	00
L03E9:	db	'"Cave good to us. We stay away from bees. They no hurt us. W'
	db	'e no hurt them. We take honey when they sleep. We eat the mi'
	db	'ce in cave. Cook them up on campfire. Very good!"*'
L0493:	db	00
L0494:	db	'"I may puke."*'
L04A2:	db	00
L04A3:	db	'cave'
L04A7:	db	00
L04A8:	db	'mice'
L04AC:	db	00
L04AD:	db	'honey'
L04B2:	db	00
L04B3:	db	'bees'
L04B7:	db	00
L04B8:	db	'bees'
L04BC:	db	00
L04BD:	db	'"They won't bother thee if thou dost not bother them."'
L04F3:	db	00
L04F4:	db	'"They friendly if we no hurt them."'
L0517:	db	00
L0518:	db	'The man sees Tseramed and frowns. He points at you accusingl'
	db	'y. "Hunt bees?"'
L0563:	db	00
L0564:	db	'"Go away!" The man spits at you and turns away.*'
L0594:	db	00
L0595:	db	'He points at Tseramed. "Him bee hunter! Go away!" The man sp'
	db	'its at you and turns away.*'
L05EC:	db	00
L05ED:	db	'"This is an act, I tell thee! These people are not savages! '
	db	'They are Britannians!"*'
L0640:	db	00
L0641:	db	'"He seems quite savage to me!"*'
L0660:	db	00
L0661:	db	'bees'
L0665:	db	00
L0666:	db	'friendly'
