		.data
L0000:	db	'bye'
L0003:	db	00
L0004:	db	'job'
L0007:	db	00
L0008:	db	'name'
L000C:	db	00
L000D:	db	'You see an attractive, studious-looking man.'
L0039:	db	00
L003A:	db	'"Yes, '
L0040:	db	00
L0041:	db	'," Taylor asks. "May I assist thee?"'
L0065:	db	00
L0066:	db	'Emps'
L006A:	db	00
L006B:	db	'wisps'
L0070:	db	00
L0071:	db	'name'
L0075:	db	00
L0076:	db	'"My name is Taylor, '
L008A:	db	00
L008B:	db	'."'
L008D:	db	00
L008E:	db	'name'
L0092:	db	00
L0093:	db	'Julius'
L0099:	db	00
L009A:	db	'job'
L009D:	db	00
L009E:	db	'"I study the local flora, fauna, and geography here at the m'
	db	'onastery."'
L00E4:	db	00
L00E5:	db	'monastery'
L00EE:	db	00
L00EF:	db	'geography'
L00F8:	db	00
L00F9:	db	'fauna'
L00FE:	db	00
L00FF:	db	'flora'
L0104:	db	00
L0105:	db	'flora'
L010A:	db	00
L010B:	db	'"There are many beautiful plants in this area. I am working '
	db	'on learning about all of them."'
L0166:	db	00
L0167:	db	'flora'
L016C:	db	00
L016D:	db	'fauna'
L0172:	db	00
L0173:	db	'"Many different species of animals reside in the forest. I h'
	db	'ave encountered some fascinating ones in my studies."'
L01E4:	db	00
L01E5:	db	'wisps'
L01EA:	db	00
L01EB:	db	'fauna'
L01F0:	db	00
L01F1:	db	'monastery'
L01FA:	db	00
L01FB:	db	'"Our order is called the Brotherhood of the Rose."'
L022D:	db	00
L022E:	db	'order'
L0233:	db	00
L0234:	db	'monastery'
L023D:	db	00
L023E:	db	'order'
L0243:	db	00
L0244:	db	'"Yes, '
L024A:	db	00
L024B:	db	'. One other monk, Aimi, lives here in the Abbey. She is a pa'
	db	'inter and a gardener."'
L029D:	db	00
L029E:	db	'gardener'
L02A6:	db	00
L02A7:	db	'painter'
L02AE:	db	00
L02AF:	db	'Kreg'
L02B3:	db	00
L02B4:	db	'order'
L02B9:	db	00
L02BA:	db	'painter'
L02C1:	db	00
L02C2:	db	'He smiles. "Between us, she is a far better gardener."'
L02F8:	db	00
L02F9:	db	'painter'
L0300:	db	00
L0301:	db	'gardener'
L0309:	db	00
L030A:	db	'"She raises the most lovely flowers that I have ever seen! T'
	db	'hou must see them to believe of their existence."'
L0377:	db	00
L0378:	db	'gardener'
L0380:	db	00
L0381:	db	'geography'
L038A:	db	00
L038B:	db	'"I use my knowledge of the local landscape to aid in my stud'
	db	'ies. The better I know the locale, the farther away I can tr'
	db	'avel from the Brotherhood Abbey and still be sure I will abl'
	db	'e to return -- unlike a fellow monk of mine."'
L046C:	db	00
L046D:	db	'geography'
L0476:	db	00
L0477:	db	'fellow'
L047D:	db	00
L047E:	db	'fellow'
L0484:	db	00
L0485:	db	'"He became lost some time ago while surveying the area for b'
	db	'irds -- the Golden-Cheeked Warbler, I believe it was. Sadly,'
	db	' he travelled too far, and we have not heard from him since.'
	db	'~~"I do not wish to suffer the same fate."'
L0563:	db	00
L0564:	db	'fellow'
L056A:	db	00
L056B:	db	'Kreg'
L056F:	db	00
L0570:	db	'"That name does not sound familiar, '
L0594:	db	00
L0595:	db	'. Perhaps he is not from this area."'
L05B9:	db	00
L05BA:	db	'Kreg'
L05BE:	db	00
L05BF:	db	'Julius'
L05C5:	db	00
L05C6:	db	'"Julius? I cannot be certain, but 'tis possible he may be so'
	db	'meone who now resides in the... cemetery. I have heard that '
	db	'name mentioned as someone who was brought to the Abbey to be'
	db	' buried, though I know not who brought him	and I do not reme'
	db	'mber from whom I heard it. I do hope he was not a friend of '
	db	'thine," he says, apologetically.'
L0712:	db	00
L0713:	db	'Julius'
L0719:	db	00
L071A:	db	'wisps'
L071F:	db	00
L0720:	db	'"The wisps?" he laughs. "I doubt they exist. I realize many '
	db	'people seem to believe in them, but I have never seen any.~~'
	db	' "If thou must know, popular legend maintains that they inha'
	db	'bit the forest area, near the Emps. Supposedly, the Emps are'
	db	' able to speak with them." He shrugs. "Thou mayest look for '
	db	'them if that is thy wish, but I would not waste precious tim'
	db	'e, myself."'
L0893:	db	00
L0894:	db	'Emps'
L0898:	db	00
L0899:	db	'precious time'
L08A6:	db	00
L08A7:	db	'wisps'
L08AC:	db	00
L08AD:	db	'precious time'
L08BA:	db	00
L08BB:	db	'"There are so many exciting things to investigate... tree fl'
	db	'owers, for example, '
L090B:	db	00
L090C:	db	'."'
L090E:	db	00
L090F:	db	'precious time'
L091C:	db	00
L091D:	db	'Emps'
L0921:	db	00
L0922:	db	'"Ah, the Emps. I have not been able to glean much informatio'
	db	'n about them.~~"They live on the eastern edge of the deep fo'
	db	'rest, not too terribly far from here.~~"They resemble apes, '
	db	'but only slightly. They are exceedingly shy, and will rarely'
	db	' feel comfortable enough to approach a human.~~ "The only wa'
	db	'y I was able to view an Emp closely occurred when I happened'
	db	' to have honey in my pack which I had just picked up from Be'
	db	'e Cave. The creature appeared, stared at me for a few minute'
	db	's, and then asked -- asked, I say -- for mine honey. I belie'
	db	've they are empathic, hence their name.~~ "Quite an interest'
	db	'ing species, dost thou not agree?"'
L0B9C:	db	00
L0B9D:	db	'Bee Cave'
L0BA5:	db	00
L0BA6:	db	'honey'
L0BAB:	db	00
L0BAC:	db	'Emps'
L0BB0:	db	00
L0BB1:	db	'honey'
L0BB6:	db	00
L0BB7:	db	'"The honey from the caves is quite tasty, but rarely can one'
	db	' get it without a fight. The Bee Caves can be a rather dange'
	db	'rous place."'
L0C3B:	db	00
L0C3C:	db	'honey'
L0C41:	db	00
L0C42:	db	'Bee Cave'
L0C4A:	db	00
L0C4B:	db	'"Bee Cave is located to the southwest of the Abbey. But if t'
	db	'hou art planning a trip there, beware the giant bees that li'
	db	've in the caves. Their venom is very poisonous.~~'
L0CF4:	db	00
L0CF5:	db	'"If thou wishest, I can give thee a smoke bomb that will rep'
	db	'el the bees for a short time. Dost thou want it?"'
L0D62:	db	00
L0D63:	db	'"Here it is."'
L0D70:	db	00
L0D71:	db	'"Perhaps thou shouldst lighten thy load before taking the bo'
	db	'mb."'
L0DB1:	db	00
L0DB2:	db	'"Very well. But be careful if thou dost happen by the caves!'
	db	'"'
L0DEF:	db	00
L0DF0:	db	'Bee Cave'
L0DF8:	db	00
L0DF9:	db	'bye'
L0DFC:	db	00
L0DFD:	db	'"May thy knowledge increase with thine encounters with natur'
	db	'e, '
L0E3C:	db	00
L0E3D:	db	'."*'
L0E40:	db	00
