		.funcnumber	04F3H
		.data
L0000:	db	'You see before you a short, roly-poly man with a pompous smi'
	db	'rk on his face. He is holding a lantern in one hand and a di'
	db	'rty spoon in the other.'
L008F:	db	00
L0090:	db	'"Hello, good friend," says Malloy. "A pleasure to see thee a'
	db	'gain."'
L00D2:	db	00
L00D3:	db	'bye'
L00D6:	db	00
L00D7:	db	'job'
L00DA:	db	00
L00DB:	db	'name'
L00DF:	db	00
L00E0:	db	'helmet on foot'
L00EE:	db	00
L00EF:	db	'name'
L00F3:	db	00
L00F4:	db	'"My name is Malloy. Pleased to make thine acquaintance." Mal'
	db	'loy bows politely.'
L0142:	db	00
L0143:	db	'Malloy's face carries an exasperated smirk. "My partner over'
	db	' there is Owings," he says, pointing to Owings, the skinny m'
	db	'an digging away next to him. "Where are thy manners?! Say he'
	db	'llo to our visitor!"'
L020B:	db	00
L020C:	db	'"Thou dost already know my partner over there," he says, poi'
	db	'nting to Owings.'
L0258:	db	00
L0259:	db	'"Hello there!" says Owings, giving you a big smile. The fron'
	db	't of his mining helmet falls down over his eyes. Blinded, he'
	db	' gropes the air around him.*'
L02ED:	db	00
L02EE:	db	'Malloy shakes his head sadly.*'
L030C:	db	00
L030D:	db	'Malloy regains his composure. "Hello there, I am Malloy. I d'
	db	'o apologize for my partner's childish antics."'
L0377:	db	00
L0378:	db	'name'
L037C:	db	00
L037D:	db	'job'
L0380:	db	00
L0381:	db	'"Normally my job is to dig, but as my partner Owings seems t'
	db	'o be missing I suppose my job is to look for him. I hope not'
	db	'hing has happened to the little fellow."'
L0421:	db	00
L0422:	db	'"Owings and myself are working as mining engineers, a positi'
	db	'on we were fortunate enough to have acquired quite recently.'
	db	' We are working on a special project for the Britannian Mini'
	db	'ng Company."*'
L04E3:	db	00
L04E4:	db	'Owings gives a big nod, throwing his head back and snapping '
	db	'it straight down. "That is absolutely right, Malloy."*'
L0556:	db	00
L0557:	db	'"That is absolutely right, Malloy," says Owings. He gives a '
	db	'big nod which causes his helmet to fall down over his eyes.*'
L05CF:	db	00
L05D0:	db	'special project'
L05DF:	db	00
L05E0:	db	'mining engineers'
L05F0:	db	00
L05F1:	db	'mining engineers'
L0601:	db	00
L0602:	db	'"My partner and I are not exactly mining engineers, although'
	db	' we did travel to Minoc to become miners. We came here with '
	db	'a map..."*'
L0684:	db	00
L0685:	db	'"It was the map that the funny man dressed like the Avatar s'
	db	'old us!"*'
L06CA:	db	00
L06CB:	db	'"That is correct. But when we got here we discovered that th'
	db	'e Britannian Mining Company owned the rights to this area of'
	db	' land already!"*'
L0753:	db	00
L0754:	db	'"That funny man dressed like the Avatar lied to us." Owings '
	db	'scratches his head thoughtfully. "The Britannian Mining Comp'
	db	'any wanted to throw us in the prisons of Yew for claim jumpi'
	db	'ng!"*'
L080D:	db	00
L080E:	db	'"I was able to convince them that we would be more valuable '
	db	'to the Britannian Mining Company if we could come to work fo'
	db	'r them." Malloy beams proudly.*'
L08A5:	db	00
L08A6:	db	'mining engineers'
L08B6:	db	00
L08B7:	db	'funny man'
L08C0:	db	00
L08C1:	db	'map'
L08C4:	db	00
L08C5:	db	'map'
L08C8:	db	00
L08C9:	db	'"We paid nearly a hundred gold pieces for that map. It was s'
	db	'upposed to lead to a spot of valuable minerals found over a '
	db	'hundred years ago. It was a terrific investment. The map was'
	db	' an antique, but it looked like it could not have been more '
	db	'than a few years old! Thou dost not see preservation like th'
	db	'at every day!"'
L0A03:	db	00
L0A04:	db	'map'
L0A07:	db	00
L0A08:	db	'funny man'
L0A11:	db	00
L0A12:	db	'"Someone told us his name. Let me see if I can remember it..'
	db	'. Sullivan, I think it was. Funny name for an Avatar, but th'
	db	'ere thou art!"'
L0A98:	db	00
L0A99:	db	'funny man'
L0AA2:	db	00
L0AA3:	db	'special project'
L0AB2:	db	00
L0AB3:	db	'"Owings and myself are now involved in a very important spec'
	db	'ial project, but it is a secret. Can we trust thee?"'
L0B23:	db	00
L0B24:	db	'"In that case I thank thee for thine honesty. I do not reall'
	db	'y mind if a person is untrustworthy. But someone who is untr'
	db	'ustworthy and dishonest about it, that is something that I c'
	db	'annot abide."*'
L0BE6:	db	00
L0BE7:	db	'You see Owings nod his head most enthusiastically. A second '
	db	'later he has a very confused expression on his face.*'
L0C58:	db	00
L0C59:	db	'"The Britannian Mining Company has asked us to dig a tunnel '
	db	'to New Magincia! It will revolutionize the mining industry."'
L0CD1:	db	00
L0CD2:	db	'"They do not want anybody to find out about it. They said th'
	db	'at bringing more mining equipment over here would just make '
	db	'people suspicious, so they told us to start by using these s'
	db	'poons!" Owings proudly holds up his spoon to show it to you.'
	db	' He smiles.'
L0DCD:	db	00
L0DCE:	db	'"Yes, it was such a special project they told us we were the'
	db	' only ones they could think of who would even attempt to do '
	db	'such a thing!" Malloy beams proudly. "Well come on, Owings, '
	db	'we had best get back to work. We have a schedule to meet."'
L0EBC:	db	00
L0EBD:	db	'special project'
L0ECC:	db	00
L0ECD:	db	'schedule'
L0ED5:	db	00
L0ED6:	db	'tunnel'
L0EDC:	db	00
L0EDD:	db	'tunnel'
L0EE3:	db	00
L0EE4:	db	'Malloy looks at you and puts a finger to his lips. "Shhhhhhh'
	db	'h!!! I asked thee not to speak of this to anyone!"'
L0F52:	db	00
L0F53:	db	'tunnel'
L0F59:	db	00
L0F5A:	db	'schedule'
L0F62:	db	00
L0F63:	db	'"Owings, have a look at that schedule and find out how we ar'
	db	'e doing."'
L0FA8:	db	00
L0FA9:	db	'Owings bends over and goes to pick up a very large scroll. A'
	db	's he touches the tip of it he sends it rolling away down the'
	db	' mineshaft. As it rolls away it is unravelling leaving a len'
	db	'gthy trail of paper behind it. Owings chases after it but su'
	db	'cceeds in doing little else but tangling up his legs in the '
	db	'long roll of the paper. When at last he has the other end, i'
	db	't is an unreadable mess.'
L1129:	db	00
L112A:	db	'"Give me that!" says Malloy as he snatches a piece of the sc'
	db	'roll away. He examines it for a moment. "According to this w'
	db	'e shall be finished in... one hundred and seventy three year'
	db	's! Owings, we have got to start working faster!" The two of '
	db	'them go back to digging with their spoons. As they dig Mallo'
	db	'y turns to Owings and says, "This is another fine mess thou '
	db	'hast gotten me into!"'
L12A7:	db	00
L12A8:	db	'schedule'
L12B0:	db	00
L12B1:	db	'helmet on foot'
L12BF:	db	00
L12C0:	db	'Malloy kicks out with his foot, trying to dislodge the helme'
	db	't which is stuck there. He looks at Owings and pouts, "Why d'
	db	'ost thou not do something to help me?!"'
L135F:	db	00
L1360:	db	'Owings grabs the helmet on Malloy's foot and attempts to dis'
	db	'lodge it. After several fierce tugs it comes off with a loud'
	db	' popping noise. Owings pulls the helmet right into his own f'
	db	'ace and this makes a loud knocking noise.'
L143D:	db	00
L143E:	db	'Malloy goes hurling backwards, crying out in panic. He smack'
	db	's the back of his head on the rock wall behind him. He takes'
	db	' off his crumpled helmet and points to it. "A good thing I w'
	db	'as wearing this or I might have been hurt!" With that a loos'
	db	'e rock tumbles down from the ceiling landing squarely on his'
	db	' head. Malloy says "Ooooooh!" Owings breaks into a giggling '
	db	'fit. Malloy flashes you an incredulous pouting grimace.'
L15DD:	db	00
L15DE:	db	'helmet on foot'
L15EC:	db	00
L15ED:	db	'bye'
L15F0:	db	00
L15F1:	db	'Both Malloy and Owings stop what they are doing and give you'
	db	' a friendly goodbye wave.*'
L1647:	db	00
L1648:	db	'"Good day to thee, '
L165B:	db	00
L165C:	db	'."*'
L165F:	db	00
