L001C:	db	'answers'
L0023:	db	00
L0024:	db	'You see a large man with an almost cunning, erudite aura abo'
	db	'ut him.'
L0067:	db	00
L0068:	db	'"Hello, again," Alagner says.'
L0085:	db	00
L0086:	db	'name'
L008A:	db	00
L008B:	db	'The sage smiles and nods his head. "My name is Alagner. And '
	db	'who art thou?"'
L00D5:	db	00
L00D6:	db	'Avatar'
L00DC:	db	00
L00DD:	db	'"I see. Nice to meet thee. Go away. I am busy."*'
L010D:	db	00
L010E:	db	'Avatar'
L0114:	db	00
L0115:	db	'Alagner's eyes widen.~~"By the skies above! I do recognize t'
	db	'hee! This is quite an honor! What may I do for thee?"'
L0186:	db	00
L0187:	db	'name'
L018B:	db	00
L018C:	db	'job'
L018F:	db	00
L0190:	db	'"My profession -- rather, my destiny -- is to learn and know'
	db	' all things. I came to New Magincia to build my workshop and'
	db	' do so."'
L0210:	db	00
L0211:	db	'workshop'
L0219:	db	00
L021A:	db	'New Magincia'
L0226:	db	00
L0227:	db	'New Magincia'
L0233:	db	00
L0234:	db	'The sage sighs. "I left the Britannian mainland to come to t'
	db	'he relative peace and quiet of New Magincia. I am content he'
	db	're because it is isolated and free from... the filth and cor'
	db	'ruption going on in Britannia. Not many see it."'
L0318:	db	00
L0319:	db	'New Magincia'
L0325:	db	00
L0326:	db	'corruption'
L0330:	db	00
L0331:	db	'workshop'
L0339:	db	00
L033A:	db	'"This is my workshop. I peruse my books and papers here. Occ'
	db	'asionally, I invent things, such as this crystal ball."'
L03AD:	db	00
L03AE:	db	'workshop'
L03B6:	db	00
L03B7:	db	'crystal ball'
L03C3:	db	00
L03C4:	db	'crystal ball'
L03D0:	db	00
L03D1:	db	'"It is a device for recording. If I forget a procedure or a '
	db	'step in an experiment, I may look into the crystal ball and '
	db	'see yesterday's events. Please, feel free to use it. Thou wi'
	db	'lt see what I was doing yesterday."'
L04A8:	db	00
L04A9:	db	'crystal ball'
L04B5:	db	00
L04B6:	db	'Wisps'
L04BB:	db	00
L04BC:	db	'"They are unusually aloof creatures of another dimension. Th'
	db	'ou wilt think they are thy friends, but they could very well'
	db	' be spying on -thee- for someone else! They have no loyaltie'
	db	's to good or evil -- all they care about is the acquisition '
	db	'of information -- how they acquire it is sometimes honorable'
	db	', sometimes not."'
L05F9:	db	00
L05FA:	db	'Wisps'
L05FF:	db	00
L0600:	db	'corruption'
L060A:	db	00
L060B:	db	'"The Britannian people are becoming careless and lazy. They '
	db	'do not seek true knowledge. They do not respect their land. '
	db	'They do not respect each other. The resources of our land ar'
	db	'e being wasted. Miners are experimenting with dangerous reag'
	db	'ents. There is an evil in the land, and I am not so sure tha'
	db	't it is in the people themselves."'
L0759:	db	00
L075A:	db	'corruption'
L0764:	db	00
L0765:	db	'evil'
L0769:	db	00
L076A:	db	'true knowledge'
L0778:	db	00
L0779:	db	'true knowledge'
L0787:	db	00
L0788:	db	'"True knowledge is the only way to complete fulfillment."'
L07C1:	db	00
L07C2:	db	'true knowledge'
L07D0:	db	00
L07D1:	db	'evil'
L07D5:	db	00
L07D6:	db	'"Thou art a member of The Fellowship, I see. Thou must not k'
	db	'now everything about them. If thou didst, thou wouldst not b'
	db	'e a member!'
L0859:	db	00
L085A:	db	'under cover'
L0865:	db	00
L0866:	db	'"Thou hast heard of The Fellowship by now, I am sure.'
L089B:	db	00
L089C:	db	'suspect'
L08A3:	db	00
L08A4:	db	'"They are cunning and two-faced. I am working on obtaining p'
	db	'roof of this."'
L08EE:	db	00
L08EF:	db	'evil'
L08F3:	db	00
L08F4:	db	'proof'
L08F9:	db	00
L08FA:	db	'proof'
L08FF:	db	00
L0900:	db	'"I am documenting this information in my notebook."'
L0933:	db	00
L0934:	db	'proof'
L0939:	db	00
L093A:	db	'notebook'
L0942:	db	00
L0943:	db	'information'
L094E:	db	00
L094F:	db	'information'
L095A:	db	00
L095B:	db	'"It is all contained within the notebook."'
L0985:	db	00
L0986:	db	'information'
L0991:	db	00
L0992:	db	'under cover'
L099D:	db	00
L099E:	db	'"Thou didst join The Fellowship to study their ways? Thou do'
	db	'st suspect them as well? Perhaps thou hast more substance to'
	db	' thee than I thought. We are working towards the same goal."'
L0A52:	db	00
L0A53:	db	'under cover'
L0A5E:	db	00
L0A5F:	db	'suspect'
L0A66:	db	00
L0A67:	db	'"Thou dost suspect The Fellowship of foul deeds? Well then! '
	db	'Thou art perceptive indeed! Perhaps we are working toward th'
	db	'e same goal!"'
L0AEC:	db	00
L0AED:	db	'suspect'
L0AF4:	db	00
L0AF5:	db	'notebook'
L0AFD:	db	00
L0AFE:	db	'"It is hidden in a safe place, along with mine other treasur'
	db	'ed sources of knowledge."'
L0B53:	db	00
L0B54:	db	'Alagner listens as you tell him you would like to borrow the'
	db	' notebook.'
L0B9A:	db	00
L0B9B:	db	'"Since thou art on an honorable quest, I suppose I might all'
	db	'ow thee to borrow it if thou dost give me thy word that thou'
	db	' wilt return it, and if thou dost offer proof of thine eager'
	db	'ness to learn the true knowledge of the world."'
L0C7E:	db	00
L0C7F:	db	'learn'
L0C84:	db	00
L0C85:	db	'notebook'
L0C8D:	db	00
L0C8E:	db	'learn'
L0C93:	db	00
L0C94:	db	'"Very well. Dost thou know the answers to the questions of L'
	db	'ife and Death?"'
L0CDF:	db	00
L0CE0:	db	'"I do not believe thou dost.'
L0CFC:	db	00
L0CFD:	db	'"No, of course thou dost not.'
L0D1A:	db	00
L0D1B:	db	'"Only those souls who have passed on from this life know the'
	db	'se things. Seek out the spirit of The Tortured One. Ask him '
	db	'what the answers are to the questions of life and death. Whe'
	db	'n thou dost return with the correct answer, I will believe t'
	db	'hat thou art sincere in thy quest for knowledge. Only then w'
	db	'ill I allow thee to borrow the notebook."'
L0E70:	db	00
L0E71:	db	'Tortured One'
L0E7D:	db	00
L0E7E:	db	'learn'
L0E83:	db	00
L0E84:	db	'Tortured One'
L0E90:	db	00
L0E91:	db	'"Alas, he is a poor soul who is doomed to haunt his abode th'
	db	'roughout eternity."'
L0EE0:	db	00
L0EE1:	db	'Tortured One'
L0EED:	db	00
L0EEE:	db	'abode'
L0EF3:	db	00
L0EF4:	db	'abode'
L0EF9:	db	00
L0EFA:	db	'"Seek him out in Skara Brae. But be careful. It is a dangero'
	db	'us place. I should also advise thee that thou must use Seanc'
	db	'e Spells to speak with anyone on that island. They are all u'
	db	'ndead."'
L0FB5:	db	00
L0FB6:	db	'abode'
L0FBB:	db	00
L0FBC:	db	'answers'
L0FC3:	db	00
L0FC4:	db	'"Thou hast spoken to the Tortured One and learned the answer'
	db	's to the questions of Life and Death?"'
L1026:	db	00
L1027:	db	'"Then what are the answers?"'
L1043:	db	00
L1044:	db	'"Do not return until thou hast done so."'
L106C:	db	00
L106D:	db	'answers'
L1074:	db	00
L1075:	db	'bye'
L1078:	db	00
L1079:	db	'"Farewell. May thy journeys be profitable."*'
L10A5:	db	00
