L0000:	db	'Erethian looks irritated by your question, "'Tis not a hindr'
	db	'ance for one sensitive enough to feel the ridges the ink	mak'
	db	'es on the page.'
L0087:	db	00
L0088:	db	'Dost thou think me an invalid? Know that in my searches, I	h'
	db	'ave faced dangers that would turn even one such as thee to q'
	db	'uivering flesh."'
L0110:	db	00
L0111:	db	'The mage's eyes begin to glow softly. "My magic is strong en'
	db	'ough to tear down the fabric of reality and reconstruct it a'
	db	's I see fit.'
L0195:	db	00
L0196:	db	'To prove this, I'll take on the form of a winged gargoyle no'
	db	'ble..."'
L01D9:	db	00
L01DA:	db	'His hands move in passes you recognize as being magical, the'
	db	'n he speaks softly the magic words,'
L0239:	db	00
L023A:	db	'"Rel An-Quas Ailem In Garge".*'
L0258:	db	00
L0259:	db	'"Even the great dragon's form is not beyond my power." Ereth'
	db	'ian begins speaking softly, then rises to a crescendo with t'
	db	'he words,'
L02DA:	db	00
L02DB:	db	'"Rel An-Quas Ailem In BAL-ZEN"!*'
L02FB:	db	00
L02FC:	db	'The dragon looks down its snout menacingly at what you guess'
	db	' is meant to be you. Even in this powerful form, it would se'
	db	'em that Erethian is still blind, however, you get the impres'
	db	'sion that he is quite capable of taking care of himself.'
L03E8:	db	00
L03E9:	db	'"Enough of these silly charades, I really am quite busy with'
	db	' my studies." He intones the words,'
L0448:	db	00
L0449:	db	'"An Ort Rel"!*'
L0457:	db	00
L0458:	db	'Erethian looks irritated by your question, "'Tis not a hindr'
	db	'ance for one	sensitive enough to feel the ridges the ink mak'
	db	'es on the page.'
L04DF:	db	00
L04E0:	db	'Dost thou think me an invalid? Know that in my searches, I h'
	db	'ave faced dangers that would turn even one such as thee to q'
	db	'uivering flesh."'
L0568:	db	00
L0569:	db	'The mage's eyes begin to glow softly. "My magic is strong en'
	db	'ough to tear down the fabric of reality and reconstruct it a'
	db	's I see fit."'
L05EE:	db	00
L05EF:	db	'To prove this, I'll take on the form of a winged gargoyle no'
	db	'ble..."'
L0632:	db	00
L0633:	db	'His hands move in passes you recognize as being magical, the'
	db	'n he speaks softly the magic words,'
L0692:	db	00
L0693:	db	'"Rel An-Quas Ailem In Bet-Zen".*'
L06B3:	db	00
L06B4:	db	'The elderly mage looks a bit perplexed after his experience '
	db	'as a rodent. "That spell always used to work, but with all o'
	db	'f these damnable ether waves, I can't remember the proper wo'
	db	'rds?'
L076C:	db	00
L076D:	db	''Tis of no consequence, I'll take the form of a great dragon'
	db	' to prove my powers..." he begins speaking softly, then rise'
	db	's to a crescendo with the words,'
L0805:	db	00
L0806:	db	'"Rel An-Quas Ailem In MOO"!*'
L0822:	db	00
L0823:	db	'The elderly mage looks quite embarrassed, "Enough of these s'
	db	'illy charades, I really am quite busy with my studies." He t'
	db	'urns away, his face blushing furiously.*'
L08C3:	db	00
L08C4:	db	'The old mage seems on the verge of saying something, stops t'
	db	'hen says, "Were quarter's not so confined here, I'd show the'
	db	'e that my blindness in no way hampers my abilities." His aff'
	db	'liction seems to be a touchy subject with the mage.*'
L09AC:	db	00
L09AD:	db	'"Have you nothing better to do than bother an old man?!" He '
	db	'seems quite put out with this line of conversation.*'
L0A1D:	db	00
