L0000:	db	'After learning that none of the townsfolk are willing to sac'
	db	'rifice themselves for a greater good, an odd light comes int'
	db	'o Forsythe's eyes. His chin firms and his shoulders square.~'
	db	'~"Well, then. It has got to be done! And since no other brav'
	db	'e soul will do it, perhaps I shall have to show them all wha'
	db	't real courage is." He strides forward like a lord and plant'
	db	's his feet. "Please be kind enough to lead me to the well, '
L01A3:	db	00
L01A4:	db	'."*'
L01A7:	db	00
L01A8:	db	'sacrifice'
L01B1:	db	00
L01B2:	db	'He steps in line and motions for you to lead on.*'
L01E3:	db	00
L01E4:	db	'"Thou hast so many companions that I may not follow thee at '
	db	'this time."'
L022B:	db	00
