L0000:	db	'"I thank thee, '
L000F:	db	00
L0010:	db	'. That dark spirit had suppressed my will for so long that I'
	db	' was not sure I had one left. Thou hast done a great deed fo'
	db	'r Skara Brae, for myself and, indeed, all of Britannia, but '
	db	'then I suppose this is merely a matter of course for one suc'
	db	'h as thee. My gratitude is thine." He bows deeply to you.'
L0139:	db	00
L013A:	db	'"But now, I fear that all is still not right with the world.'
	db	' The ether stirs chaotically outside of this Dark Tower. Wer'
	db	'e it not for some property within the walls, I fear my mind '
	db	'would suffer the ravages of its force."'
L0215:	db	00
L0216:	db	'Hast thou reconsidered my request?'
L0238:	db	00
L0239:	db	00
L023A:	db	'"It is good to see thee again, '
L0259:	db	00
L025A:	db	'.'
L025B:	db	00
L025C:	db	'"'
L025D:	db	00
L025E:	db	'Ah, I see. No matter'
L0272:	db	00
L0273:	db	'"Now, '
L0279:	db	00
L027A:	db	'. I must ask this favor of thee. The Well of Souls, at the b'
	db	'ottom of this tower, holds many tormented souls within it an'
	db	'd binds the spirits of Skara Brae to this island. It must be'
	db	' destroyed." Horance looks at you intently.~ "I can only hop'
	db	'e that thou wilt try to free them."'
L038D:	db	00
L038E:	db	'"Well, wilt thou?" He looks at you expectantly.'
L03BD:	db	00
L03BE:	db	'I understand. Fear not'
L03D4:	db	00
L03D5:	db	'Horance thinks for a moment then, "When the well is destroye'
	db	'd, the souls within will be released to float aimlessly upon'
	db	' the ether for a time. I have badly wronged the Lady Rowena '
	db	'and her husband, I would see this wrong mended. Please, lead'
	db	' her out of this dark place and see that she is reunited wit'
	db	'h Trent. That way they will remain together when they are re'
	db	'leased. I will know when you've accomplished this task, and '
	db	'then we can continue with the destruction of the well."'
L05B0:	db	00
L05B1:	db	'"But please, '
L05BE:	db	00
L05BF:	db	', I beg thee make haste. Take Rowena to Trent! Time is short'
	db	'! Talk to her and take her to her husband! The souls in the '
	db	'well are constantly in pain, and some become so drained that'
	db	' they are snuffed out of existence like the flame of a candl'
	db	'e." He looks as if he feels the pain himself.'
L06DC:	db	00
L06DD:	db	'"Good, now we can get on with freeing the rest of Skara Brae'
	db	'. The destruction of the Well of Souls can only be brought a'
	db	'bout by the selfless sacrifice of a spirit. A living being w'
	db	'ill not do, because the soul is tied to the body.~~"Go out i'
	db	'nto the town and find a spirit willing to make the sacrifice'
	db	' for the sake of all Skara Brae. I suggest that thou shoulds'
	db	't ask Mayor Forsythe first, as it is his right to be conside'
	db	'red before the others." He strokes his chin thoughtfully as '
	db	'you leave.'
L08C7:	db	00
