L0000:	db	'"Fellow members, each of thee has faced -- and doubtless sha'
	db	'll face again -- a moment in which thou dost feel the heat o'
	db	'f the fever. A moment when thy mind has been clouded with il'
	db	'lusory thoughts and visions. A moment when thy recognition h'
	db	'as simply vanished, without rhyme or reason. A moment when, '
	db	'perhaps, thou hast even doubted the very words of The Fellow'
	db	'ship itself!"*'
L0176:	db	00
L0177:	db	'You see the clerk gasp, her eyes widening in disbelief.*'
L01AF:	db	00
L01B0:	db	'"The second principle of the Triad is `trust thy brother.' ''
	db	'Tis a simple practice when thou dost know thy brother. But T'
	db	'he Fellowship was not always known to thee. It may, at one t'
	db	'ime, have been difficult to put thy trust in something as la'
	db	'rge as The Fellowship.~~ "However, to gain full knowledge of'
	db	' thine inner strength, one must have the courage to walk on '
	db	'the fire of trust!"*'
L032C:	db	00
L032D:	db	'"'Tis true! Trust was the key to my freedom!"*'
L035B:	db	00
L035C:	db	'"Trust requires great courage, and that courage exists withi'
	db	'n thyself."*'
L03A4:	db	00
L03A5:	db	'Iolo leans toward you.~~ "I believe we have heard enough of '
	db	'this, no?"*'
L03EC:	db	00
L03ED:	db	'"Good. Let us leave."*'
L0403:	db	00
L0404:	db	'Iolo sighs deeply.*'
L0417:	db	00
L0418:	db	'"But as long as one remains aware, this problem will not pla'
	db	'gue thee."*'
L045F:	db	00
L0460:	db	'"Come, friend. That is enough of this. Drinks are on me."~~ '
	db	'As you make your way out of the Hall, the leader's voice con'
	db	'tinues to drone on and on.*'
L04F3:	db	00
