L0000:	db	'Trent paces around the burned-out remains of his shop. When '
	db	'he sees you return, he rushes forward, looking for his love,'
	db	' Rowena.'
L0080:	db	00
L0081:	db	'The starcrossed lovers rush into each other's ghostly embrac'
	db	'e. For a time it's hard to see where one spirit begins and t'
	db	'he other ends. You barely make out the image of Trent replac'
	db	'ing Rowena's ring on her finger.~~Then the two slowly turn t'
	db	'o face you. "Thou hast done so much for us, I hope that in h'
	db	'elping us, thou hast been assisted in thine own quest." Tren'
	db	't bows to you then turns to regard his lovely wife.*'
L021D:	db	00
L021E:	db	'"How can I help thee, '
L0234:	db	00
L0235:	db	'? Is there something I have forgotten?" He looks at you, per'
	db	'plexed.'
L0278:	db	00
L0279:	db	'The large ghost continues to work, but now he whistles a swe'
	db	'et, sad tune as he hammers on the iron bars of the cage.'
L02ED:	db	00
L02EE:	db	'"Why, where has the cage gone to? 'Twas here just a moment a'
	db	'go, I am certain. I cannot progress until I can find the cag'
	db	'e!"*'
L036A:	db	00
L036B:	db	'bye'
L036E:	db	00
L036F:	db	'What next?'
L0379:	db	00
L037A:	db	'free'
L037E:	db	00
L037F:	db	'Soul Cage'
L0388:	db	00
L0389:	db	'Soul Cage'
L0392:	db	00
L0393:	db	'"This is a special cage, made to fit the shape of a man. Mis'
	db	'tress Mordra says that it will contain the Liche, Horance, o'
	db	'nce it has been lowered into his Well of Souls." His voice s'
	db	'eems much softer than before.'
L0464:	db	00
L0465:	db	'Soul Cage'
L046E:	db	00
L046F:	db	'free'
L0473:	db	00
L0474:	db	'"Yes, thou wilt help me free her, wilt thou not?" A tinge of'
	db	' the edge comes back to his voice.'
L04D2:	db	00
L04D3:	db	'His grip on the haft of his hammer relaxes and he smiles wit'
	db	'h gratitude.~~"Thou cannot know how much this means to me. I'
	db	' thank thee."'
L0558:	db	00
L0559:	db	'His grip on the haft of his hammer tightens. "See to it thou'
	db	'	art quick about thy departure! If thou dost, I will assume '
	db	'thou hast changed thy mind!"*'
L05EE:	db	00
L05EF:	db	'free'
L05F3:	db	00
L05F4:	db	'What next?'
L05FE:	db	00
L05FF:	db	'"Why, I beg thee to please help in the return my lovely Rowe'
	db	'na to me," he pleads.'
L0650:	db	00
L0651:	db	'"I will need a bar of iron to complete the cage. Several can'
	db	' be found in the town cemetery."'
L06AD:	db	00
L06AE:	db	'What next?'
L06B8:	db	00
L06B9:	db	'"Ah, I'll need the iron bar that thou dost carry." He holds '
	db	'out his hand and takes the iron bar from you.'
L0722:	db	00
L0723:	db	'"With this, I will finish it shortly. Wait here whilst I ten'
	db	'd to the cage."'
L076E:	db	00
L076F:	db	'"Take the cage to Mistress Mordra and she will tell thee mor'
	db	'e about it and its use."'
L07C3:	db	00
L07C4:	db	'sacrifice'
L07CD:	db	00
L07CE:	db	'"I cannot even consider that until I am reunited with my lov'
	db	'e." He seems very adamant about this.'
L082F:	db	00
L0830:	db	'sacrifice'
L0839:	db	00
L083A:	db	'bye'
L083D:	db	00
L083E:	db	'"Please, hurry. Every second my love must endure Horance's f'
	db	'oul presence is like a knife in my side." He begins to pace '
	db	'about his shop.*'
